{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-NR-AnchorCarrierFreqList-r16 ::=  SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxFreqSL-NR-r16)) OF ARFCN-ValueNR","paragraph_zero_based":13608},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13609},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-EUTRA-AnchorCarrierFreqList-r16 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxFreqSL-EUTRA-r16)) OF ARFCN-ValueEUTRA","paragraph_zero_based":13610},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13611},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DiscConfigCommon-r17 ::=   SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":13612},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-RelayUE-ConfigCommon-r17   SL-RelayUE-Config-r17,","paragraph_zero_based":13613},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-RemoteUE-ConfigCommon-r17  SL-RemoteUE-Config-r17","paragraph_zero_based":13614},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":13615},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13616},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SIB12-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":13617},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":13618},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13619},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SIB12 field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13620},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"segmentContainer","paragraph_zero_based":13621},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field includes a segment of the encoded SIB12-IEs. The size of the included segment in this container should be small enough that the SIB message size is less than or equal to the maximum size of a NR SI, i.e. 2976 bits when SIB12 is broadcast.","paragraph_zero_based":13622},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"segmentNumber","paragraph_zero_based":13623},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field identifies the sequence number of a segment of SIB12-IEs. A segment number of zero corresponds to the first segment, A segment number of one corresponds to the second segment, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":13624},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"segmentType","paragraph_zero_based":13625},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates whether the included segment is the last segment or not.","paragraph_zero_based":13626},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CSI-Acquisition","paragraph_zero_based":13627},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates whether CSI reporting is enabled in sidelink unicast. If not set, SL CSI reporting is disabled.","paragraph_zero_based":13628},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-DRX-ConfigCommonGC-BC","paragraph_zero_based":13629},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the sidelink DRX configuration for groupcast and broadcast communication, as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. This field, if present, also indicates the gNB is capable of sidelink DRX.","paragraph_zero_based":13630},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-EUTRA-AnchorCarrierFreqList","paragraph_zero_based":13631}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["878659b57dec5e87c9da62db60b3606d0188f3ae626da839f278ac4d0bb96e4f","5c1dbdeb6cf98ec8e2f7fdc7737cadfe0fc907b6be71836e17b393ad32ef0461","10f7495a619b5a06a5c5975bc3ab8453fa995ce71a2b7df241e7d164fc3db8b2","28194ea8d2427a0f2e5796a385f06345dcf8a17afd8227042d8bb5b32e615d03","355f62ebf5305a0ba42759a91bc7cf80d2d22dc3f05cda0f580e9b280c92fb4c","ddaf940243edee23430c81b82f98324adb4a17a5603d53652c539cbc8838df66","a805fe4fa4d738323060c200c65e4befb352239729fd1494303e41ba2ae04cb2","f4f20ac8bebf3a18c70ece035071d15e18fd565607114aa8d7fd4e400a4bbf5f","45929f68a5689bf3d97c4c8138dd28d16