{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14808},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BWP-Uplink field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":14809},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bwp-Id","paragraph_zero_based":14810},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"An identifier for this bandwidth part. Other parts of the RRC configuration use the BWP-Id to associate themselves with a particular bandwidth part.","paragraph_zero_based":14811},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The network configures the BWPs with consecutive IDs from 1. The Network does not include the value 0, since value 0 is reserved for the initial BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":14812},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14813},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":14814},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":14815},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SetupOtherBWP","paragraph_zero_based":14816},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present upon configuration of a new UL BWP. The field is optionally present, Need M, otherwise. ","paragraph_zero_based":14817},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14818},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–BWP-UplinkCommon","paragraph_zero_based":14819},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE BWP-UplinkCommon is used to configure the common parameters of an uplink BWP. They are \"cell specific\" and the network ensures the necessary alignment with corresponding parameters of other UEs. The common parameters of the initial bandwidth part of the PCell are also provided via system information. For all other serving cells, the network provides the common parameters via dedicated signalling.","paragraph_zero_based":14820},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BWP-UplinkCommon information element","paragraph_zero_based":14821},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":14822},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-BWP-UPLINKCOMMON-START","paragraph_zero_based":14823},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14824},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BWP-UplinkCommon ::=                SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":14825},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    genericParameters                   BWP,","paragraph_zero_based":14826},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    rach-ConfigCommon                   SetupRelease { RACH-ConfigCommon }                                      OPTIONAL,   -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":14827},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    pusch-ConfigCommon                  SetupRelease { PUSCH-ConfigCommon }                                     OPTIONAL,   -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":14828},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    pucch-ConfigCommon                  SetupRelease { PUCCH-ConfigCommon }                                     OPTIONAL,   -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":14829},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...,","paragraph_zero_based":14830},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":14831}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["1bcf01c037441544a3840dadc0e51f6f742bd72060569d826ca59caecba6dbf5","2401e8e5483e561668995b19023571c136b0c3c30232ad3e14eb5679490b8efc","aaf0a2dc83efa69d6f69273144dadf1a19126de1a68d7a8255045af1fb278496","a0aa6e988b3a7f4d7f8ab7f22fd05c74cc667c6fb19102564e0b663d2557d984","b7a03bf9df3458cb1d550959732a8b04c48eeedab98467bb1cb1b47cd0457e6d","0d1fc330515ef081ea8b0281d9e65dff1c43eae85366ff8a941fc1cce320618c","c7609b88cfa4e