t-r16   ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofConfiguredGrantConfig-r16)) OF ConfiguredGrantConfigIndex-r16","paragraph_zero_based":14941},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14942},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ConfiguredGrantConfigType2DeactivationState-r16 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofConfiguredGrantConfig-r16)) OF ConfiguredGrantConfigIndex-r16","paragraph_zero_based":14943},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14944},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ConfiguredGrantConfigType2DeactivationStateList-r16  ::=","paragraph_zero_based":14945},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                             SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofCG-Type2DeactivationState)) OF ConfiguredGrantConfigType2DeactivationState-r16","paragraph_zero_based":14946},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14947},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-BWP-UPLINKDEDICATED-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":14948},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":14949},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14950},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BWP-UplinkDedicated field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":14951}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e591531ddc17a1af5d9739bd138205a06a1f22d43bdc79baf0f3a79ddd0b82c0","5b22f8e4611eb06c58d5a41ef752652c374aa9a29466aa3c5b069f9d00b16ab4","7b661bfd096f4770e98749a75e3dc136d932cc9a90329f04a300d78e429f675c","bd8131d39b63429927d923cc3841afac0186ab693838a3c1b4f7527b89fe318d","6d970d39bf4483e35e4d6b57e609de853b73465b2b1beaee6d63f3d7994a6036","8adbac069b2bc33242ac0712054a964c8e16b5cf6edcb989d27125c099628215","910558b7ae6833a15c63b643e1e20197005f29701b6e6b4027c84dff0ca831a7","772ee6fc574727bdaf200978d8d7668c489a4459dad86fe30c1a57de2faa6f9e","78146e04a487ed5d1884bf4a123814e34498f27396b68a1e4173054ec56da0ac","0605c33a4e5c90a761c3820c8ac5b65a826ce99a2b93ff5e2e3a8b67194a1615","7c45d52f3d86de90b31c0f2f5a8a6b38f2580685c8fe81828dfd03e118f61de6","885fa7da85e8aba657782de213f787b00f4b8085dc703c1531478d81d4d7de30","79b690d07914582bb3f8d35d53bdf472fa820cf5c55ffccdb568fda1ea643b83","fd2167992b6c6bac3a3dadd679137e814e65a8fa5e2ae1cd73332936e9ac17fa","be4d238ce6e9f51c3bd5a98e9f4aebf14d55f4d16800cb3c16ae0825ca325d05","7e982a9db9ad9771fbc42ea53f57128bdf3fc044d3599aeeb084fb2c83340512","392c9e7bcfb555a85bf756fff7da0d4c205db61b2c8c912f876ef57148dd9198","a5e83aa54e40441388f00612ae13d01bbcacae07229822b2e212502b29f68fd5","4bcedd3d41737bc8bc91b1547a7aa32bf1644e251b8cba0497a1a081d1872b0e","8ba0ca3eefea642848aa100bc4abb0cfd7ed0e800d4800c0d3dcc9950d6a4205","dcea4bfe1de2ab02c7b1d0f0357499aa37df8d8596704f7347ab341986555824","e9274a60dda48defa6f1debbae4a4d88da5caa3d08cdfa1bf43b36495d4fc846","a7c423b17b88ea9810141a33376fb5d54a0163960c6a99a094cc492b0c3e0809","6ee776cca88fc74c83f43d1e984c77c8a9661cc98040d9ec7ea6f3f34a4c0274"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[14928,14951],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p14928"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"beamFailureRecoveryConfig","paragraph_zero_based":14952},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration of beam failure recovery. If supplementaryUplink is present, the field is present only in one of the uplink carriers, either UL or SUL.","paragraph_zero_based":14953},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"configuredGrantConfig","paragraph_zero_based":14954},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A Configured-Grant of type1 or type2. It may be configured for UL or SUL but in case of type1 not for both at a time. Except for reconfiguration with sync, the NW does not reconfigure configuredGrantConfig when there is an active configured uplink grant Type 2 (see TS 38.321 [3]). However, the NW may release the configuredGrantConfig at any time. Network can only configure configured grant in one BWP using either this field or configuredGrantConfigToAddModList.","paragraph_zero_based":14955},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"configuredGrantConfigToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":14956},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates a list of one or more configured grant configurations to be added or modified for one BWP. Except for reconfiguration with sync, the NW does not reconfigure a Type 2 configured grant configuration when it is active (see TS 38.321 [3]). The network configures multiple CG configurations for one BWP with either all configurations or no configuration configured with cg-RetransmissionTimer-r16.","paragraph_zero_based":14957},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"configuredGrantConfigToReleaseList","paragraph_zero_based":14958},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates a list of one or more UL Configured Grant configurations to be released. The NW may release a configured grant configuration at any time.","paragraph_zero_based":14959},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"configuredGrantConfigType2DeactivationStateList","paragraph_zero_based":14960},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates a list of the deactivation states in which each state can be mapped to a single or multiple Configured Grant type 2 configurations to be deactivated when the corresponding deactivation DCI is received, see clause 7.3.1 in TS 38.212 [17] and clause 10.2 in TS 38.213 [13].","paragraph_zero_based":14961},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cp-ExtensionC2, cp-ExtensionC3","paragraph_zero_based":14962},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configures the cyclic prefix (CP) extension (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 5.3.1). For 15 kHz SCS, {1..28} are valid for both cp-ExtensionC2 and cp-ExtensionC3. For 30 kHz SCS, {1..28} are valid for cp-ExtensionC2 and {2..28} are valid for cp-ExtensionC3. For 60 kHz SCS, {2..28} are valid for cp-ExtensionC2 and {3..28} are valid for cp-ExtensionC3.","paragraph_zero_based":14963},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"lbt-FailureRecoveryConfig","paragraph_zero_based":14964},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configures parameters used for detection of consistent uplink LBT failures for operation with shared spectrum channel access, as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":14965},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pathlossReferenceRSToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":14966},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of Reference Signals (e.g. a CSI-RS config or a SS block) to be used for path loss estimation for PUSCH, PUCCH and SRS for unified TCI state operation. If unifiedTCI-StateType is not configured for the serving cell, no element in this list is configured.","paragraph_zero_based":14967},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pucch-Config","paragraph_zero_based":14968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH configuration for one BWP of the normal UL or SUL of a serving cell. If the UE is configured with SUL, the network configures PUCCH only on the BWPs of one of the uplinks (normal UL or SUL). The network configures PUCCH-Config at least on non-initial BWP(s) for SpCell and on all BWP(s) for PUCCH SCell. If supported by the UE, the network may configure at most one additional SCell of a cell group with PUCCH-Config (i.e. PUCCH SCell). If PUCCH cell switching is supported by the UE, the network may configure two TDD serving cells with PUCCH-Config within each PUCCH group. For supporting PUCCH cell switching in the PUCCH group with the SpCell, the TDD SpCell and one TDD SCell shall have PUCCH-Config on their normal UL. For supporting PUCCH cell switching in the PUCCH group with only SCells, two TDD SCells shall have PUCCH-Config on their normal UL.","paragraph_zero_based":14969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In (NG)EN-DC and NE-DC, the NW configures at most one serving cell per frequency range with PUCCH. In (NG)EN-DC and NE-DC, if two PUCCH groups are configured, the serving cells of the NR PUCCH group in FR2 use the same numerology. For NR-DC, the maximum number of PUCCH groups in each cell group is one, and only the same numerology is supported for the cell group with carriers only in FR2.","paragraph_zero_based":14970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The NW may configure PUCCH for a BWP when setting up the BWP. The network may also add/remove the pucch-Config in an RRCReconfiguration with reconfigurationWithSync (for SpCell or PUCCH SCell) or with SCell release and add (for PUCCH SCell) to move the PUCCH between the UL and SUL carrier of one serving cell. In other cases, only modifications of a previously configured pucch-Config are allowed.","paragraph_zero_based":14971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If one (S)UL BWP of a serving cell is configured with PUCCH, all other (S)UL BWPs must be configured with PUCCH, too.","paragraph_zero_based":14972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pucch-ConfigurationList","paragraph_zero_based":14973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH configurations for two simultaneously constructed HARQ-ACK codebooks (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 9.1). Different PUCCH Resource IDs are configured in different PUCCH-Config within the pucch-ConfigurationList if configured.","paragraph_zero_based":14974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pucch-ConfigurationListMulticast1","paragraph_zero_based":14975}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["27a18d4846b88d5c380f6118ccd39635a5c56aeb57437bd4e313cee5d7c54845","1c032b52857c446041de992bdab99c8cf02b3c842dad83fc65c48fe19618dc0c","585cc49a429851879558da60170b660cf3479abf8af436103ae9e3b6c46b14e7","5de555872b232ac29166321e4f0fb6f48396c2230653d28228a2e8f6ca800087","0f1af671f494b2666e3d4e9587fcd4b0a4dd797993e46760cf90a0d5f8b3658a","4b2dba0843dc9201242eec152950bdf34145db8604f925141010a7f9e0bb70f3","e6922b7a195562eec3fe54929e5f0bc4751bda1831348faf90be71d6ed120cd2","20261667814b44eb76074cfad6ac41752c7e3cc159c325dff5c3d1bbd8530c67","b3134bfe22aa242984914b5d60b2e81ac91946da8a47c400854ab0135416a707","a15dc0139a1c7734972579165cf2892e7b617966621e239d5c9a32d6e4e572ba","33aee1b739b4d4b2a2e7edf9a4e61b30ff7be46166abb7aadae2cec77fa19a46","8ea6fa3d3ce3e06c0add4c4c12e3dc1500f5da5eec054d61514ce850fe272e67","0d342b835600fcc9a3bf9852d06036f64dc5347d0311c433d08f19c2759ad4be","6d5aae2a4328b7c2e760f65b711b120b6bdf63f057a54836027df48d7c62f071","21368b6b8eb2e64c916a268f1495978569832e7b37a209c1d0200b46e65c551e","086a116642703694d4294b93a41c6b8e38231c7333d516ba2b1a972139203ca6","1486c32792ae8e8188350e606eb998bdf1cf655ebf601cfd3d6b389fcad784ec","986b0652da472697f947d264bc6878a63add7d822ab26d3144736a987b59211a","f78757b0e097834c51182fc2b0403e8f6829b2550e0d55bc6c24a10ce6f85174","1b0d0750b4ef2e07823a44c14a1a06b3649db0df986cfbab4ead1f0f06949b4e","69eae09befde8a60a30bc37f90d1459bf0f27819335ff087c150014a8ccf1d05","57dfdb896bb46313dab7b648630f45a79aa0c39bd3a07a3ee2b587229ed10a1a","aa913c4ec9e204c15c3fada7878010e4d62261579abb292e9487669e973c4584","719c169669bc6887eacd0029f411384609e52cba73b43811a4b4a1b7098508ba"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[14952,14975],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p14952"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH configurations for two simultaneously constructed HARQ-ACK codebooks for MBS multicast (see TS 38.213, clause 9).","paragraph_zero_based":14976},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pucch-ConfigurationListMulticast2","paragraph_zero_based":14977},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH configurations for two simultaneously constructed NACK-only feedback for MBS multicast (see TS 38.213, clause 9).","paragraph_zero_based":14978},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pusch-Config","paragraph_zero_based":14979},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUSCH configuration for one BWP of the normal UL or SUL of a serving cell. If the UE is configured with SUL and if it has a PUSCH-Config for both UL and SUL, an UL/SUL indicator field in DCI indicates which of the two to use. See TS 38.212 [17], clause 7.3.1.","paragraph_zero_based":14980},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pucch-ConfigMulticast1","paragraph_zero_based":14981},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH configuration for the HARQ-ACK codebook for MBS multicast when multicast feedback is not configured with a priority value (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 9). If the field is not configured, pucch-Config applies.","paragraph_zero_based":14982},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pucch-ConfigMulticast2","paragraph_zero_based":14983},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH configuration for the NACK-only feedback for MBS multicast when multicast feedback is not configured with a priority value (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 9). If the field is not configured, pucch-Config applies.","paragraph_zero_based":14984},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PUCCH-Config","paragraph_zero_based":14985},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the UE specific PUCCH configurations used for the HARQ-ACK feedback reporting for NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":14986},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-Config","paragraph_zero_based":14987},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Uplink sounding reference signal configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":14988},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ul-powerControl","paragraph_zero_based":14989},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configures power control parameters for PUCCH, PUSCH and SRS when UE is configured with unifiedTCI-StateType for this serving cell. For each serving cell, ul-powerControl is either configured in all BWP-UplinkDedicated or it is not configured in any BWP-UplinkDedicated. When unifiedTCI-StateRef in the BWP-UplinkDedicated or in the PDSCH-Config if the unifiedTCI-StateType is set to joint, of a serving cell refers to another serving cell, ul-powerControl is either configured in all BWP-UplinkDedicated of these two serving cells or it is not configured in any BWP-UplinkDedicated of these two serving cells.","paragraph_zero_based":14990},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ul-TCI-StateList","paragraph_zero_based":14991},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the applicable UL TCI states for PUCCH, PUSCH and SRS.","paragraph_zero_based":14992},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ul-TCI-ToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":14993},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates a list of UL TCI states.","paragraph_zero_based":14994},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"unifiedTCI-StateRef","paragraph_zero_based":14995},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Provides the serving cell and UL BWP where UL TCI states applicable to this UL BWP are defined. The value of unifiedTCI-StateType of current serving cell is the same in the serving cell indicated by unifiedTCI-StateRef.","paragraph_zero_based":14996},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"useInterlacePUCCH-PUSCH","paragraph_zero_based":14997},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the field is present, the UE uses uplink frequency domain resource allocation Type 2 for PUSCH (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 8.3 and TS 38.214 [19], clause 6.1.2.2) and uses interlaced PUCCH Format 0, 1, 2, and 3 for PUCCH (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 9.2.1).","paragraph_zero_based":14998},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":14999}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["14c6e4beb04673e5acd732aec6e9248415708de9081522ae3b858f784cda5a8e","8f057df3d480385c0974a5f5a698521fc9c9578c17017af6d64d24e0c491651a","4279096a0456b5f49973d79f4640bc4ab4da4c27682b35b4216e85d3cd35dc9d","3be81313a047921514329a81502c51f037e0f13984639b520a0f53de330213e9","caa9c57662cf5a664cad7b83a7df69e9dc2cce763d7a0a3d487d1b0d17b8c82a","30c6146aecf75ac52014842161bcf7d97d4e4e19bffa4d7cd78477e00a69bc1b","9fb0aeda02f10673629e649074cca927a27a5b10e3c87babb620710f6359d5c0","31d13a0d2eefb8c2a78444705b262b326ba6eba8ec3fabe232ad13b55d85f028","c67bc611b7e780cea8cbac1774a7829cac01ea7a315aac7bd9a6ac00729cd85a","283568b05f5c1e80b5ef61b6ed113c40cf7eb6d6b0ce7ecc1bb8fa4d1d64906e","2d1fb62b1fad101e2df2d0d3b2ea0707ce03ded5d149252edd897791d69cbbb6","0b30bba49c4329ee831fcfc1498caa2c3330ad4a2f7698a05cbcba6d8d1fa1e2","ad3bb956dcd5366dbed564bcf2ebe109cc23ed3f36b964920c6bea7f3aa2a972","bf90e2da116202a04f79d275e5c47827c861ef2c9a0f8f8fdcde458fca8b44f4","957d2d6282e02f4bfecb19c87749c3e0001d81401fcf30d7e0e283d2560c7151","07c0cbff52bd97e277e762397f655952d96fcb624f19a3312e83535bfaf70b0f","dbcf8d70ea3c2ee514256b89c17e41ca6fdd04eeaa0ebb15c9df20b743db708e","1150f6a57d07181ae1e1caa66c68ae8c724aa95f6ee47bab722b529696c9160c","812189ef710aa43162380cfc2b2d1cf2be01f99d49ab997f645f5b41658caadc","2af12e26f964201dbcad7eaa3882ef2005f1777a8c28ac57a010da4cac6e99ce","4c94ae20067cb5eb1f6150c414407a530b3f99bf1be4f9a49de3096787738504","81a35f64417c19c3194bbcf0f3d8854e369661f5e669795bfd20d284d724943e","0734e49b9a9570c89d48a72c2490e8d464b7f8d943dc22801dfb12225d370085","12d143edd71c21f476725015911be1520f9575a02d0319c27887197b4a2167ef"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[14976,14999],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p14976"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":15000},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":15001},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NoTCI-PC","paragraph_zero_based":15002},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if unifiedTCI-StateType is configured for this serving cell and ul-powerControl is not configured for any UL TCI state or joint TCI state of this serving cell. Otherwise it is absent, Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15003},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SpCellOnly","paragraph_zero_based":15004},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need M, in the BWP-UplinkDedicated of an SpCell. It is absent otherwise. ","paragraph_zero_based":15005},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15006},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:In case of RRCReconfiguration with reconfigurationWithSync, the UE performs a MAC reset, which involves releasing the PUCCH-CSI/SRS/SR configuration in accordance with clause 5.3.12 and TS 38.321 [3], clauses 5.12 and 5.2. Hence, for these parts of the dedicated radio resource configuration, delta signalling is not supported in the message when reconfigurationWithSync is included.","paragraph_zero_based":15007},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15008},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CandidateBeamRS","paragraph_zero_based":15009},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CandidateBeamRS inlcudes candidate beams for beam failure recovery in case of beam failure detection. See also TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.17.","paragraph_zero_based":15010},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CandidateBeamRS information element","paragraph_zero_based":15011},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":15012},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CANDIDATEBEAMRS-START","paragraph_zero_based":15013},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15014},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15015},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CandidateBeamRS-r16 ::=                SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":15016},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    candidateBeamConfig-r16                CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":15017},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        ssb-r16                                SSB-Index,","paragraph_zero_based":15018},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        csi-RS-r16                             NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceId","paragraph_zero_based":15019},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    },","paragraph_zero_based":15020},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    servingCellId                          ServCellIndex                                                            OPTIONAL  -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15021},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":15022},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15023}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b3c0051d768ba0fdc6be2d4cebe5e5cbc6a7cc5d9c35115dc086676c2c45c6b4","3b621db8a68c8c11f609c4180edc2d453e22bc701bc20cf1ca665abca6d4e6d4","ed9e7afc1e9c344d3247c0735de4855adb2e0294a03f3e9c18d77e5446b46fee","6bca14355ba96c3bf778ea249b9d0ab927a87b5c1b128e7c6e7f29861d6a314c","8a765f8184585afd0109e0471b160d95da0f6f47844dd40ee46d48103fb72cd2","451389f107da88d4cf5b725b785084e627f7cba98e65f73d32661ebda93dd074","a983c1f35020891a3222030808b061fe241c76020ad87d6a52bbcb3ce4271023","be500d45a90ccd69519bd8cb5f986aec3b920ca9f78fbb4c85f1495a05876253","8dc81e47f6306f46082cb190e10a4e67557b7950c3438373731be5bc76d84df4","bae986fbf5df271757c33f5ce2e736f9921246155c118f9930f0b39a20815692","d855be30743c2474b3a36f4a4c8278aaea9fef9dbd2689226d0f0b7a240ad882","8f64ec308c5b494354305099b1b09b60ff5ae8648f95b3823738b1cd29f854ad","1effd93650fb41e8f04f88ac8681fc924dbfa2af03fdfb7819e663fa5853565d","c3b1115c465487723ff2e194b004ce087d73bf5fc3013ce81a882385a715a492","c99b5c20c33f12897fb9c97e8ca6efb3cbed49b8555046fa09e7df1e00f42fa1","76ad9de8f5486d72fc72597b482b282351aba2bb133d0148e0f2e27847ac8293","66b0b9384b0c8ef22e78e83fb462c3141d2225dcd16e96ae9b510461502ec09b","55591acc5565ce8ce958648019e35aef603b07e32186d84456f194a52827cdcf","918e6f511bb267f76d9b283f6b7846c403ba043a0f5fd7ee4fa461069a88a869","4b1111bf389e501d133ac06e2b86cbde1e1fb72d6f069b26e7e29cc657f680a3","c63fef3a82d4e0a3d7ea77d1a81b756b8a19568b926600aecd9fdbd3cd931fbf","c2e9d6b0a24d0cf4e7b5f0cc147ca3ad13163ed833c9a09a705a206551022337","c30898b94f663daf477d86debeb9b9cf82fb43cea2a582aa39faf81104c6b25e","e9f6405f214484d1f6baf5033fb51fb381b7d1bdb8befbe8f742b60bd7957da3"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[15000,15023],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p15000"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CANDIDATEBEAMRS-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":15024},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":15025},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15026},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CandidateBeamRS field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":15027},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"candidateBeamConfig","paragraph_zero_based":15028},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the resource (i.e. SSB or CSI-RS) defining this beam resource.","paragraph_zero_based":15029},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"servingCellId","paragraph_zero_based":15030},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the field is absent, the RS belongs to the serving cell in which BeamFailureRecoveryRSConfig is configured.","paragraph_zero_based":15031},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15032},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CellAccessRelatedInfo","paragraph_zero_based":15033},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CellAccessRelatedInfo indicates cell access related information for this cell.","paragraph_zero_based":15034},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CellAccessRelatedInfo information element","paragraph_zero_based":15035},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":15036},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CELLACCESSRELATEDINFO-START","paragraph_zero_based":15037},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15038},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CellAccessRelatedInfo   ::=         SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":15039},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    plmn-IdentityInfoList               PLMN-IdentityInfoList,","paragraph_zero_based":15040},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    cellReservedForOtherUse             ENUMERATED {true}             OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15041},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...,","paragraph_zero_based":15042},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":15043},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    cellReservedForFutureUse-r16        ENUMERATED {true}             OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15044},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    npn-IdentityInfoList-r16            NPN-IdentityInfoList-r16      OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15045},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]],","paragraph_zero_based":15046},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":15047}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["5ef028c471e770044b857c62e835de0a865a1b54755b86339764b62597adbf6c","79b96b486826df6b696328313831353d5a2880a7251c8f8ba8ef7f8ecfd5e95e","9031cff207b521bc3199fb793b8daf80e451bad851d69d07ad10aba7af5c8ab1","2b554583a316d1521886b45d711a33db0476578bc23804a5c24c5ca0a4a1e341","e2fad3df905030bf8df968d59925d6425d85799e64fd44ae2d358eb18aff4115","d16253c52bd76910e6a1a9e5ba419b9cde6eab11c01026ef04cee6fd46e7ed7c","e9bc8191e3665773db5baebc0e7d8bcce8bce087f26b338baaf22441bf7f02f8","31b76e6346bf04abeb7e04c3406ffeb4daa0c15eed82e1f172c8336f12b65245","eb5f76ccff0d2ad2379beba40530dbbf153402f2e49596a3b44802f2be44bcac","4f06d1f3344efe1d25edb3413ef9475767f8debf007712bf3b6e9710cc2b914b","b05308dfee685cd9f277dcec99cb9bd15a241b1148eb50d894fdca449ee70809","69bc06327eb3939574889f1a8270748e87287c376f33ebdd6d0174bc920da62e","0603497f05588b7903ebf11cf6d1790a92d999c173d8cb8b8454dda2f233fa7d","77e25bbee34e448dbbbfb30178133c7611c75717276dcd240bf829976c92386a","60b8db584eccf2d7f7a627ac9384d381617daf46ee8b6d0247b0dcc81e668a81","750c6806e213afb53702f2e45fefe14d984dbe6e836d23dfa22e77f1eb09197e","a7d00b9e015e0889fcf6e8fb475ec40847911e5a928228493e648dffead5edd3","f31e58c419c3914dd25df6d2aaa1082306c47d15ba78ba39e13fc14aa05ee5d7","2d17e7f6e642e9f98cdc64c3b0df2a1d009ea9f989d4637bb54d8fa9cd540919","fe29c5b54350a61346ecd0dc4ce768faf502ca5800c8299e04d259883a6ddbce","1a61956f14deeca511e12b7e2e84a54f63b10aa8945571709d46ced2ff40b27e","326bb42c1cd19a3b21ca32e3ddc6fff59e9b09dd2b28d19fa2c0b2f8e843ad73","5dbe57c7ed2b585cac77faf064a1a1ede0ddef2486ab1a9ac9cf897927a09e7a","718baec291338b1975a418a457f09b71af5eb41085160a486ebdb8fb2161e46b"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[15024,15047],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p15024"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    snpn-AccessInfoList-r17             SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNPN-r16)) OF SNPN-AccessInfo-r17    OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15048},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":15049},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":15050},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15051},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SNPN-AccessInfo-r17 ::=         SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":15052},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    extCH-Supported-r17                 ENUMERATED {true}             OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15053},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    extCH-WithoutConfigAllowed-r17      ENUMERATED {true}             OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15054},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    onboardingEnabled-r17               ENUMERATED {true}             OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15055},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    imsEmergencySupportForSNPN-r17      ENUMERATED {true}             OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":15056},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":15057},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15058},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CELLACCESSRELATEDINFO-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":15059},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":15060},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15061},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CellAccessRelatedInfo field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":15062},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellReservedForFutureUse","paragraph_zero_based":15063},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the cell is reserved, as defined in 38.304 [20] for future use. The field is applicable to all PLMNs and NPNs. This field is ignored by IAB-MT.","paragraph_zero_based":15064},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellReservedForOtherUse","paragraph_zero_based":15065},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the cell is reserved, as defined in 38.304 [20]. The field is applicable to all PLMNs. This field is ignored by IAB-MT for cell barring determination, but still considered by NPN capable IAB-MT for determination of an NPN-only cell.","paragraph_zero_based":15066},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"npn-IdentityInfoList","paragraph_zero_based":15067},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The npn-IdentityInfoList is used to configure a set of NPN-IdentityInfo elements. Each of those elements contains a list of one or more NPN Identities and additional information associated with those NPNs. The total number of PLMNs (identified by a PLMN identity in plmn -IdentityList), PNI-NPNs (identified by a PLMN identity and a CAG-ID), and SNPNs (identified by a PLMN identity and a NID) together in the PLMN-IdentityInfoList and NPN-IdentityInfoList does not exceed 12, except for the NPN-only cells. A PNI-NPN and SNPN can be included only once, and in only one entry of the NPN-IdentityInfoList. In case of NPN-only cells the PLMN-IdentityList contains a single element that does not count to the limit of 12 and the cellIdentity of the first entry of the PLMN-IdentityInfoList is set to the same value as the cellIdentity-r16 of the first entry of the NPN-IdentityInfoList. The NPN index is defined as B+c1+c2+…+c(n-1)+d1+d2+…+d(m-1)+e(i) for the NPN identity included in the n-th entry of NPN-IdentityInfoList and in the m-th entry of npn-Identitylist within that NPN-IdentityInfoList entry, and the i-th entry of its corresponding NPN-Identity, where","paragraph_zero_based":15068},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"- B is the index used for the last PLMN in the PLMN-IdentittyInfoList; in NPN-only cells B is considered 0;","paragraph_zero_based":15069},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"- c(j) is the number of NPN index values used in the j-th NPN-IdentityInfoList entry;","paragraph_zero_based":15070},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"- d(k) is the number of NPN index values used in the k-th npn-IdentityList entry within the n-th NPN-IdentityInfoList entry;","paragraph_zero_based":15071}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0b53e606e2062f07e790166706277d56546c45b446e817817b16719b330f2b68","ef432583f60fd6be548bdeeaf0b3367e06ef347707281b4d2ad5cfee5e64cf67","6f2a68fe5d234ebb237a492d02f077424752963c69933dcc4ffab543d23d2e75","cbac1067ffa8c0e32bcc689db35b93f202bdf779466b985caae357c791435323","7bb4665642938ed97488e5f1a3992221b17b87597c279398b548f9a63335e066","c73b51aa719ad05cb353c65d6c720b40b615884249fbaee211b34cbc96a88195","70e39400dd3e3e59f1f8e329af9da8c8876d9e16196a5af39c72a7135715eddf","d5f1d69fa4055d40dcf2b903e03f6b97e6c0356038ece246d1320468a7884880","ccecef18847f249cd2d82a1f5f48c2b53faa78385478b360df1fc49dcf80f554","1d75b4034309db54cb6d96646c659ac0142501b0de411c74f243cb7f600e4ed1","cfdcffddd9f5f3e9983c26f99f341f282b95fc8308b2f568b0685ba7ca0bfdc8","329007565cbf0a75989400065f49336ba07637191ddf507ba9d3e647dbf520bc","3105f0baa25756c88da722130445669ca16bb810b4b2f26a9179166c1b63e13e","3e5eed9b6686ce306cface099d25eb9bc244e246feb25db539ec285a76313913","296a1776233c5a4f3646d2adc8d2edd59d86bf71b603474cafe91ca4db337f43","adabb7b13394661e1d079f04fd464d1ade9123b1b766ad945319afb2888e419d","99344bb294843f32b863074357ae9040501e57e37eca1884f5920122cf99a7a2","a77ad57299e54b853020d8134223a0a55a159ba1232ece5df87dd3a8c7f4b491","a76d52a295b89c1af27cf7d91746e148d8ac26e2de6e26d84def48d612742758","2260e30bd92ddf8cb44b5f647da61d1237bcc8d7c69ce6ff06995a512ab6ceb0","5736f1e8006405ab1eeceb34e6b1dda0806716b504d036c1d71648fe5be12fa2","0573843e2982a3019f5557078ea99eb902f7072512034c588942c81e68daf739","160a75d3be70cbca32afc70c8bdc3611213f215d6ac6c921b8c3e0ad535dc668","f82a59558996f41e4137b792f2afff097ef0b169f01e7215bbb5187dc5cb232c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[15048,15071],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p15048"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"- e(i) is","paragraph_zero_based":15072},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    - i if the n-th entry of NPN-IdentityInfoList entry is for SNPN(s);","paragraph_zero_based":15073},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    - 1 if the n-th entry of NPN-IdentityInfoList entry is for PNI-NPN(s).","paragraph_zero_based":15074},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"plmn-IdentityInfoList","paragraph_zero_based":15075},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The plmn-IdentityInfoList is used to configure a set of PLMN-IdentityInfo elements. Each of those elements contains a list of one or more PLMN Identities and additional information associated with those PLMNs. A PLMN-identity can be included only once, and in only one entry of the PLMN-IdentityInfoList. The PLMN index is defined as b1+b2+…+b(n-1)+i for the PLMN included at the n-th entry of PLMN-IdentityInfoList and the i-th entry of its corresponding PLMN-IdentityInfo, where b(j) is the number of PLMN-Identity entries in each PLMN-IdentityInfo, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":15076},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"snpn-AccessInfoList","paragraph_zero_based":15077},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This list provides access related information for each SNPN in npn-IdentityInfoList, see TS 23.501 [32]. The n-th entry of the list contains the access related information of the n-th SNPN in npn-IdentityInfoList. ","paragraph_zero_based":15078},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15079},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SNPN-AccessInfo field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":15080},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"extCH-Supported","paragraph_zero_based":15081},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the SNPN supports access using credentials from a Credentials Holder as specified in TS 23.501 [32].","paragraph_zero_based":15082},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"extCH-WithoutConfigAllowed","paragraph_zero_based":15083},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the SNPN allows registration attempts with credentials from a Credentials Holder from UEs that are not explicitly configured to select the SNPN as specified in TS 23.501 [32].","paragraph_zero_based":15084},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"imsEmergencySupportForSNPN","paragraph_zero_based":15085},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the SNPN supports IMS emergency bearer services for UEs in limited service mode in the cell. If absent, IMS emergency call is not supported by the SNPN in the cell for UEs in limited service mode.","paragraph_zero_based":15086},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"onboardingEnabled","paragraph_zero_based":15087},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the onboarding SNPN allows registration for onboarding in the cell as specified in TS 23.501 [32].","paragraph_zero_based":15088},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15089},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CellAccessRelatedInfo-EUTRA-5GC","paragraph_zero_based":15090},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CellAccessRelatedInfo-EUTRA-5GC indicates cell access related information for an LTE cell connected to 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":15091},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CellAccessRelatedInfo-EUTRA-5GC information element","paragraph_zero_based":15092},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":15093},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CELLACCESSRELATEDINFOEUTRA-5GC-START","paragraph_zero_based":15094},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":15095}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c54