   drx-HARQ-RTT-TimerUL-r17                INTEGER (0..448)","paragraph_zero_based":18110},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":18111},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":18112},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-DRX-CONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":18113},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":18114},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":18115},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DRX-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":18116},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-HARQ-RTT-TimerDL","paragraph_zero_based":18117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of symbols of the BWP where the transport block was received. drx-HARQ-RTT-TimerDL-r17 is only applicable for SCS 480 kHz and 960 kHz. If configured, the UE shall ignore drx-HARQ-RTT-TimerDL (without suffix) for SCS 480 kHz and 960 kHz.","paragraph_zero_based":18118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-HARQ-RTT-TimerUL","paragraph_zero_based":18119}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["609c466fa6bcd81e8279d4227887e411bcad04c4bf4eba872a77906ac16ac121","2f1b13ff83b2ca42682bacaf0bd10752d21d88c7c7bb6ce3350707105c1d2650","688fae06d71dce50892a03c5e66b4b80a2b707efe40230bf1d2b798cfac1f6b8","d2559da2c3996b5a7718a28593de6818ee0e3b1bdf3fe115de085bd98e3cafa7","fa7fb7e73f75d1ad3c1907989e75214b35a555429f328d16524f12e65bd8b2ae","029e0c8508cc453da8b7ad4b5d7dfa34ce06f4fcc5a81804a3419182a1fddb2b","ab106aa5edafa2e77dd1101dad10767ce2e4f970147cac71e8b7c7d78758ea4e","2e3976d1d9dcb1fcfdf1bd1675b045cb9596d9f1a6a0dc3fc987c17bda197af6","1980fa12e7efce8a528e8a2d00233aadfe211a80499cdcb08773537a608dbb56","37216589bd901f3b8a272b12dcd0965031063ae73b2a1e1939c7c9274e9e20fb","278fff3cbc0bf59493c736a5af561e173210ac026c8545c304993f6d1b023f12","8075c353f39ff7fd4afa79cd5c6a1fe289f19e6160ba003c177afd9d0b61c5ab","6cfd96b12c64df9b9e544c23180dd83f1332d8e6f674393bea3463f22aed2c9f","be0385fc648d55e23843b228ab108c8c37442331eed7712c703ab06a9498054d","739bccb57d7538aa382115f8f99bd03a6460e1f81f646633dd189f261ef234d2","3b938d1397391d3cf9fa76231a341c970796005ad30754ece009fd018324c086","2c66d4cf02f67b5eb5269efdb606bc795fe8fc6f98589890b9c0f9de17acec21","f9e2edf8301b58e5845a7cf6d97d2687be8e28704b436e23c8e0a97270463046","39587b67ae493714119d910d7dd86eb8cf23bb2c7a790db28104acc2500cb475","a5d788489040e6d1268447955895e524c64228dda72728018e1e1a418c1a8108","6f011f0930d1f87b8f0aac3b5a39a376da59c673bc2ba02122eb56097635a9c5","bcb7a19c595b471d731a529d86f9289823a39384ea7e4104b08d232a2ad77156","327f95eeb5fc0dbcf5f919081044c4b3c22e2dc1e9c2bef6b9ee1f6c5d5a5f2e","bbfe02b5e20d0eaf0fe4b96ff39393c9bab30c10d03ec48e83bcf71408ea5113"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[18096,18119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p18096"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of symbols of the BWP where the transport block was transmitted. drx-HARQ-RTT-TimerUL-r17 is only applicable for SCS 480 kHz and 960 kHz. If configured, the UE shall ignore drx-HARQ-RTT-TimerUL (without suffix) for SCS 480 kHz and 960 kHz.","paragraph_zero_based":18120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-InactivityTimer","paragraph_zero_based":18121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in multiple integers of 1 ms. ms0 corresponds to 0, ms1 corresponds to 1 ms, ms2 corresponds to 2 ms, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":18122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-LongCycleStartOffset","paragraph_zero_based":18123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-LongCycle in ms and drx-StartOffset in multiples of 1 ms. If drx-ShortCycle is configured, the value of drx-LongCycle shall be a multiple of the drx-ShortCycle value.","paragraph_zero_based":18124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-onDurationTimer","paragraph_zero_based":18125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in multiples of 1/32 ms (subMilliSeconds) or in ms (milliSecond). For the latter, value ms1 corresponds to 1 ms, value ms2 corresponds to 2 ms, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":18126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-RetransmissionTimerDL","paragraph_zero_based":18127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of slot lengths of the BWP where the transport block was received. value sl0 corresponds to 0 slots, sl1 corresponds to 1 slot, sl2 corresponds to 2 slots, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":18128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-RetransmissionTimerUL","paragraph_zero_based":18129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of slot lengths of the BWP where the transport block was transmitted. sl0 corresponds to 0 slots, sl1 corresponds to 1 slot, sl2 corresponds to 2 slots, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":18130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-ShortCycleTimer","paragraph_zero_based":18131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in multiples of drx-ShortCycle. A value of 1 corresponds to drx-ShortCycle, a value of 2 corresponds to 2 * drx-ShortCycle and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":18132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-ShortCycle","paragraph_zero_based":18133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in ms. ms1 corresponds to 1 ms, ms2 corresponds to 2 ms, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":18134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-SlotOffset","paragraph_zero_based":18135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in 1/32 ms. Value 0 corresponds to 0 ms, value 1 corresponds to 1/32 ms, value 2 corresponds to 2/32 ms, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":18136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":18137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–DRX-ConfigSecondaryGroup","paragraph_zero_based":18138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE DRX-ConfigSecondaryGroup is used to configure DRX related parameters for the second DRX group as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":18139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DRX-ConfigSecondaryGroup information element","paragraph_zero_based":18140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":18141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-DRX-CONFIGSECONDARYGROUP-START","paragraph_zero_based":18142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":18143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["53c653ef232ffee627c14d10800511c666352dd26d0307de597be21fd95f2334","3afdbeadb3c8bce95d2334747bbfd509ee0d2e3ba2a