{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MeasObjectEUTRA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":19656},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"allowedMeasBandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":19657},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The maximum allowed measurement bandwidth on a carrier frequency as defined by the parameter Transmission Bandwidth Configuration \"NRB\" TS 36.104 [33].","paragraph_zero_based":19658},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"associatedMeasGap","paragraph_zero_based":19659},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the associated measurement gap for measuring this EUTRA frequency. If this field is absent, the associated meaurment gap is the gap configured via gapFR1 or gapUE.","paragraph_zero_based":19660},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"carrierFreq","paragraph_zero_based":19661},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Identifies EUTRA carrier frequency for which this configuration is valid. Network does not configure more than one MeasObjectEUTRA for the same physical frequency, regardless of the E-ARFCN used to indicate this.","paragraph_zero_based":19662},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellsToAddModListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":19663},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to add/ modify in the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19664},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellsToRemoveListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":19665},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to remove from the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19666},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra-PresenceAntennaPort1","paragraph_zero_based":19667},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When set to true, the UE may assume that at least two cell-specific antenna ports are used in all neighbouring cells.","paragraph_zero_based":19668},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra-Q-OffsetRange","paragraph_zero_based":19669},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used to indicate a cell, or frequency specific offset to be applied when evaluating triggering conditions for measurement reporting. The value is in dB. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, value dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":19670},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"excludedCellsToAddModListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":19671},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to add/ modify in the exclude-list of cells.","paragraph_zero_based":19672},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"excludedCellsToRemoveListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":19673},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to remove from the exclude-list of cells.","paragraph_zero_based":19674},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"widebandRSRQ-Meas","paragraph_zero_based":19675},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If set to true, the UE shall, when performing RSRQ measurements, use a wider bandwidth in accordance with TS 36.133 [40]. The network may set the field to true if the measurement bandwidth indicated by allowedMeasBandwidth is 50 resource blocks or larger; otherwise the network sets this field to false.","paragraph_zero_based":19676},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":19677},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–MeasObjectId","paragraph_zero_based":19678},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE MeasObjectId used to identify a measurement object configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":19679}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0c5a28c20258771ebb105693c53fbe09aaa827c1a22ae64806e06814058521e1","d3b96a46ff1bf30b84987c503ed28b8c4cbf1aac4f4262fd28443d6ea878a259","e90c11230c9cdecf31a7e9927c784cf71e609cf8703590472149