{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if supplementaryUplink is configured within ServingCellConfig. It is mandatory present otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":24384},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24385},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–Q-OffsetRange","paragraph_zero_based":24386},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE Q-OffsetRange is used to indicate a cell, beam or measurement object specific offset to be applied when evaluating candidates for cell re-selection or when evaluating triggering conditions for measurement reporting. The value is in dB. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":24387},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Q-OffsetRange information element","paragraph_zero_based":24388},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":24389},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-Q-OFFSETRANGE-START","paragraph_zero_based":24390},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24391},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Q-OffsetRange ::=                   ENUMERATED {","paragraph_zero_based":24392},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-24, dB-22, dB-20, dB-18, dB-16, dB-14,","paragraph_zero_based":24393},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-12, dB-10, dB-8, dB-6, dB-5, dB-4, dB-3,","paragraph_zero_based":24394},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-2, dB-1, dB0, dB1, dB2, dB3, dB4, dB5,","paragraph_zero_based":24395},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB6, dB8, dB10, dB12, dB14, dB16, dB18,","paragraph_zero_based":24396},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB20, dB22, dB24}","paragraph_zero_based":24397},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24398},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-Q-OFFSETRANGE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":24399},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":24400},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24401},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–Q-QualMin","paragraph_zero_based":24402},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE Q-QualMin is used to indicate for cell selection/ re-selection the required minimum received RSRQ level in the (NR) cell. Corresponds to parameter Qqualmin in TS 38.304 [20]. Actual value Qqualmin = field value [dB].","paragraph_zero_based":24403},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Q-QualMin information element","paragraph_zero_based":24404},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":24405},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-Q-QUALMIN-START","paragraph_zero_based":24406},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24407}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8001e59340f8c26082db137c19ad171b2238b3ced088eae273b8363ddec5fa2e","dc99cc8c8a18e9107b3954d609b06fee4fba962c43fd08fbdb7dc0de2c416a6a","f946856bed87da7dcb93e38f2bf2eb156c7ac9f34d87d0730434d27d222c1b68","7bd41820abcfb9fece734bd3ad7a4316c943840e03c45897e3bed4b890812aad","db639d8fd87b89906c5a8b4c692c436e3d5ced632f499119ccc8e6a85e1f18d1","5a40d64af427fea4a149c5ce272962699a843f8b6846fe16c98b7ab11a95951d","70597baaae062b9c5469312c7d0ce857c2c54ccbd4156c54c82b1185a73963f5","c0f8fb35f2defef9fedd801d9e0df76f5bb1eb3a982776b0b8184932a04c6256","57f03ceefc3e167b89bce90b6fb75991a7c23fb