{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    prach-ConfigurationIndex-v1610              INTEGER (256..262)                                              OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":24888},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]],","paragraph_zero_based":24889},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":24890},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ra-ResponseWindow-v1700                     ENUMERATED {sl240, sl320, sl640, sl960, sl1280, sl1920, sl2560} OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":24891},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":24892},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":24893},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24894},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RACH-CONFIGGENERIC-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":24895},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":24896},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24897},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH-ConfigGeneric field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":24898},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msg1-FDM","paragraph_zero_based":24899},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The number of PRACH transmission occasions FDMed in one time instance. (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 6.3.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":24900},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msg1-FrequencyStart","paragraph_zero_based":24901},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Offset of lowest PRACH transmission occasion in frequency domain with respective to PRB 0. The value is configured so that the corresponding RACH resource is entirely within the bandwidth of the UL BWP. (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 6.3.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":24902},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"powerRampingStep","paragraph_zero_based":24903},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Power ramping steps for PRACH (see TS 38.321 [3],5.1.3).","paragraph_zero_based":24904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"prach-ConfigurationFrameOffset-IAB","paragraph_zero_based":24905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Frame offset for ROs defined in the baseline configuration indicated by prach-ConfigurationIndex and is used only by the IAB-MT. (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 6.3.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":24906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"prach-ConfigurationIndex","paragraph_zero_based":24907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PRACH configuration index. For prach-ConfigurationIndex configured under beamFailureRecoveryConfig, the prach-ConfigurationIndex can only correspond to the short preamble format, (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 6.3.3.2). If the field prach-ConfigurationIndex-v1610 is present, the UE shall ignore the value provided in prach-ConfigurationIndex (without suffix).","paragraph_zero_based":24908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"prach-ConfigurationPeriodScaling-IAB","paragraph_zero_based":24909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scaling factor to extend the periodicity of the baseline configuration indicated by prach-ConfigurationIndex and is used only by the IAB-MT. Value scf1 corresponds to scaling factor of 1 and so on. (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 6.3.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":24910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"prach-ConfigurationSOffset-IAB","paragraph_zero_based":24911}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c41d3aef2f4272ef65c8f436ba224adf9307763079ec9b973098dc8478107758","1f6bff79fa63f560bb0aa172c9de60085ca061372714a482f0f36b4ac8e089db","f264b6121c81572bb26f6ff95d93d0f7fb937932c8e9b00bf34806dedec988a6","aa02052f0e19b2cead9dc