{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-15 kHz: 280.","paragraph_zero_based":28152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-30 kHz: 560.","paragraph_zero_based":28153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-60 kHz: 1120.","paragraph_zero_based":28154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-120 kHz: 560.","paragraph_zero_based":28155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-480 kHz: 2240.","paragraph_zero_based":28156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-960 kHz: 4480.","paragraph_zero_based":28157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"positionInDCI","paragraph_zero_based":28158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Position in DCI of the bit field indicating Channel Occupancy duration for UE's serving cells (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1.1).","paragraph_zero_based":28159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"servingCelIId","paragraph_zero_based":28160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The ID of the serving cell for which the configuration is applicable.","paragraph_zero_based":28161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"subcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":28162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reference subcarrier spacing for the list of Channel Occupancy durations (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1.1).","paragraph_zero_based":28163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Only the following values are applicable depending on the used frequency range:","paragraph_zero_based":28164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1:    15, 30, or 60 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":28165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-2:  120, 480, or 960 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":28166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28167},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SearchSpaceSwitchTrigger field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":28168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"positionInDCI","paragraph_zero_based":28169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The position of the bit within DCI payload containing a search space switching flag (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1.1).","paragraph_zero_based":28170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"servingCellId","paragraph_zero_based":28171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The ID of the serving cell for which the configuration is applicable or the group of serving cells as indicated by CellGroupsForSwitch-r16 containing this servingCellId.","paragraph_zero_based":28172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–S-NSSAI","paragraph_zero_based":28174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE S-NSSAI (Single Network Slice Selection Assistance Information) identifies a Network Slice end to end and comprises a slice/service type and a slice differentiator, see TS 23.003 [21].","paragraph_zero_based":28175}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f2d4e878b87404a825d91c04c6aa794b6b3ea8520bc0c569cacff77167cbc3aa","462ce916e22ad9f8ec13ea6c6a44c640f251f9082ad253519392a2da19627fd0","b66b77cfc49f7793a3ab00dba26e27c194b0e04a689589b5befab07668436d42","225663013ad2ac34a2113860ca8323cf80532454a155aa2eea1996fccfc28ac0","eee710e92981ed021283b1430727f60dface83b48028bbf594ff6509e6afa9e1","3e2a7d1ee7e8e746844a768318d285b44673979bac1986d3d4fedfffe8683f86","eb323f66285e57f4c6802d8e3b08d05b6e7dc3e4665da94b0b1b857d4e275f1a","c3668cfd5ea3220951b4fe26af9610fff9ede20281da953d8554ead56b178482","22d6daefd586a1cdfcb957b70729667bffaa21b9c984eee021fd83c32b83b56f","f8a4245a9ce261fbc1f02e484dc69e5eaeb7149a548b1074843cefd8f3b06407","166766d1b016af6cee44ef61ac69fd2f5731e041281a435b918b19dc7a024c1d","09599666e062aa539e89fb1943c8c614273d2407e4f527ab8ad75a