{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28944},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS-TPC-CommandConfig ::=               SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":28945},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    startingBitOfFormat2-3                  INTEGER (1..31)                                                     OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":28946},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    fieldTypeFormat2-3                      INTEGER (0..1)                                                      OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":28947},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...,","paragraph_zero_based":28948},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":28949},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    startingBitOfFormat2-3SUL               INTEGER (1..31)                                                     OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":28950},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":28951},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":28952},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28953},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SRS-TPC-COMMANDCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":28954},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":28955},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28956},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS-TPC-CommandConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":28957},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"fieldTypeFormat2-3","paragraph_zero_based":28958},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The type of a field within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional), which indicates how many bits in the field are for SRS request (0 or 2).","paragraph_zero_based":28959},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Note that for Type A, there is a common SRS request field for all SCells in the set, but each SCell has its own TPC command bits. See TS 38.212 [17] clause 7.3.1 and , TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.3.","paragraph_zero_based":28960},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"startingBitOfFormat2-3","paragraph_zero_based":28961},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The starting bit position of a block within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional) and TPC commands. The value 1 of the field corresponds to the first/left most bit of format2-3. The value 2 of the field corresponds to the second bit format2-3, and so on (see TS 38.212 [17], clause 7.3.1 and TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.3).","paragraph_zero_based":28962},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"startingBitOfFormat2-3SUL","paragraph_zero_based":28963},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The starting bit position of a block within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional) and TPC commands for SUL carrier (see TS 38.212 [17], clause 7.3.1 and TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.3).","paragraph_zero_based":28964},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28965},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SSB-Index","paragraph_zero_based":28966},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SSB-Index identifies an SS-Block within an SS-Burst. See TS 38.213 [13], clause 4.1.","paragraph_zero_based":28967}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2602549fa2eb2702193a5266ddf1bba79f47f3f5d9e0f3e2d546d196958b4c6d","298e079e7c2b0f2e6fc3a09ee7acee546e23417e5b13b2ca59ec46a18a51eb10","eb606f78878510af62ea562c12089162ac84cb14a0eb8893c181e09365e7e654","cc5e67b5e0c76122e40bb103193b2262f3c296ef13b45158cb38671699c9c128","fd0b29c57ec4dd2f73b4d5005e5bba51c62e385d53ff9a5dda44e7b38