{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"referenceSubcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":29376},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reference SCS used to determine the time domain boundaries in the UL-DL pattern which must be common across all subcarrier specific carriers, i.e., independent of the actual subcarrier spacing using for data transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":29377},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Only the following values are applicable depending on the used frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":29378},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1:    15, 30, or 60 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":29379},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-1:  60 or 120 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":29380},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-2:  120, 480, or 960 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":29381},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":29382},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The network configures a not larger than any SCS of configured BWPs for the serving cell. The network or SL-PreconfigGeneral configures a not larger than the SCS of (pre-)configured SL BWP.See TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1.","paragraph_zero_based":29383},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":29384},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TDD-UL-DL-Pattern field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":29385},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dl-UL-TransmissionPeriodicity","paragraph_zero_based":29386},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Periodicity of the DL-UL pattern, see TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1. If the dl-UL-TransmissionPeriodicity-v1530 is signalled, UE shall ignore the dl-UL-TransmissionPeriodicity (without suffix).","paragraph_zero_based":29387},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nrofDownlinkSlots","paragraph_zero_based":29388},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of consecutive full DL slots at the beginning of each DL-UL pattern, see TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1. In this release, the maximum value for this field is 320.","paragraph_zero_based":29389},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nrofDownlinkSymbols","paragraph_zero_based":29390},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of consecutive DL symbols in the beginning of the slot following the last full DL slot (as derived from nrofDownlinkSlots). The value 0 indicates that there is no partial-downlink slot. (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1).","paragraph_zero_based":29391},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nrofUplinkSlots","paragraph_zero_based":29392},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of consecutive full UL slots at the end of each DL-UL pattern, see TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1. In this release, the maximum value for this field is 320.","paragraph_zero_based":29393},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nrofUplinkSymbols","paragraph_zero_based":29394},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of consecutive UL symbols in the end of the slot preceding the first full UL slot (as derived from nrofUplinkSlots). The value 0 indicates that there is no partial-uplink slot. (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.1).","paragraph_zero_based":29395},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":29396},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–TDD-UL-DL-ConfigDedicated","paragraph_zero_based":29397},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE TDD-UL-DL-ConfigDedicated determines the UE-specific Uplink/Downlink TDD configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":29398},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TDD-UL-DL-ConfigDedicated information element","paragraph_zero_based":29399}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["60ee2c3f9a72e2fc3de8253813ef910c81df5b59