{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CRS-InterfMitigation-r17 ::=        SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":32064},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-1 CRS-IM (Interference Mitigation) in DSS scenario","paragraph_zero_based":32065},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-DSS-15kHzSCS-r17             ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":32066},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-2 CRS-IM in non-DSS and 15 kHz NR SCS scenario, without the assistance of network signaling on LTE channel bandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":32067},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-nonDSS-15kHzSCS-r17          ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":32068},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-3 CRS-IM in non-DSS and 15 kHz NR SCS scenario, with the assistance of network signaling on LTE channel bandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":32069},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-nonDSS-NWA-15kHzSCS-r17      ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":32070},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-4 CRS-IM in non-DSS and 30 kHz NR SCS scenario, without the assistance of network signaling on LTE channel bandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":32071},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-nonDSS-30kHzSCS-r17          ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":32072},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-5 CRS-IM in non-DSS and 30 kHz NR SCS scenario, with the assistance of network signaling on LTE channel bandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":32073},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-nonDSS-NWA-30kHzSCS-r17      ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL","paragraph_zero_based":32074},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":32075},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32076},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETDOWNLINKPERCC-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32077},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32078},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32079},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id","paragraph_zero_based":32080},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id identifies a set of features applicable to one carrier of a feature set. The FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id of a FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC is the index position of the FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC in the featureSetsDownlinkPerCC. The first element in the list is referred to by FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id = 1, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":32081},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id information element","paragraph_zero_based":32082},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":32083},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETDOWNLINKPERCC-ID-START","paragraph_zero_based":32084},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32085},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id ::=      INTEGER (1..maxPerCC-FeatureSets)","paragraph_zero_based":32086},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32087}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c77a03da1bd892d8648c6d8173a2bed4c3c3065bb332d541aaa7f1ad2a547029","4cdcd70de1f04219d13b41c4bfcc1e3fce1d519c77