{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-CR-Limit-r16                       INTEGER(0..10000)                                                     OPTIONAL,   -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":37296},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-TxParameters-r16                   SL-PSSCH-TxParameters-r16                                             OPTIONAL    -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":37297},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":37298},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37299},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-r16 ::=                        INTEGER (0..100)","paragraph_zero_based":37300},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37301},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-CBR-COMMONTXCONFIGLIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":37302},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":37303},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37304},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-CommonTxConfigList field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":37305},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CBR-RangeConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":37306},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the list of CBR ranges. Each entry of the list indicates in SL-CBR-LevelsConfig the upper bound of the CBR range for the respective entry. The upper bounds of the CBR ranges are configured in ascending order for consecutive entries of sl-CBR-RangeConfigList. For the first entry of sl-CBR-RangeConfigList the lower bound of the CBR range is 0. Value 0 corresponds to 0, value 1 to 0.01, value 2 to 0.02, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":37307},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CR-Limit","paragraph_zero_based":37308},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the maximum limit on the occupancy ratio. Value 0 corresponds to 0, value 1 to 0.0001, value 2 to 0.0002, and so on (i.e. in steps of 0.0001) until value 10000, which corresponds to 1.","paragraph_zero_based":37309},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CBR-PSSCH-TxConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":37310},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the list of available PSSCH transmission parameters (such as MCS, sub-channel number, retransmission number and CR limit) configurations.","paragraph_zero_based":37311},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TxParameters","paragraph_zero_based":37312},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates PSSCH transmission parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":37313},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37314},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-ConfigDedicatedNR","paragraph_zero_based":37315},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-ConfigDedicatedNR specifies the dedicated configuration information for NR sidelink communication/discovery.","paragraph_zero_based":37316},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-ConfigDedicatedNR information element","paragraph_zero_based":37317},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":37318},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-CONFIGDEDICATEDNR-START","paragraph_zero_based":37319}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ebbe6d06384b1d7fe8a0cfce04c6880288630e00c194efa509b6cac544afd5a5","552fca0d5760e9248f40de7977f16a2de713cfbd4783d1bcda77920d33763403","815885b678635186f48ec2f826e2e945f7b2f0ecb237ec4a71610ebcbe70120f","2a2d5853e14ba853661ea5ceac8071c4a66facebd45522f3566c989e268a0755","6f411d91b007d84a831885d44527afdc109e00fd88a9c8883210df5fd3c02dfb","e0aa4d1ea0a3a82dce8ec585c377eefcc03996263520d16bd431291375be07e9"