{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TimeReferenceSFN-Type1","paragraph_zero_based":37488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates SFN used for determination of the offset of a resource in time domain. If it is present, the UE uses the 1st logical slot of associated resource pool after the starting time of the closest SFN with the indicated number preceding the reception of the sidelink configured grant configuration type 1 as reference logical slot, see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.8.3. If it is not present, the reference SFN is 0.","paragraph_zero_based":37489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TimeResourceCG-Type1","paragraph_zero_based":37490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the time resource location of sidelink configured grant type 1. An index giving valid combinations of up to two slot positions (jointly encoded) as time resource indicator value (TRIV), as defined in TS 38.212 [17].","paragraph_zero_based":37491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-DestinationIdentity","paragraph_zero_based":37493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-DestinationIdentity is used to identify a destination of a NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":37494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DestinationIdentity information element","paragraph_zero_based":37495},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":37496},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-DESTINATIONIDENTITY-START","paragraph_zero_based":37497},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37498},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DestinationIdentity-r16 ::=           BIT STRING (SIZE (24))","paragraph_zero_based":37499},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37500},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-DESTINATIONIDENTITY-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":37501},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":37502},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37503},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-DRX-Config","paragraph_zero_based":37504},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-DRX-Config is used to configure DRX related parameters for NR sidelink communication/discovery. The SL DRX timers should be calculated in the unit of physical slot.","paragraph_zero_based":37505},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DRX-Config information element","paragraph_zero_based":37506},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":37507},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-DRX-CONFIG-START","paragraph_zero_based":37508},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37509},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DRX-Config-r17 ::=                      SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":37510},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-DRX-ConfigGC-BC-r17                     SL-DRX-ConfigGC-BC-r17                                                 OPTIONAL,     -- Cond HO","paragraph_zero_based":37511}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a3e8235a84497b01c9d2bc0a4fbb77f4b9d6aa16e137ac9acf4a4f9cc5177fb5","53dde81a9e4253ff7ed0116c607ba3f7795770c2559a03f39cf4fc104f9ea31e","76e3d6ae260eb436dd90f41b155efde02a34a26b96e9c7e785ad0cde1caf353c","5fbd4ef8e4ecbaf07db5d7f98faa7e93e4e73b8d12fcb6ab120e8df865c74032","679039ead8931bfdeabac60aa69f0cd0eb82901d471eb0bdf957b77681d73263","0059c2a1b1c11b8d896aca6ebdb4d5cea1c673b06c273601c29c695a00ec5106","d7dd749e714f6bf7950e8f12110a62e60a6cba484edfd7ab