{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-SyncPriority-r16              ENUMERATED {gnss, gnbEnb}                                           OPTIONAL, -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":37776},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-NbAsSync-r16                  BOOLEAN                                                             OPTIONAL, -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":37777},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-SyncConfigList-r16            SL-SyncConfigList-r16                                               OPTIONAL, -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":37778},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":37779},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":37780},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-FREQCONFIGCOMMON-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":37781},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":37782},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37783},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-FreqConfigCommon field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":37784},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"frequencyShift7p5khzSL","paragraph_zero_based":37785},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Enable the NR SL transmission with a 7.5 kHz shift to the LTE raster. If the field is absent, the frequency shift is disabled.","paragraph_zero_based":37786},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-AbsoluteFrequencyPointA","paragraph_zero_based":37787},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Absolute frequency of the reference resource block (Common RB 0). Its lowest subcarrier is also known as Point A.","paragraph_zero_based":37788},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-AbsoluteFrequencySSB","paragraph_zero_based":37789},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the frequency location of sidelink SSB. The transmission bandwidth for sidelink SSB is within the bandwidth of this sidelink BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":37790},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-BWP-List","paragraph_zero_based":37791},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the list of sidelink BWP(s) on which the NR sidelink communication configuration. In this release, only one BWP is allowed to be configured for NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":37792},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-NbAsSync","paragraph_zero_based":37793},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates whether the network can be selected as synchronization reference directly/indirectly only, if sl-SyncPriority is set to gnss. If this field is set to TRUE, the network is enabled to be selected as synchronization reference directly/indirectly. The field is only present in SidelinkPreconfigNR. Otherwise it is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":37794},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SyncPriority","paragraph_zero_based":37795},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates synchronization priority order, as specified in clause 5.8.6..","paragraph_zero_based":37796},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SyncConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":37797},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the configuration by which the UE is allowed to receive and transmit synchronisation information for NR sidelink communication. Network configures sl-SyncConfig including txParameters when configuring UEs to transmit synchronisation information. If this field is configured in SL-PreconfigurationNR-r16, only one entry is configured in sl-SyncConfigList.","paragraph_zero_based":37798},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"valueN","paragraph_zero_based":37799}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","