{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-NumReservedBits","paragraph_zero_based":38832},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of reserved bits in first stage SCI.","paragraph_zero_based":38833},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TimeResourcePSCCH","paragraph_zero_based":38834},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of symbols of PSCCH in a resource pool.","paragraph_zero_based":38835},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38836},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-PSSCH-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38837},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-BetaOffsets2ndSCI","paragraph_zero_based":38838},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates candidates of beta-offset values to determine the number of coded modulation symbols for second stage SCI. The value indicates the index of Table 9.3-2 of TS 38.213 [13].","paragraph_zero_based":38839},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PSSCH-DMRS-TimePatternList","paragraph_zero_based":38840},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the set of PSSCH DMRS time domain patterns in terms of PSSCH DMRS symbols in a slot that can be used in the resource pool.","paragraph_zero_based":38841},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-Scaling","paragraph_zero_based":38842},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates a scaling factor to limit the number of resource elements assigned to the second stage SCI on PSSCH. Value f0p5 corresponds to 0.5, value f0p65 corresponds to 0.65, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":38843},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38844},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-PSFCH-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38845},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MinTimeGapPSFCH","paragraph_zero_based":38846},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The minimum time gap between PSFCH and the associated PSSCH in the unit of slots.","paragraph_zero_based":38847},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-NumMuxCS-Pair","paragraph_zero_based":38848},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of cyclic shift pairs used for a PSFCH transmission that can be multiplexed in a PRB.","paragraph_zero_based":38849},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PSFCH-CandidateResourceType","paragraph_zero_based":38850},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of PSFCH resources available for multiplexing HARQ-ACK information in a PSFCH transmission (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 16.3).","paragraph_zero_based":38851},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PSFCH-HopID","paragraph_zero_based":38852},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scrambling ID for sequence hopping of the PSFCH used in the resource pool.","paragraph_zero_based":38853},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PSFCH-Period","paragraph_zero_based":38854},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the period of PSFCH resource in the unit of slots within this resource pool. If set to sl0, no resource for PSFCH, and HARQ feedback for all transmissions in the resource pool is disabled.","paragraph_zero_based":38855}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["828c7adb66ad0f3f875262c3a175016c95127f77f757998b618b3459c6499d1b","0d5287b9c7371854bb1b8cd2c98dba6e74204e65a48935f4ab5356f532167e54","e3da3dc14f5fe597837625dcc9ddd0251a024be6f6a244b03f52c0ac818d394a","ec2b0aa046bcaaae2575069239bb333a9ade05c28d7f7ee5ab039f9a2ddb7067","1dbb37f89fa39be199181ffcaf22bfb34862ad45d9ab713f23c7fd3e0f0f1c92","c6a9d67e799978f949e3f1301717ea3a2b4412e95c7d749b2eb69a2416e4a74b","5bc6b9de85c780f36ffd4eee65c47f529b8e9df0977e38b4407ce69e0474395a","4d60dfe201c25df0d3ef054c30bd07d57d966bdaf8924f6ff73e0dbe89894b0a","bb1af0a81cb979b62fbb7af81faf1325fbb9e46c7361b1a5db9f1b3b9281f8ef","21e68c5dafbd7ee98ff03a7b198441028e857160247c8316b29bec6d7bcd9266","bf8236a0f7770730767d8fd633ee7dcde6e2d0a36f16708e342e04d910f2c671","2e804fe29e15ae074ed3e77ec163e530d99e5d782de1fda66fa956b28cb7f1eb","7b6a37f8f5be2f55b4d07c9a4a690a2fc7a5732b5779cd711be3950adbec49e1","a541887a64187eada8520b8940134a1feadac88fbe503a5e021957fce724304f","e2b6710ebb7f1af11db23efa9e68cfdd6a6b21210396297090f72a333b976197","6e8e0e226a708242c5d9349035dc47f46c41d2340261aff341e4067864d1f0dc","4e799b006ea4fb292da8e060ca92a3e88bc0015c37cd0d993e3c06855e131d35","6cc6abb1bcaa3e7075b499e97a3fcd20d196c51e46e6925b2abd6550130fdfd9","395ddece641cd01ce1d643bc1e48301322f35f1efcb9f42f180898a533f72dfc","e849813fad02a7305ce1a24a56de74b6aceff9e09f9ef3e403b3fd2abf0240d5","46143234f355db478f5a93a00e6b271bfb218aee8c31110f96974a4886108f01","2bff9409430482606d92ecc188ca0e9103027993d138f5751aadf91896e557d6","62d35ba9365743df238cd67221348ecd527dd54046f695f4cc4eb729e5a9d335","bde50ef7c88c362b54d1e1ed79fa66c32e23c65b662b79455a1d6e46ca500dae"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[38832,38855],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p38832"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PSFCH-RB-Set","paragraph_zero_based":38856},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the set of PRBs that are actually used for PSFCH transmission and reception. The leftmost bit of the bitmap refers to the lowest RB index in the resource pool, and so on. Value 0 in the bitmap indicates that the corresponding PRB is not used for PSFCH transmission and reception while value 1 indicates that the corresponding PRB is used for PSFCH transmission and reception (see TS 38.213 [13]).","paragraph_zero_based":38857},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38858},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-PTRS-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38859},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PTRS-FreqDensity","paragraph_zero_based":38860},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence and frequency density of SL PT-RS  as a function of scheduled BW. If the field is not configured, the UE uses K_PT-RS = 2","paragraph_zero_based":38861},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PTRS-TimeDensity","paragraph_zero_based":38862},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence and time density of SL PT-RS  as a function of MCS. If the field is not configured, the UE uses L_PT-RS = 1","paragraph_zero_based":38863},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PTRS-RE-Offset","paragraph_zero_based":38864},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the subcarrier offset for SL PT-RS . If the field is not configured, the UE applies the value offset00 (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 8.4.1.2.2).","paragraph_zero_based":38865},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38866},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-UE-SelectedConfigRP field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38867},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":38868},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the mapping between PSSCH transmission parameter (such as MCS, PRB number, retransmission number, CR limit) sets by using the indexes of the configurations in sl-CBR-PSSCH-TxConfigList, CBR ranges by using the indexes to the entry of the CBR range configurations in sl-CBR-RangeConfigList, and priority ranges. It also indicates the default PSSCH transmission parameters to be used when CBR measurement results are not available, and MCS range for the MCS tables used in the resource pool. The field sl-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList-v1650 is present only when sl-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList-r16 is configured.","paragraph_zero_based":38869},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MaxNumPerReserve","paragraph_zero_based":38870},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the maximum number of reserved PSCCH/PSSCH resources that can be indicated by an SCI.","paragraph_zero_based":38871},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MultiReserveResource","paragraph_zero_based":38872},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates if it is allowed to reserve a sidelink resource for an initial transmission of a TB by an SCI associated with a different TB, based on sensing and resource selection procedure.","paragraph_zero_based":38873},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-ResourceReservePeriodList","paragraph_zero_based":38874},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Set of possible resource reservation period allowed in the resource pool in the unit of ms. Up to 16 values can be configured per resource pool. The value ms0 is always configured.","paragraph_zero_based":38875},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-RS-ForSensing","paragraph_zero_based":38876},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether DMRS of PSCCH or PSSCH is used for L1 RSRP measurement in the sensing operation.","paragraph_zero_based":38877},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SensingWindow","paragraph_zero_based":38878},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameter that indicates the start of the sensing window.","paragraph_zero_based":38879}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6b7f8dd1aa0cc3015d3311d935e420f732de6308ad4f0391e492c9fab4ea7192","c028451f80877199216a511e29606d4e7ebab88f226863b01fe710b7678fc917","af8d1379a0e53517c95b290cdd1c68f7b7451f2810a942b1626acaa02083c179","e940168a401492caad18a1947a175ba1fb5b7db9d542fb88f6da9ea02e5d461b","ff31e59dfee982c1782eff5ee68a6a2688f9b6573ab9120e1338bb4e699c57ba","772f9ad55a05a65e61744980dbfaf37da7562f88460c7089b26c3f1001ebc529","5e64af722dae6dd940084f7ad74cd86fec6575429d63885b86b581d927cf04ff","cc2f3f166425c75668aed4fd416b477210345cc4163eb24ae2c70d87ec6d4671","e7c7d806105c3405e77042a142e28022d9ee37f66a39183807829abb01cc86d6","dc1c065b4fbea8bff9a4ecf451c8eb4f75e2aea4eeeca38b9a179032ea396ae0","c83ac555128d3887ee3e797fd701eafba617aae5bb4e39eb1c4d8e5132f591fb","7d8b918616fc9ae60fecfd09264c68495e072830a1dcdabb21aad19ba7c11031","5f298cbf39fc9c33ca465748b9ceb82dedf146527a7fb96018b015b8a89696b2","5d3e86a24ec8634d17a9f6eed029f891c5a307c47b680b35d39afd28ba670ef0","eb66c21b3f53dcc22ea96733a9d2c9b06d6790f188bd4744bf0783d6dcbd5a34","f4b45bd19f9fb6ce9e07bfbdff56c4f9b47239ab3d3d926d2c881298ec9e985b","0e63c6d753119387da30c2d0091823cdfea5efa811d89ca82188488d0730c716","be422ba291a4cd5db18cff5bef9599836dcc23940e155973262ec10f2298b456","87da0fa6d9995e8f669cf7e20c9184137c428907eeae536e06c7e03709eb5885","6fe178e1e415c9e6a032840b2cfd3c6a9b2886cfc4a5e117d3519ffa1cabe498","18beec5045980a6449e7bf9ec94c79576ad2201b874fb19ea5c3116a30697f81","42b37d101c5ff3b76f2ee504a16c2f4de9e3433bc91bf70dabc9da7d0d2771f5","28dfa856ed5f41eb8c100cded0da1927cdcc80c798a53f3e45ebf901864605ec","43ab8835248dbe3b94cab343ff26d5f32c29a5e477f002ce91ba43eb15a75589"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[38856,38879],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p38856"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SelectionWindowList","paragraph_zero_based":38880},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameter that determines the end of the selection window in the resource selection for a TB with respect to priority indicated in SCI. Value n1 corresponds to 1*2µ, value n5 corresponds to 5*2µ, and so on, where µ = 0,1,2,3 refers to SCS 15,30,60,120 kHz respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":38881},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-Thres-RSRP-List","paragraph_zero_based":38882},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates a list of 64 thresholds, and the threshold should be selected based on the priority in the decoded SCI and the priority in the SCI to be transmitted. A resource is excluded if it is indicated or reserved by a decoded SCI and PSSCH/PSCCH RSRP in the associated data resource is above a threshold.","paragraph_zero_based":38883},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38884},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-PowerControl field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38885},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MaxTransPower","paragraph_zero_based":38886},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the maximum value of the UE's sidelink transmission power on this resource pool when the sidelink transmission is performed only on this resource pool. The unit is dBm. If the sidelink transmission is PSFCH, and multiple resource pools are used, the maximum transmission power for PSFCH is configured as sum of fields sl-maxTransPower over multiple resource pools, as specified in TS 38.101-1 [15].","paragraph_zero_based":38887},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-Alpha-PSSCH-PSCCH","paragraph_zero_based":38888},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates alpha value for sidelink pathloss based power control for PSCCH/PSSCH when sl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH is configured. When the field is absent the UE applies the value 1. ","paragraph_zero_based":38889},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH","paragraph_zero_based":38890},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates P0 value for sidelink pathloss based power control for PSCCH/PSSCH. If not configured, sidelink pathloss based power control is disabled for PSCCH/PSSCH. When sl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH-r17 is configured, the UE ignores sl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH-r16.","paragraph_zero_based":38891},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dl-Alpha-PSSCH-PSCCH","paragraph_zero_based":38892},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates alpha value for downlink pathloss based power control for PSCCH/PSSCH when dl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH is configured. When the field is absent the UE applies the value 1. ","paragraph_zero_based":38893},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH","paragraph_zero_based":38894},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates P0 value for downlink pathloss based power control for PSCCH/PSSCH. If not configured, downlink pathloss based power control is disabled for PSCCH/PSSCH. When dl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH-r17 is configured, the UE ignores dl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH-r16.","paragraph_zero_based":38895},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A Remote UE which is out of coverage, considers downlink pathloss based power control is disabled for PSCCH/PSSCH when dl-P0-PSSCH-PSCCH is configured.","paragraph_zero_based":38896},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dl-Alpha-PSFCH","paragraph_zero_based":38897},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates alpha value for downlink pathloss based power control for PSFCH when dl-P0-PSFCH is configured. When the field is absent the UE applies the value 1. For resource pools configured with PSFCH resources overlapping in time, this field is either not configured in any of the resource pools or configured with the same value for all the resource pools.","paragraph_zero_based":38898},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dl-P0-PSFCH","paragraph_zero_based":38899},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates P0 value for downlink pathloss based power control for PSFCH. If not configured, downlink pathloss based power control is disabled for PSFCH. When dl-P0-PSFCH-r17 is configured, the UE ignores dl-P0-PSFCH-r16. For resource pools configured with PSFCH resources overlapping in time, this field is either not configured in any of the resource pools or configured with the same value for all the resource pools.","paragraph_zero_based":38900},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A Remote UE which is out of coverage, considers downlink pathloss based power control is disabled for PSFCH when dl-P0-PSFCH is configured.","paragraph_zero_based":38901},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38902},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-MinMaxMCS-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38903}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["bfa956b23c4d45719de9e9e5922e0479cec91c6499fa0e3c16a282ca37a7590e","27a0db4ddd1fc22f8862b780a986d27665e38b77941c75d08bccba8da6638edc","b8b0ba1b76302f26b2e73e75c4fa17d5aa63d3d9a474c5ca06ae18e5d165844b","4a2b0f40430326236a51f8dbe1728cf2ca35fc51e5f89f0f174a72d3be56839f","e1f65034c38e06ea4a213d21e5972b1abf624cd7332dfe09429f642e3e1accfc","58a99fd6d40235270da764162efdb94a4d6f2e9aa1af9125a3827fef2f129472","84b16ee19f12c67b123949554652e23e36ed8d728821ed9e3f334f59f3f3747b","e16abb958bbaeb97c5d350e5301e9adb7ae97ba138ebd0d2dff69045e7f34024","309c42a2525e199eef6777f3779637fb94a814f0fa5a693b2ac59c2e7f8158b1","ce432c5f1ec76467c6591591ddf3bc2984ee4ea9ab3c549062200eb0ac8e8d4d","59d71a765cc63a48488e89af44b7be2513ae3f6d5dc47066a273b466c884c2c6","e13f833b05c24c291c1f822fb633035fb983e1cfbe9ac140a89d81a37da19f5f","81a9e8ae84e411876c114c9bec7f42c3a23d4b62c8bc343a71daf27e5bc2124a","d3a74dc707068bc9c2199d1ce9cdb2d3522048521cfedb595a22cfb99b66e3ef","c9a94aa2029a1b082d3e06c0dccc73c953f260fef8d6b9e48829652e56e6166b","81bab4d5f644b53657e95ea98877de0091db2f458e799bbdde3b578a75aec614","ffccb05ff8acd5a74bc7ba05eb733fd5bcf180de2bdffa209a551aacd5b8f08f","10f1152367de2a60a22ff62a145c83c05e41ab97287022e3ca92768b14c0db27","adc6a040b4132c706edc5c55bfbdc403dc1d9121c10115700b728fb844bb001e","4f251d41f71c81743e87155f03c7a0dbe98089a321fdbdce450d224f8780b714","05781c1123a1911c30b41e9e40f43c2a1b8f433a693cc30bdceb6d07f1df49d4","c926d5951729c02f3868043c45b2c86a08bc5b26ad6f5ccf292a4d197ab88fc4","0a4b51995e295dbc04e7ab52d76bef08c6e568bff066c4211ea17b1328ce778f","cb6d2a9d4539c60091bc9902d451fd586ba596b17a573078e01c13c507baa0c1"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[38880,38903],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p38880"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MaxMCS-PSSCH","paragraph_zero_based":38904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the maximum MCS value when using the associated MCS table. If no MCS is configured, UE autonomously selects MCS from the full range of values.","paragraph_zero_based":38905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MinMCS-PSSCH","paragraph_zero_based":38906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the minimum MCS value when using the associated MCS table. If no MCS is configured, UE autonomously selects MCS from the full range of values.","paragraph_zero_based":38907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-RLC-BearerConfig","paragraph_zero_based":38909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-RLC-BearerConfig specifies the SL RLC bearer configuration information for NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":38910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-RLC-BearerConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":38911},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":38912},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-RLC-BEARERCONFIG-START","paragraph_zero_based":38913},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38914},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-RLC-BearerConfig-r16 ::=                   SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":38915},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-RLC-BearerConfigIndex-r16                  SL-RLC-BearerConfigIndex-r16,","paragraph_zero_based":38916},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-ServedRadioBearer-r16                      SLRB-Uu-ConfigIndex-r16                          OPTIONAL,   -- Cond LCH-SetupOnly","paragraph_zero_based":38917},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-RLC-Config-r16                             SL-RLC-Config-r16                                OPTIONAL,   -- Cond LCH-Setup","paragraph_zero_based":38918},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfig-r16               SL-LogicalChannelConfig-r16                      OPTIONAL,   -- Cond LCH-Setup","paragraph_zero_based":38919},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":38920},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":38921},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38922},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-RLC-BEARERCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":38923},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":38924},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38925},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-RLC-BearerConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38926},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfig","paragraph_zero_based":38927}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["335c4240f2ae6238e8fc0b1908e21b34cd361efdd1a4a5fef8ab1aeb92919bad","6f4efa8b43683247d8e3ed9f7f5f2f4f74a86e9cc78b9635af5d18044521fd3d","3148dcb20b9e9903782f08ce3d7360321c34fde6e82f943dbd35f573bb12c575","b1e355cc969af77161023eb61e53a099195193a8a72ba97d88f1325ee8ff06cb","08e0d65039ae8b205545230fcfcf47e1b7af1c807ec112a8347e09034b94c052","5f58f64a4a1c663ea78d7691c92ddd63eb596af0e0a748a1fb1af916ce09d0d0","124b4ab9e1d7858a5819643dacd24eced02a2f981e32e2abf367407d1a2c4bde","4ad8d146cf72dfff25c480516142dcbb5942750d93e0e26eebb7cfa6ffc307fe","e628bc2df53fcf43894a7eb6ff3da96ea8b7efc69b44d896777f047364b4677a","c090e0de9e2f8517fba1dd895f06a8dd6128e8023952a57c8904e04e792cc023","5fe693068d111f76ef420bc033133afe59d981d2de899782cb4de14d3556c373","a0f6f48ff41bd959394ded5d0fb19d715e453876457abd3c1eebb0891a75132f","f35a6e96b29278d12cb619dbe8a4e6769ee6651bd0c4d3c2840a1ec6c3988947","fac3d713890b9e61c038dac2afa863b5c3bfb049b8a0eff919c2fe7b7cbebe1b","d9eeb47bd1821ca132048646903c1319ae1f7d21e912785de3331a0c2d3c7b94","f17cc3edab2af1a4e207cd202302c8173cf77fc4cbebf79bf732c01d59ad4881","03392d1bafbdd8904091d59275dd313a20b286b6443273718c2b529f9cd783d6","3a5d2ba015a30c2590528d0df51bc3e084fe42653766d107452ea074b16c3759","8918fe40c1736df80407c264319b4f7c4c5c48b916af645e820f1cdc9482bf07","a2e10122b683f5c0d878683ae8c947ab0fff6407ab50c424d37b1162363624ca","2cd28eb91e15fb9abc627049debc74764b43cac7f459b00c1abcd664a2521db2","a8f790ee572702d69469b13b3d315099b087a2def616010b56ca0aa4da0462d3","f1e5774762fc2196ba1fcec9946b10bdf3dac6c84cae891e5255fd3b61da164b","7bee24319e13cd82e0cafb8fc0f78bb228f31462e344e9cc369a0fe20e9cc15e"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[38904,38927],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p38904"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is used to configure MAC SL logical channel parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":38928},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-RLC-BearerConfigIndex","paragraph_zero_based":38929},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The index of the RLC bearer configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":38930},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-RLC-Config","paragraph_zero_based":38931},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Determines the RLC mode (UM, AM) and provides corresponding parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":38932},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-ServedRadioBearer","paragraph_zero_based":38933},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Associates the sidelink RLC Bearer with a sidelink DRB. It indicates the index of SL radio bearer configuration, which is corresponding to the RLC bearer configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":38934},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38935},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":38936},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":38937},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"LCH-Setup","paragraph_zero_based":38938},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present upon creation of a new sidelink logical channel via the dedicated signalling and in case of sidelink DRB configuration via system information and pre-configuration; otherwise the field is optionally present, Need M.","paragraph_zero_based":38939},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"LCH-SetupOnly","paragraph_zero_based":38940},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is mandatory present upon creation of a new sidelink logical channel via the dedicated signalling and in case of sidelink DRB configuration via system information and pre-configuration. Otherwise, it is absent, Need M.","paragraph_zero_ba