{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Determines the RLC mode (UM, AM) and provides corresponding parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":38976},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PacketDelayBudget","paragraph_zero_based":38977},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the Packet Delay Budget for a PC5 Relay RLC channel. Upper bound value for the delay that a packet may experience expressed in unit of 0.5ms.","paragraph_zero_based":38978},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38979},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-RLC-ChannelID","paragraph_zero_based":38980},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-RLC-ChannelID is used to identify a PC5 Relay RLC channel in the link between L2 U2N Relay UE and L2 U2N Remote UE.","paragraph_zero_based":38981},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-RLC-ChannelID information element","paragraph_zero_based":38982},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":38983},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-RLC-CHANNELID-START","paragraph_zero_based":38984},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38985},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-RLC-ChannelID-r17 ::=    INTEGER (1..maxSL-LCID-r16)","paragraph_zero_based":38986},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38987},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-RLC-CHANNELID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":38988},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":38989},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38990},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-RLC-Config","paragraph_zero_based":38991},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-RLC-Config is used to specify the RLC configuration of sidelink DRB. RLC AM configuration is only applicable to the unicast NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":38