{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If configured, the synchronization configuration is used for SLSS transmission/reception when the UE is synchronized to GNSS. If not configured, the synchronization configuration is used for SLSS transmission/reception when the UE is synchronized to eNB/gNB.","paragraph_zero_based":39240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SyncRefMinHyst","paragraph_zero_based":39241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Hysteresis when evaluating a SyncRef UE using absolute comparison.","paragraph_zero_based":39242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SyncRefDiffHyst","paragraph_zero_based":39243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Hysteresis when evaluating a SyncRef UE using relative comparison.","paragraph_zero_based":39244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-NumSSB-WithinPeriod","paragraph_zero_based":39245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of sidelink SSB transmissions within one sidelink SSB period. The applicable values are related to the subcarrier spacing and frequency as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":39246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1, SCS = 15 kHz: 1","paragraph_zero_based":39247},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1, SCS = 30 kHz: 1, 2","paragraph_zero_based":39248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1, SCS = 60 kHz: 1, 2, 4","paragraph_zero_based":39249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2, SCS = 60 kHz: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32","paragraph_zero_based":39250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2, SCS = 120 kHz: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64","paragraph_zero_based":39251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TimeOffsetSSB","paragraph_zero_based":39252},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the slot offset from the start of sidelink SSB period to the first sidelink SSB.","paragraph_zero_based":39253},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TimeInterval","paragraph_zero_based":39254},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the slot interval between neighboring sidelink SSBs. This value is applicable when there are more than one sidelink SSBs within one sidelink SSB period.","paragraph_zero_based":39255},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SSID","paragraph_zero_based":39256},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the ID of sidelink synchronization signal associated with different synchronization priorities.","paragraph_zero_based":39257},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"syncInfoReserved","paragraph_zero_based":39258},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reserved for future use.","paragraph_zero_based":39259},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"syncTxThreshIC, syncTxThreshOoC","paragraph_zero_based":39260},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the thresholds used while in coverage and out of coverage, respectively. Value 0 corresponds to -infinity, value 1 to -115 dBm, value 2 to -110 dBm, and so on (i.e. in steps of 5 dBm) until value 12, which corresponds to -60 dBm, while value 13 corresponds to +infinity.","paragraph_zero_based":39261},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39262},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-Thres-RSRP-List","paragraph_zero_based":39263}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["3dd59218c9d56e5e5960af8bf7499980309a477d6df8f25848483d4260508243","082e1c81194c703b975c880ab3dbd259b17db4b1e6325bbd8078297204ea1eb8","125dc375b8a0c513a3af017b2673f7bb4616ccc6c44df2d223dffd96c505791d","9b204f08dfbd7315790ae9ec32b2c8d32cfa11e47c1f564fbc3a1728a58702de","50a3f18d57b989b3a8a83f10fed42bf645e31182050603698b3a7d6528d9a235","5adc543096d809283dc05887b1753bb1651083166384db9ad2783a8b88a1c527","d5c1b40b7190db585205c247ad5646723dca90d06af3ee8a60dd5d7159becb96","df5d681cc7ef2983c92c994826af8bbcfaf23ce425a837b039112d5ecb362895","25e3574950cdbafd38f20762b19f199d10c72484163d8b3ccb58f7b16d3ec438","b0c88a78ead7d8604560247b88f9d65a3c0a9f97860f0d34b827af87056a8359","55711647d8a5c98bd94c6353055b1e439a01c515dfaecbbe2d881a853d265f97","3b134aefc88ee99a4be5148d5f408d234faab9fdf933c83ef04bf6140348cb6c","d7ab29e741ffa09e5de480262ecc44e40dbdcad3676842b7f29f0f7e94ec70af","165d40ea43c2a444aeeac2550dd110d3ff44a88b3d8baa79995abd9a60f7c20e","1768305e3a188d7a21d2a1d719388d3f6a86cd6b58696e078d58818b03bf24af","efd6c75c62d9248b604202729e51567c05fd01c740d7cfc23c96d1ec838a1179","3dc30ff4d53f3415cf20503916e987d767dca2aa45e0ac3f09a8f90e64a6f526","097b92aca353a68d47ea702b76426f10c01844e1ae19531414003cebe9646fb4","600aac50227fb687b67db782de5317236301a4dfb9ed532707062f5888ad570c","364533ef80a954e43831b64a0c99b6f09a1ea3e15a2b1ab81bcf941d18001e21","a4d8534ffea415c065c568a41d072e36297d13a440acb5e030db00921f318883","783b0fb376194c2ffae6aa96759bd326f65fdc138fffc933fe5024773ae0ae22","4eee6eabe72cd55185a163c4077689656e625ba0816dd5f6fc345491fc789593","f856684e48823728b5552bbffc6e1a86a92990873a68c246a2c3291b3de2a416"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[39240,39263],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p39240"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IE SL-Thres-RSRP-List indicates a threshold used for sensing based UE autonomous resource selection (see TS 38.215 [9]). A resource is excluded if it is indicated or reserved by a decoded SCI and PSSCH/PSCCH RSRP in the associated data resource is above the threshold defined by IE SL-Thres-RSRP-List. Value 0 corresponds to minus infinity dBm, value 1 corresponds to -128dBm, value 2 corresponds to -126dBm, value n corresponds to (-128 + (n-1)*2) dBm and so on, value 66 corresponds to infinity dBm.","paragraph_zero_based":39264},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-Thres-RSRP-List information element","paragraph_zero_based":39265},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":39266},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-THRES-RSRP-LIST-START","paragraph_zero_based":39267},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39268},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-Thres-RSRP-List-r16 ::=    SEQUENCE (SIZE (64)) OF SL-Thres-RSRP-r16","paragraph_zero_based":39269},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39270},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-Thres-RSRP-r16 ::=         INTEGER (0..66)","paragraph_zero_based":39271},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-THRES-RSRP-LIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-TxPower","paragraph_zero_based":39276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-TxPower is used to limit the UE's sidelink transmission power on a carrier frequency. The unit is dBm. Value minusinfinity corresponds to –infinity.","paragraph_zero_based":39277},{"literal_t