{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ul-PrioritizationThres-r16                   INTEGER (1..16)                                             OPTIONAL,    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":39312},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-PrioritizationThres-r16                   INTEGER (1..8)                                              OPTIONAL,    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":39313},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":39314},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":39315},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39316},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-UE-SELECTEDCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39317},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39318},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39319},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-UE-SelectedConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":39320},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PrioritizationThres","paragraph_zero_based":39321},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the SL priority threshold, which is used to determine whether SL TX is prioritized over UL TX, as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Network does not configure the sl-PrioritizationThres and the ul-PrioritizationThres to the UE separately.","paragraph_zero_based":39322},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-ProbResourceKeep","paragraph_zero_based":39323},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the probability with which the UE keeps the current resource when the resource reselection counter reaches zero for sensing based UE autonomous resource selection (see TS 38.321 [3]).","paragraph_zero_based":39324},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PSSCH-TxConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":39325},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates PSSCH TX parameters such as MCS, sub-channel number, retransmission number, associated to different UE absolute speeds and different synchronization reference types for UE autonomous resource selection.","paragraph_zero_based":39326},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-ReselectAfter","paragraph_zero_based":39327},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of consecutive skipped transmissions before triggering resource reselection for sidelink communication (see TS 38.321 [3]).","paragraph_zero_based":39328},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ul-PrioritizationThres","paragraph_zero_based":39329},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the UL priority threshold, which is used to determine whether SL TX is prioritized over UL TX, as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Network does not configure the sl-PrioritizationThres and the ul-PrioritizationThres to the UE separately.","paragraph_zero_based":39330},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39331},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-ZoneConfig","paragraph_zero_based":39332},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-ZoneConfig is used to configure the zone ID related parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":39333},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-ZoneConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":39334},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":39335}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["22e943b02f54438e042207be425a4a5f9001232b1e471007cc1458e98c6075db","3e2a2c13f3b6a6b1de6d8170d0fa53589c2e265cb0ed5adfc14d4b3150a440d5","32ad3df4cbef61a7fb9c596aa64b8559325a31074ad6f3f9587bc7b745ae6335","4661c97e872bb2ced13383fba93c085bdf8b6fe5488e9907582bf484e7bcd70c","595f045dd871628e3b696a7e2c9f1a