{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"G-RNTI used to scramble the scheduling and transmission of MTCH.","paragraph_zero_based":39576},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"headerCompression","paragraph_zero_based":39577},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If rohc is configured, the UE shall apply the configured ROHC profile(s) in downlink.","paragraph_zero_based":39578},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mbs-SessionId","paragraph_zero_based":39579},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates an identifier of the MBS session provided by the MTCH.","paragraph_zero_based":39580},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mrb-listBroadcast","paragraph_zero_based":39581},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of broadcast MRBs to which the associated broadcast MBS session is mapped to.","paragraph_zero_based":39582},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mtch-neighbourCell","paragraph_zero_based":39583},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates neighbour cells which provide this service on MTCH. The first bit is set to 1 if the service is provided on MTCH in the first cell in mbs-NeighbourCellList, otherwise it is set to 0. The second bit is set to 1 if the service is provided on MTCH in the second cell in mbs-NeighbourCellList, and so on. If the service is not available in any neighbouring cell and mbs-NeighbourCellList is signalled, the network sets all bits in this field to 0. The field is absent when mbs-NeighbourCellList is absent or an empty mbs-NeighbourCellList is signalled. If this field is absent when mbs-NeighbourCellList is absent or a non-empty mbs-NeighbourCellList is signalled, the related service may or may not be available in any neighbouring cell, i.e. the UE cannot determine the presence or absence of an MBS service in neighbouring cells based on the absence of this field. If this field is absent and an empty mbs-NeighbourCellList is signalled, then the UE shall assume that MBS broadcast services signalled in mbs-SessionInfoList in the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message are not provided in any neighbour cell.","paragraph_zero_based":39584},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mtch-schedulingInfo","paragraph_zero_based":39585},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the index of DRX configuration entry in drx-ConfigPTM-List that is used for scheduling the MTCH. The value 0 corresponds to the first entry in drx-ConfigPTM-List, the value 1 corresponds to the second entry in drx-ConfigPTM-List and so on. In case mtch-schedulingInfo is absent for a G-RNTI (i.e. no PTM DRX), the UE shall monitor for PDCCH scrambled with G-RNTI in any slot according to the search space configured for MTCH [see TS 38.213 [13], clause 10.1].","paragraph_zero_based":39586},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mtch-SSB-MappingWindowIndex","paragraph_zero_based":39587},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the index of MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowCycleOffset configuration entry in MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList. The value 0 corresponds to the first entry in MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList, the value 1 corresponds to the second entry in MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList and so on. This field is set to the same value for all MBS sessions mapped to the same G-RNTI.","paragraph_zero_based":39588},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdcp-SN-SizeDL","paragraph_zero_based":39589},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates that PDCP sequence number size of 12 bits is used, as specified in TS 38.323 [5]. When the field is absent the UE applies the value as specified in 9.1.1.7.","paragraph_zero_based":39590},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdschConfigIndex","paragraph_zero_based":39591},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the index of PDSCH configuration entry in pdschConfigList for MTCH. Value 0 corresponds to the first entry in pdschConfigList, the value 1 corresponds to the second entry in pdschConfigList and so on. When the field is absent the UE applies the first entry in pdschConfigList for MTCH.","paragraph_zero_based":39592},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sn-FieldLength","paragraph_zero_based":39593},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates that the RLC SN field size of 6 bits is used, see TS 38.322 [4]. When the field is absent the UE applies the value as specified in 9.1.1.7.","paragraph_zero_based":39594},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"t-Reassembly","paragraph_zero_based":39595},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Timer for reassembly in TS 38.322 [4], in milliseconds. Value ms0 means 0 ms, value ms5 means 5 ms and so on. When the field is absent the UE applies the value in specified in 9.1.1.7.","paragraph_zero_based":39596},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"t-Reordering","paragraph_zero_based":39597},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in ms of t-Reordering specified in TS 38.323 [5]. Value ms1 corresponds to 1 ms, value ms10 corresponds to 10 ms, and so on.  When the field is absent the UE applies the value as specified in 9.1.1.7.","paragraph_zero_based":39598},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39599}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f3a3e32105463205e94eb9b36903dd3d009572f572c6630eed62a353fec75ac9","e3d3ce2bb3b57c4b428471b4c5372d67543dead2ab2043bb71225e7c23e6f4ad","87dfb48d58db2fe9d1f181c514fcd622d1866f0c375305922d3bb8980b4dc67d","590391058588ea5e620feef17f2aa25faf427b8f484c56ecb0c0cca949dfdbd3","12b9057e671c605bef032c553b5695d93181b4cddb80268e3144872f1f2dadcb","6c2b4eba8096988b9065d20facaa3fd1b1eafe5195fb4b69a72186b543f3665e","72ba68431a6e579620430d494db7cbf05ddc9ece48c796fea34dd1c608c5e059","e96b5932de25cb43b92a10e656f994cf1244ce239e4b84806bdc69ce7164750a","d114111deeb3aeaafddbff82b0c6f8233420fd64eb3c2ff92c62182a1cc16b57","dedb52a0b26c8301a23a010f316a5f8a85cbea31d810cf3f479828e37cffe7a4","97af68891cb49cddd65e95162ee0b84d9a4da4424857aa30cf33c448185c1328","a37fa38ffca712850b630d80cca817719eca4111f41f32fc52d7805d5f979053","2adfdf10a351abb873a8a0a24f76c32d34853e1c5ab7a31369010708ef5adfa5","d0bf073d9b54d99a9ec7bc82db0568f352ff7219c5227192213fa8b1804416ea","684b461886e4d47802273579b724d9578153a554b8d33f171af1ec464567ec35","ea7de0806adc904eb0c4633f9f6af97130f3a5d4b807f418c88599a4635bf7d2","b0860286857632291c2055ffd83492a55092362d1a9a17d1c4261ed72d5a09a4","572ee0bc3d2809f7fa83c83fa0ae5d66673326ee55aee57e5e4b050f9a9063f6","6a0857a86c2a97cd04f438cd88a1d61069919256dfd637974cb19e74fc7ee9a0","d12c41e5d663b38c6f18d5fcb761258b2eda3fa95d3ad4ebba4bc8b0104ddae1","91a63939ab7c62d6fb4f9201d032d6898ff1f5f09dfa56673bc9ac27732775c1","8a78fb344bf1f724e92c3a8f7f0bcf3fc1d9e8458d35b93a79786742918a76eb","052a06d3c8c2dc74e02de136761df21866b8509973394ac1b14a761515ef7c06","e4ca7fef0b0c9c87ff75b12dc63b140d230e96d8af6dfc11d10945463b2ddb09"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[39576,39599],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p39576"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":39600},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":39601},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-Mapping","paragraph_zero_based":39602},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if the number of actual transmitted SSBs determined according to ssb-PositionsInBurst in SIB1 is more than 1, and searchspaceMTCH is not set to zero (including the case where searchSpaceMTCH is absent and searchSpaceMCCH is not set to zero). Otherwise, it is absent, Need R.","paragraph_zero_based":39603},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39604},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList","paragraph_zero_based":39605},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList is used to configure MTCH PDCCH ocassions to SSB mapping window related periodic and offset parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":39606},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList information element","paragraph_zero_based":39607},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":39608},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MTCH-SSB-MAPPINGWINDOWLIST-START","paragraph_zero_based":39609},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39610},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList-r17 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofMTCH-SSB-MappingWindow-r17)) OF MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowCycleOffset-r17","paragraph_zero_based":39611},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39612},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowCycleOffset-r17 ::= CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":39613},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms10                                      INTEGER(0..9),","paragraph_zero_based":39614},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms20                                      INTEGER(0..19),","paragraph_zero_based":39615},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms32                                      INTEGER(0..31),","paragraph_zero_based":39616},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms64                                      INTEGER(0..63),","paragraph_zero_based":39617},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms128                                     INTEGER(0..127),","paragraph_zero_based":39618},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms256                                     INTEGER(0..255)","paragraph_zero_based":39619},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":39620},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39621},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MTCH-SSB-MAPPINGWINDOWLIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39622},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39623}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["5d8f8a13a0cabf6a849997edafc871fd02783a299a49809cb1a7ca2bbbf08400","f462d70c6ff7acdbf57490e4cff6fede295a540bc830d5d3e72257c686d0b943","9b2ec942d15b522ba71e92cb4c326e8ac1f40d8f06351c18fc21546fdc78f92e","5753c8412f7b2c1864a1f8091a986ca49f5ca5e96f07c7b7d5c01aa30de4bedd","f1b20d49e2072060d2f8ed86d3e97d51c368989b144cb4aceabcd72b1dcb3e3f","b4c7fdd8154774ed5a90b5249a334b0a1154db5de3c3134f68ea18882070217e","84ace2c41d60f1f6c8c7ba0770cb22606be068abd658228db881720b7c532972","dc859e34dd68c1927e08bab9d01782a9726aaabd6b5d9790cc49b8271dfd9f3b","4070664bc0e88ddef3ab0f566eb78d666308d69e111394b7edf65aaccae1fd3c","c89572e6a271020dc7bc80cce3b5fc14f3a29c9ea17abcecbf78540762176877","6bf05a38816a305864c329291f4aebfe176a97f310d90741abdac83a51fcc5a1","156f49e91279c6f06e2116de15e144e248fe8e37c7c52b23ea293d57c1e98342","a37d079b23c741c5d98befd954d65747c5bbadfd4eaeff9c874f2c293fc12396","313e073c366d369175303cd9271605956bcdb73eba3c85632ea6dbfc0447704d","8b8cf96ed7cf8d80833d69eb8338de84f9817f9b8b8ba9cda67cd802e71f3d07","3ed52978cd7221398524c30f070499e1283794a8ab23e6147d7b7ddac815c41c","a037fccdf02b4ada4dce0ca652953540353f55a0fa0e91abd72a634a0fe8b241","02bd8b7bc55b693d702ab24d392f5f856c976c625c8fcfcc6a54d683bd4012aa","8244624985918eb3e166dad567e3ee7a6c82f2ee6d5bdf2dd816c56a150c55ff","5f802dc9e6cace9b7550b6522730ea67501df5fcd9fbf4f70e47d0f42f5146a2","313b73e5a53c250b363c2a7f6fddfd2c464b58ae739f36bbcb0b16242bbb592a","6319b5e343b51d8bbf670806732a12977853271046c5bde7550a1cdeae311194","61cd47f8a5c670a9a24f89d74d81ead0f8928822d6bf98d66313e1040bd1bc6f","25d855e4d1c8cb18da1072c76d1b61f7577b0aa925369e2e116a6a747ef8a783"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[39600,39623],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p39600"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39624},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":39625},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowCycleOffset","paragraph_zero_based":39626},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the cycle and offset for MTCH PDCCH ocassions to SSB mapping. Values in unit of ms. ms10 corresponds to cycle of 10 ms with corresponding offset between 0 and 9 ms, value ms20 corresponds to cycle of 20 ms with corresponding offset between 0 and 19 ms, and so on. The mapping window starts at a subframe in a SFN where [(SFN number × 10) + subframe number] modulo (cycle) = offset.","paragraph_zero_based":39627},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDCCH monitoring occasions for MTCH in a mapping window which are not overlapping with UL symbols (determined according to tdd-UL-DL-ConfigurationCommon) are sequentially numbered starting from 1 in the maping window. The [x×N+K]th PDCCH monitoring occasion for MTCH in this mapping window corresponds to the Kth transmitted SSB, where x = 0, 1, ...X-1, K = 1, 2, …N, N is the number of actual transmitted SSBs determined according to ssb-PositionsInBurst in SIB1 and X is equal to CEIL(number of PDCCH monitoring occasions in MTCH to SSB mapping transmission window/N). The actual transmitted SSBs are sequentially numbered from one in ascending order of their SSB indexes.","paragraph_zero_based":39628},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39629},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast","paragraph_zero_based":39630},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast is used to configure parameters for acquiring the PDSCH for MCCH and MTCH.","paragraph_zero_based":39631},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast information element","paragraph_zero_based":39632},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":39633},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PDSCH-CONFIGBROADCAST-START","paragraph_zero_based":39634},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39635},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast-r17 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":39636},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    pdschConfigList-r17                    SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofPDSCH-ConfigPTM-r17) ) OF PDSCH-ConfigPTM-r17,","paragraph_zero_based":39637},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    pdsch-TimeDomainAllocationList-r17     PDSCH-TimeDomainResourceAllocationList-r16                          OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":39638},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    rateMatchPatternToAddModList-r17       SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofRateMatchPatterns)) OF RateMatchPattern   OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":39639},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    lte-CRS-ToMatchAround-r17              RateMatchPatternLTE-CRS                                             OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":39640},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    mcs-Table-r17                          ENUMERATED {qam256, qam64LowSE}                                     OPTIONAL,   -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":39641},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    xOverhead-r17                          ENUMERATED {xOh6, xOh12, xOh18}                                     OPTIONAL    -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":39642},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":39643},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39644},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigPTM-r17 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":39645},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    dataScramblingIdentityPDSCH-r17        INTEGER (0..1023)         OPTIONAL,   -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":39646},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    dmrs-ScramblingID0-r17                 INTEGER (0..65535)        OPTIONAL,   -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":39647}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0d7d43bb2a33bfee866325ec3a3652adabaee8d0d2f11b9e357b75753e12106e","89a1226d8414b93c4d0078bcd4138fb48ed3c90670e23d0027e9f1191bd98d40","e4e2121819b09a1ce525327b9bc228ada9f5f849dbeb00ce1eafe65cc947cac4","770737b7ab3a7d574772938a21049872668183f9400423ffde0cef2bd7f41640","5bcc931f36e3f141743eda1aa83b73bc4bbc8e8f383d2a3ed8698433d22a0406","3317ecc3219092a08e4abd310affcdc46cef4c6c5fdc64e98a372f22c03fd95f","32d1aaa9307378e6d7e1366a864769229e12233d53388918172ed77d950b3d52","cc21b85b3242ad9c61ad2e0632be6773b5fa8bf23a2fb56742fbd266f40471f0","a01af85b167df1f9d45b8eecdefd7b4166c0b3239b1315d73f244e2a94c8cfc6","62ec43186741811cc5bedd5b094ab3998772c7721ab394d0caa73e6d7ba0dc90","8cbb196dc165a44ce37681fadea8cd717723b102cc6be179addbbaee25dafb7d","2d2866ee9b207f00565fd8a541c28c5d24ece3d3fa97d444b4b26f95632e05a1","6dca65c0e9dbf79f523a9809425e34b9b377b127c93fc3b20b0954801325cd51","69553e25005be9b4eeeaba8b1f37a86e271596fa93bfd841fe946372594b88fc","203f989c6594786c623990c169628f320da44b34709814a6756da9c3273a6a63","f0119ee174c44681e9b4458da30aa93dbbfbee72d2400afdd1063cb626ef2149","3171592cf690a65b413a7dab03e2cbe547894b922e0742acfccb2ad63afd8774","955637f1d7adc6178d0b1e654b2acf14496b2bcc73c3e0031c76644d30d5f450","bb5a9acbbc2a686f70ac2756312afb9fd154032f901136ac8826ddb66df86352","987a527587e1452bfd086afd8f3bf086baa123889f2ff565c15fdaf551724118","45be716e683eb0578a18f4c90e1eeaf61ad4fcb4032a098549561c66aea526ae","74aade262636afd4ea508bb620229dbf8f3ce3589ed511565af5ec4a5b9873cd","5f50f0c21adb5bf2e7d1bf52548a37876dc6930e23345ab966c2b60be7f404e1","4253c3a8f9650fe7060657c3480500e8619f1386d98426d6f28a14070b5b82a0"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[39624,39647],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p39624"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    pdsch-AggregationFactor-r17            ENUMERATED {n2, n4, n8}   OPTIONAL    -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":39648},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":39649},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39650},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PDSCH-CONFIGBROADCAST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39651},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39652},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39653},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":39654},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"lte-CRS-ToMatchAround","paragraph_zero_based":39655},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameters to determine an LTE CRS pattern that the UE shall rate match around.","paragraph_zero_based":39656},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdschConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":39657},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of PDSCH parameters which can be configured per G-RNTI. Only one entity is allowed to be configured if included in SIB20.","paragraph_zero_based":39658},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdsch-TimeDomainAllocationList","paragraph_zero_based":39659},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of time-domain configurations for timing of DL assignment to DL data.","paragraph_zero_based":39660},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field pdsch-TimeDomainAllocationList applies to DCI format 4_0 (see table 5.1.2.1.1-1 in TS 38.214 [19]). When the field is absent, the UE follows PDSCH time domain resource allocation determination rule as specified in TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.2.1.1.","paragraph_zero_based":39661},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rateMatchPatternToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":39662},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Resources patterns which the UE should rate match PDSCH around. The UE rate matches around the union of all resources indicated in the rate match patterns (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.4.1).","paragraph_zero_based":39663},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mcs-Table","paragraph_zero_based":39664},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates which MCS table the UE shall use for PDSCH. If the field is absent the UE applies the value 64QAM. The field mcs-Table applies to DCI format 4_0 with CRC scrambled by MCCH-RNTI/G-RNTI (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.3.1).","paragraph_zero_based":39665},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"xOverhead","paragraph_zero_based":39666},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Accounts for an overhead from CSI-RS, CORESET, etc. If the field is absent, the UE applies value xOh0 (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":39667},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39668},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigPTM field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":39669},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dataScramblingIdentityPDSCH","paragraph_zero_based":39670},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Identifier(s) used to initialize data scrambling (c_init) for PDSCH as specified in TS 38.211 [16], clause 7.3.1.1. When the field is absent the UE applies the value physCellId configured for this serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":39671}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["85426f104b347dc135eee599012a7bb970e5d1bbd1b36c7a165c856ce5d53dc5","678be4e5c6f8d8f8496e7cbbbe03b5952c2b74187d8fac1be92ab6141510b915","74f2ae6160d77fc23b46e34d19c5d85542345aad9ccd9f592b91abc8d7399356","b4745b09ff5cf39625fa63e6c2e3c391d96c96399ba5227c40adcef424