{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the sidelink cause for the sidelink RLF (value rlf), sidelink AS configuration failure (value configFailure) and the rejection of sidelink DRX configuration (value drxReject-v1710) for the associated destination for unicast.","paragraph_zero_based":11712},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":11713},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-RxDRX-Report field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":11714},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-DRX-ConfigFromTx","paragraph_zero_based":11715},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the sidelink DRX configuration received from the peer UE for NR sidelink unicast communication.","paragraph_zero_based":11716},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":11717},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-RxInterestedGC-BC-Dest field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":11718},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-RxInterestedQoS-InfoList","paragraph_zero_based":11719},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the QoS profile for which UE reports its interested service to which SL DRX is applied to the network, for NR sidelink groupcast or broadcast reception.","paragraph_zero_based":11720},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":11721},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-TxResourceReqDisc field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":11722},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CastTypeDisc","paragraph_zero_based":11723},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the cast type for the NR sidelink discovery messages. Only value broadcast can be set in this release.","paragraph_zero_based":11724},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-DestinationIdentityDisc","paragraph_zero_based":11725},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is used to indicate the destination L2 ID for which the TX resource request and allocation from the network are concerned for relay discovery and non-relay discovery.","paragraph_zero_based":11726},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SourceIdentityRelayUE","paragraph_zero_based":11727},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is used to indicate the source L2 ID of relay-related discovery transmission by L2 U2N Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":11728},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TxInterestedFreqListDisc","paragraph_zero_based":11729},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Each entry of this field indicates the index of frequency on which the UE is interested to transmit NR sidelink discovery. The value 1 corresponds to the frequency of first entry in sl-FreqInfoList broadcast in SIB12, the value 2 corresponds to the frequency of second entry in sl-FreqInfoList broadcast in SIB12 and so on. In this release, only value 1 can be included in the interested frequency list. In this release, only one entry can be included in the list.","paragraph_zero_based":11730},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":11731},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-TxResourceReqCommRelayInfo field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":11732},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-RelayDRXConfig","paragraph_zero_based":11733},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is used to indicate the applied sidelink DRX configuration for the relay related communication.","paragraph_zero_based":11734},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-DestinationIdentityL2U2N","paragraph_zero_based":11735}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e3250e6c0cd3fb3aba61a07b59149d950b97cf801261256eaaffa40eb003836b","original_member_sha256":"43effeec8825b995fac78441fed0808abcec562c85ad3256681daf06dadbee2c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b43d30fc93731ee344709d3cf4947e3bcbd931823c1a436895623bebe879f8e5","6b544d4457ae646811837bb58964f350c7d41885ce95