{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Entry index in the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19896},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"physicalCellIdRange","paragraph_zero_based":19897},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Physical cell identity or a range of physical cell identities.","paragraph_zero_based":19898},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":19899},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRAN-Cell field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":19900},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"physicalCellId","paragraph_zero_based":19901},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Physical cell identity of a cell in the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19902},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellIndividualOffset","paragraph_zero_based":19903},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Cell individual offset applicable to a specific cell. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":19904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":19905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MeasObjectEUTRA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":19906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"allowedMeasBandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":19907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The maximum allowed measurement bandwidth on a carrier frequency as defined by the parameter Transmission Bandwidth Configuration \"NRB\" TS 36.104 [33].","paragraph_zero_based":19908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"associatedMeasGap","paragraph_zero_based":19909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the associated measurement gap for measuring this EUTRA frequency. If this field is absent, the associated meaurment gap is the gap configured via gapFR1 or gapUE.","paragraph_zero_based":19910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"carrierFreq","paragraph_zero_based":19911},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Identifies EUTRA carrier frequency for which this configuration is valid. Network does not configure more than one MeasObjectEUTRA for the same physical frequency, regardless of the E-ARFCN used to indicate this.","paragraph_zero_based":19912},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellsToAddModListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":19913},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to add/ modify in the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19914},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellsToRemoveListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":19915},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to remove from the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19916},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra-PresenceAntennaPort1","paragraph_zero_based":19917},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When set to true, the UE may assume that at least two cell-specific antenna ports are used in all neighbouring cells.","paragraph_zero_based":19918},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra-Q-OffsetRange","paragraph_zero_based":19919}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e3250e6c0cd3fb3aba61a07b59149d950b97cf801261256eaaffa40eb003836b","original_member_sha256":"43effeec8825b995fac78441fed0808abcec562c85ad3256681daf06dadbee2c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["537acd723dda655dba69d31544ed36ed89a336678bdaa200d6d104501f21898b","acbd4c74a81f5dc497ecc9276632073bf325eefdff4f5dc962eaae48cd76afc1","c0dde00a91d039c1022ff429d5479348adb3691078ee0387535193cbf781fd66","ce9d181f28f156456438a594fd1148bbc45e3a45a67c0dcde2b796c75764a5cf","9916d47db91469746855fe29e7b5de63ae9e95327a505ed19c5b08c827cc2044","029826a9c901edaa5400701efc6ab5aaa2a33f8999903c7c965529fcb953b107","27acfcb7dc262ba3b5d3dc5342bb8ea1daea2e784e889476f50ff69199e3304c","45e27cd4d9b1eaf3ab773e5a04c6995b3a62b654b29b037bc0f954e9ad166675","c911bf921a9a7d294bccd7d8a591c73a39ebe06763e0da56e6ba60f2b050cf72","664aafd49391a547b8515efbf30e55ac9a75eecaa8b95d181002d0