{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of subframes for PHR reporting as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Value sf10 corresponds to 10 subframes, value sf20 corresponds to 20 subframes, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":22992},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-ProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":22993},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of subframes for PHR reporting as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Value sf0 corresponds to 0 subframe, value sf10 corresponds to 10 subframes, value sf20 corresponds to 20 subframes, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":22994},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-Tx-PowerFactorChange","paragraph_zero_based":22995},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in dB for PHR reporting as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Value dB1 corresponds to 1 dB, dB3 corresponds to 3 dB and so on. The same value applies for each serving cell (although the associated functionality is performed independently for each cell).","paragraph_zero_based":22996},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-Type2OtherCell","paragraph_zero_based":22997},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If set to true, the UE shall report a PHR type 2 for the SpCell of the other MAC entity. See TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.4.6. Network sets this field to false if the UE is not configured with an E-UTRA MAC entity.","paragraph_zero_based":22998},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"twoPHRMode","paragraph_zero_based":22999},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates if the power headroom shall be reported as two PHRs (each PHR associated with a SRS resource set) is enabled or not.","paragraph_zero_based":23000},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":23001},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PhysCellId","paragraph_zero_based":23002},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The PhysCellId identifies the physical cell identity (PCI).","paragraph_zero_based":23003},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysCellId information element","paragraph_zero_based":23004},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":23005},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PHYSCELLID-START","paragraph_zero_based":23006},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":23007},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysCellId ::=                      INTEGER (0..1007)","paragraph_zero_based":23008},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":23009},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PHYSCELLID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":23010},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":23011},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":23012},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PhysicalCellGroupConfig","paragraph_zero_based":23013},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PhysicalCellGroupConfig is used to configure cell-group specific L1 parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":23014},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysicalCellGroupConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":23015}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e3250e6c0cd3fb3aba61a07b59149d950b97cf801261256eaaffa40eb003836b","original_member_sha256":"43effeec8825b995fac78441fed0808abcec562c85ad3256681daf06dadbee2c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["49203766a13c1c15b7878a15740ba1d05b5f2a316567d4a523baddb4faffa5f6","202bf7614c843ba3bb1f8168742dffb27f5961f82cba503df0a7b881ed218b78","0650180e111ee6a07afbfe75ee078433629f87ae707af470bbcefcb9d33b9029","81939ceab25ad21cee29a6228b802bccda6ad0dfdd396daefc026b9398062899","e4e3de00ba69fa2ead32aec97e4d6fb2758ce02a6f16f3960c297472bd0075fc","dbeed7fb933c3002e62afe9e5eefb307e33167933b60c2a32283e72eea820cfb","f5c98ac70b315624114007a42deddd584d2038c1fd7e3c0fefa9091c4093929a","059840705deda46b81412a6230a41f80fb6adef53a845728c2a5