{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        ra-Prioritization-r16                                RA-Prioritization,","paragraph_zero_based":24912},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        ra-PrioritizationForAI-r16                           BIT STRING (SIZE (2))","paragraph_zero_based":24913},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    }                                                                                                                   OPTIONAL, -- Cond InitialBWP-Only","paragraph_zero_based":24914},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ra-ContentionResolutionTimer-r16                     ENUMERATED {sf8, sf16, sf24, sf32, sf40, sf48, sf56, sf64}     OPTIONAL, -- Cond 2StepOnly","paragraph_zero_based":24915},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...,","paragraph_zero_based":24916},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":24917},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ra-PrioritizationForSlicingTwoStep-r17               RA-PrioritizationForSlicing-r17              OPTIONAL, -- Cond InitialBWP-Only","paragraph_zero_based":24918},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    featureCombinationPreamblesList-r17 SEQUENCE (SIZE(1..maxFeatureCombPreamblesPerRACHResource-r17)) OF FeatureCombinationPreambles-r17 OPTIONAL  -- Cond AdditionalRACH","paragraph_zero_based":24919},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":24920},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":24921},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24922},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GroupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA-r16 ::=                       SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":24923},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ra-MsgA-SizeGroupA                                   ENUMERATED {b56, b144, b208, b256, b282, b480, b640, b800,","paragraph_zero_based":24924},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                                     b1000, b72, spare6, spare5, spare4, spare3, spare2, spare1},","paragraph_zero_based":24925},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    messagePowerOffsetGroupB                             ENUMERATED {minusinfinity, dB0, dB5, dB8, dB10, dB12, dB15, dB18},","paragraph_zero_based":24926},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    numberOfRA-PreamblesGroupA                           INTEGER (1..64)","paragraph_zero_based":24927},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":24928},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24929},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RACH-CONFIGCOMMONTWOSTEPRA-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":24930},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":24931},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24932},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":24933},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"featureCombinationPreamblesList","paragraph_zero_based":24934},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Specifies a series of preamble partitions each associated to a combination of features and 2-step RA. The network does not configure this list to have more than 16 entries.","paragraph_zero_based":24935}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e3250e6c0cd3fb3aba61a07b59149d950b97cf801261256eaaffa40eb003836b","original_member_sha256":"43effeec8825b995fac78441fed0808abcec562c85ad3256681daf06dadbee2c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8b348e72f1d6791e3309ccf2f65ded74fc59651ec99bd359b4b2942d63f6b13f","f10bbc4c36984261fdd49a0ae7d74a3c8337eae2e1a6f769806ef4099450806c","91379d301335540131498f6c43eccfd4ed92baabfa4e31b103c50f9179a088d5","322430c9589077fcfff150a51a17d2c7b456e90521ea0eec785dcf0b3ce570bf","d7a7e46df88eabd6d3fa4872fb865aec39c24b98312fd80712f3fc83caee9d8d","9712f95c0a005ba1fde960805e5f50e03ba97e3ece6272ef4751861e2db49bc1","66e6549ed6326d340e82c5dcb49fc8c0f190576ea5cb6b3146684b5656339542","0f03de7b262285c0fe4e83d1541e60e247915aa1e61c1b8aaa518ba2694672b3","02c59d83b19d857875514ba2969e797ef9959517c8d35bf50e5f69f4a1b764a2","9975ae3d60e2f6d0b6b67ce2e7eff512a4e347cbfae91b423e3333a98b3719ca","65397c9cb1c43d31bb0b788af374c070cd676d0a358fab6de3915f32c6e98e60","844842d89875f9ab49327347afd2f36788c42879cf390eae355c29baedb167da","32effa5a413c4619aa608b73037888ce4a37336158a53bca4b3936365034f2cf","13fefc9029fe1fb0d94e228598070302bc1a5c5b7b486d22d9306791a5dcf9d2","7bc992a835e9fd47134634c3b483e1f6a5a76c20cc520927054de5ac389cfd9c","dd19cb338ba7f508e899dba53f4654459cfd43b6aa4871d1140aafe15769d6e5","4792cbce9efa73d3146d02fd95f4554459cbc96cad40d9a43c0512231aa9196e","2672702b691dfda5b9250c3d5dc19560084e7d5491b5d40a7be4d62cbe62850c","976977e069555436b9a77838b8220531049b8249544f4e88de1543b3d11486e5","81a149add750fbcdf4356a31cb2728ae5ab65c67f350f23c8a2aa788e94c5f4b","e1da9797d2edd53faca20673382d8f70c657f3e8af8be3821feee746a1b90c69","25c255c45b51cb5734ff24932baafe43f4399cef9e306cfdde121de93fc4497d","9670375b1fed9edaf111fc08a4ff7d43dd8906101171f2d92eb919b144b22daf","c04f42689b7a796994ea1473ba0286f2ddc926b6e621c6370b0820b55e345713"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[24912,24935],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx:p24912"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"groupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA","paragraph_zero_based":24936},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Preamble grouping for 2-step random access type. If the field is absent then there is only one preamble group configured and only one msgA PUSCH configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":24937},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-CB-PreamblesPerSSB-PerSharedRO","paragraph_zero_based":24938},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of contention-based preambles used for 2-step RA type from the non-CBRA 4-step type preambles associated with each SSB for RO shared with 4-step type RA. The number of preambles for 2-step RA type shall not exceed the number of preambles per SSB minus the number of contention-based preambles per SSB for 4-step type RA. The possible value range for this parameter needs to be aligned with value range for the configured SSBs per RACH occasion in ssb-perRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB in RACH-ConfigCommon. The field is only applicable for the case of shared ROs with 4-step type random access.","paragraph_zero_based":24939},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-PRACH-RootSequenceIndex","paragraph_zero_based":24940},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PRACH root sequence index. If the field is not configured in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA which is configured directly within a BWP (i.e., not within AdditionalRACH-Config), the UE applies the value in field prach-RootSequenceIndex in RACH-ConfigCommon in the configured BWP. If the field is absent in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA in AdditionalRACH-Config, the UE applies the corresponding value of prach-RootSequenceIndex in RACH-ConfigCommon in the same AdditionalRACH-Config. When both 2-step and 4-step type random access is configured, this field is only configured for the case of separate ROs between 2-step and 4-step type random access.","paragraph_zero_based":24941},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For FR2-2, only the following values are applicable depending on the used subcarrier spacing:","paragraph_zero_based":24942},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"120 kHz:  L=139, L=571, and L=1151","paragraph_zero_based":24943},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"480 kHz:  L=139, and L=571","paragraph_zero_based":24944},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"960 kHz:  L=139","paragraph_zero_based":24945},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-RestrictedSetConfig","paragraph_zero_based":24946},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration of an unrestricted set or one of two types of restricted sets for 2-step random access type preamble. If the field is not configured in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA which is configured directly within a BWP (i.e. not within AdditionalRACH-Config), the UE applies the value in field restrictedSetConfig in RACH-ConfigCommon in the configured BWP. If the field is absent in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA in AdditionalRACH-Config, the UE applies the value of restrictedSetConfig in RACH-ConfigCommon in the same AdditionalRACH-Config. When both 2-step and 4-step type random access is configured, this field is only configured for the case of separate ROs between 2-step and 4-step type random access.","paragraph_zero_based":24947},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-RSRP-Threshold","paragraph_zero_based":24948},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE selects 2-step random access type to perform random access based on this threshold (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.1). This field is only present if both 2-step and 4-step RA type are configured for the BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":24949},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-RSRP-ThresholdSSB","paragraph_zero_based":24950},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UE may select the SS block and corresponding PRACH resource for path-loss estimation and (re)transmission based on SS blocks that satisfy the threshold (see TS 38.213 [13]).","paragraph_zero_based":24951},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-SSB-PerRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB","paragraph_zero_based":24952},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The meaning of this field is twofold: the CHOICE conveys the information about the number of SSBs per RACH occasion. Value oneEight corresponds to one SSB associated with 8 RACH occasions, value oneFourth corresponds to one SSB associated with 4 RACH occasions, and so on. The ENUMERATED part indicates the number of Contention Based preambles per SSB. Value n4 corresponds to 4 Contention Based preambles per SSB, value n8 corresponds to 8 Contention Based preambles per SSB, and so on. The total number of CB preambles in a RACH occasion is given by CB-preambles-per-SSB * max(1, SSB-per-rach-occasion). If the field is not configured in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA which is configured directly within a BWP (i.e. not within AdditionalRACH-Config) and both 2-step and 4-step are configured for the BWP, the UE applies the value in the field ssb-perRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB in RACH-ConfigCommon. If the field is not configured in AdditionalRACH-Config and both 2-step and 4-step are configured in AdditionalRACH-Config, the UE applies the value in the field ssb-perRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB in RACH-ConfigCommon in the same AdditionalRACH-Config. The field is not present when RACH occasions are shared between 2-step and 4-step type random access in the BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":24953},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-SSB-SharedRO-MaskIndex","paragraph_zero_based":24954},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the subset of 4-step type ROs shared with 2-step random access type for each SSB. This field is configured when there is more than one RO per SSB. If the field is absent, and 4-step and 2-step has shared ROs, then all ROs are shared.","paragraph_zero_based":24955},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-SubcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":24956},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Subcarrier spacing of PRACH (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 5.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":24957},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Only the following values are applicable depending on the used frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":24958},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1:    15 or 30 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":24959}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e3250e6c0cd3fb3aba61a07b59149d950b97cf801261256eaaffa40eb003836b","original_member_sha256":"43effeec8825b995fac78441fed0808abcec562c85ad3256681daf06dadbee2c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["dc9ab50cd3a711fd2253e2e5a7537902201a683e80fd8110b11e9c93bcd65693","2f54cfdba291fb2216b9df1d98576fb4156ac6642e0239e8d86d354ee691eee2","08ab436deee337a09f0a2746047169ad332ab606e1fafe2dac3d0f43c543aa9b","77ab5812ffb088c1ba0a536f8e094027920716b184a1e5c4cb8dd1ed6e2bc466","9173ddefcf1a51b1775f5c139059125db54949a88121f2a411db38614ec05fb3","d308bb00f3556b765bf3a56d18dea1af3589851ccafdd3415ebae5a7525d9e25","52216743c7bb8fdf8b9c8fd348bdb9cebb585feba249cd48d16c9614d22ed3a2","7a9f6cd8277e12e3acb6294f4abea56e79dab30bf2629e4887a218b7f92f0683","335c2f5d2b6a982dbcab51eb61a7c1a65259dd31c215539811d85d5eb5bfc5b7","67ac09fd33e5e8ff886ad15d028c17823b005055a3ec0242162f8eb57751201c","2698a9f742d1afc95c63002ce7beeae30816ebe95608884fb8ebe5f053aa0c03","351a6ea23fc391a6af0b57a217e03b3daa9c8d3d4fb1f65f96a07e9eabb8eb47","7b700769530c5b804b393f27c15fb83d2eea86d1490203f4533ea57ad2262486","ce3ca973c816a32a924131d52abe4bad9fceeab2d73cb342c0d14b8c3728904c","ed6f0fc3bc6ec3090432c175fae77daca2c69ef12d9418acb74829259228cc66","eb5a6974408ff386089c69713aa804b1dfc3895f11b6195d1afe7573657ce776","6619670937557741f80daf2b7632b52999994423d14026455e8f476d82e74e57","e6400f4581e009226fa7a041476c0782a6bc761529be6fcc3494690730da8694","f0dff5e5f81fe746e18b3733c339f4b458641f3899f8c03261ee449fa45ff7dc","78fe4a27fac3f48f11bbf530e4d0db67056392d7a169d88b41c59c4d52e53ab8","93e61e5994bae334137e5d010751bd7949ea84a78cb97eaf4493204b911af3d3","d37774e3241f669654bd0cad5bf48268fea5efba91eb6fc58369bd54a3c9a72f","67732d84e3f18b415436963e4bf6b22fb2342b823a8827b31e27f90e721a665c","029feeb50b289d797634d31a9bedc1b12569bec01cee37781134570577df1a4a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[24936,24959],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx:p24936"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-1:  60 or 120 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":24960},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-2:  120, 480, or 960 kHz.","paragraph_zero_based":24961},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the field is absent, the UE applies the SCS as derived from the msgA-PRACH-ConfigurationIndex in RACH-ConfigGenericTwoStepRA (see tables Table 6.3.3.1-1, Table 6.3.3.1-2, Table 6.3.3.2-2 and Table 6.3.3.2-3, TS 38.211 [16]) in case of 2-step only BWP, otherwise the UE applies the same SCS as Msg1 derived from RACH-ConfigCommon. The value also applies to contention free 2-step random access type (RACH-ConfigDedicated).","paragraph_zero_based":24962},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-TotalNumberOfRA-Preambles","paragraph_zero_based":24963},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the total number of preambles used for contention-based and contention-free 2-step random access type when ROs for 2-step are not shared with 4-step. If the field is absent, and 2-step and 4-step does not have shared ROs, all 64 preambles are available for 2-step random access type.","paragraph_zero_based":24964},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-TransMax","paragraph_zero_based":24965},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Max number of MsgA preamble transmissions performed before switching to 4-step random access (see TS 38.321 [3], clauses 5.1.1). This field is only applicable when 2-step and 4-step RA type are configured and switching to 4-step type RA is supported. If the field is absent, switching from 2-step RA type to 4-step RA type is not allowed.","paragraph_zero_based":24966},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-ContentionResolutionTimer","paragraph_zero_based":24967},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The initial value for the contention resolution timer for fallback RAR in case no 4-step random access type is configured (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.5). Value sf8 corresponds to 8 subframes, value sf16 corresponds to 16 subframes, and so on. If both 2-step and 4-step random access type resources are configured on the BWP, then this field is absent. If the field is absent in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA in AdditionalRACH-Config, the UE shall apply the corresponding value in RACH-ConfigCommon in the same AdditionalRACH-Config.","paragraph_zero_based":24968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-Prioritization","paragraph_zero_based":24969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameters which apply for prioritized random access procedure on any UL BWP of SpCell for specific Access Identities (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.1a).","paragraph_zero_based":24970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-PrioritizationForAI","paragraph_zero_based":24971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the field ra-Prioritization-r16 applies for Access Identities. The first/leftmost bit corresponds to Access Identity 1, the next bit corresponds to Access Identity 2. Value 1 for an Access Identity indicates that the field ra-Prioritization-r16 applies, otherwise the field does not apply.","paragraph_zero_based":24972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-PrioritizationForSlicingTwoStep","paragraph_zero_based":24973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameters which apply to configure prioritized CBRA 2-step random access type for slicing.","paragraph_zero_based":24974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rach-ConfigGenericTwoStepRA","paragraph_zero_based":24975},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2-step random access type parameters for both regular random access and beam failure recovery.","paragraph_zero_based":24976},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24977},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GroupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":24978},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"messagePowerOffsetGroupB","paragraph_zero_based":24979},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Threshold for preamble selection. Value is in dB. Value minusinfinity corresponds to –infinity. Value dB0 corresponds to 0 dB, dB5 corresponds to 5 dB and so on. (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.1).","paragraph_zero_based":24980},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"numberOfRA-PreamblesGroupA","paragraph_zero_based":24981},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The number of CB preambles per SSB in group A for idle/inactive or connected mode. The setting of the number of preambles for each group should be consistent with msgA-SSB-PerRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB or msgA-CB-PreamblesPerSSB-PerSharedRO if configured.","paragraph_zero_based":24982},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-MsgA-SizeGroupA","paragraph_zero_based":24983}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e3250e6c0cd3fb3aba61a07b59149d950b97cf801261256eaaffa40eb003836b","original_member_sha256":"43effeec8825b995fac78441fed0808abcec562c85ad3256681daf06dadbee2c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ab4d57513f4000890f4a6e9124e8157ecaf2a1527b8009b5d4930f4596f7120d","613879897c23c1c50a319b74be17c96cbc860e6ac3cf3c8f20203a01315e34a1","b31061aa28d68bb9a757aadd358144ad61d02a366ffb01d3c0e6fbc04263682b","23428d2c5dc68befa9d9148dd3136cffe71c876979612a927da79283e7589c5e","21aefb1c50f9fc3bb717a6b93a965b99b36a29845764655806a926aab0730b37","81b35228741e1610d092b62d8623174c0fb36b972336e04bf7d4c7d7e332ce96","ace4a1a2f86412242da684b50d1c53302e05dda829138722be2a38533e3da332","d29f8c73eeb2864262cd5ca859c9fc55ae12c6ba60a9e3e4ea5f0848184571cf","73aa17a4bd75e1ddc2ef2f79c6ebb0f64a33a13930c76a9622fce405960e381d","dfa6bcaca1daeab27c2fc1c176c39ddd4fda35c4879daa85a9edff4ac9fccc0a","a569f6c317c65c3d54646072338f1247b1c7e326f49c84e8f58554e7da9ab555","08dbb025b19c5819344d36d3b7051eede7af7ae648b5ba70f8901ab21bef4a94","bef2ba7f7c6cc06a5755c7b2d33009df6841986de228292f5be6d370f8ab52e2","b918e3b144eb80d9d83699fc7f0783230b6e3b278aa26ecd7a556c0871b7893b","40c775167a5d5ce7fe3de14c793f7156ee7931f97e15d9f496acc293712b046c","95e150818f425ffa953f182c9bc5c3ac9318636cbbd40c68015de73d5c517936","be1abeb8ff3ca39497860fecfbc1480051491328e38e32f8910004b12a180935","c52af952436026aa23e6d02033b2cc77ba42e52315cf4be9e700f626b2626a13","64a6a89474bb5829f67c92e1b64810e7a5308cfa1419dfc247ddfac229b004f9","c2f0138062313ac29120e24697217545e5809c441d45ad5d3f7d8dc28f9dfdc6","9f51fbad061c0d653b8c056ddccfe8a652716b70f2127c566c0078ab0fa3b90e","03ce9a355040aff3c7b76b625fd38261c40b44371f3cc0b70e4d6f16b5016a7f","ece057668c5298f5c9b922809132c6073386ad04dcfa5af16832762c25f7c059","f9114212fdaa5824d9fe3b3fa9f69312654bf77159eefaf0e35c2d42d024b93a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[24960,24983],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx:p24960"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Transport block size threshold in bits below which the UE shall use a contention-based RA preamble of group A. (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.1).","paragraph_zero_based":24984},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24985},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":24986},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":24987},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2Step4Step","paragraph_zero_based":24988},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if both 2-step random access type and 4-step random access type are configured in the BWP, otherwise the field is not present.","paragraph_zero_based":24989},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in AdditionalRACH-Config if both 2-step random access type and 4-step random access type are configured for the same feature combination in the BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":24990},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2StepOnlyL139","paragraph_zero_based":24991},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if msgA-PRACH-RootSequenceIndex L=139 and no 4-step random access type is configured, otherwise the field is absent, Need S.","paragraph_zero_based":24992},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2StepOnly","paragraph_zero_based":24993},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in BWP-UplinkCommon if rach-ConfigCommon field is absent in this BWP-UplinkCommon, otherwise the field is optionally present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in BWP-UplinkCommon, Need S.","paragraph_zero_based":24994},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in AdditionalRACH-Config if rach-ConfigCommon field is absent in this AdditionalRACH-Config, otherwise the field is optionally present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in AdditionalRACH-Config, Need S.","paragraph_zero_based":24995},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"AdditionalRACH","paragraph_zero_based":24996},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if the msgA-ConfigCommon is included in an AdditionalRACH-Config. When included in initialUplinkBWP-RedCap to indicate other feature(s) than redcap, this field is mandatory present with at least two FeatureCombinationPreambles list entries: one list entry indicating only redcap and the other(s) indicating both redcap and one or multiple other feature(s) (e.g. smallData, nsag or msg3-Repetitions).","paragraph_zero_based":24997},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Otherwise, it is optional, Need R.","paragraph_zero_based":24998},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"InitialBWP-Only","paragraph_zero_based":24999},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is optionally present, Need R, if this BWP is the initial BWP of SpCell. Otherwise, the field is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":25000},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SharedRO","paragraph_zero_based":25001},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if the 2-step random access type occasions are shared with 4-step random access type, otherwise the field is not present.","paragraph_zero_based":25002},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":25003},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–RACH-ConfigDedicated","paragraph_zero_based":25004},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE RACH-ConfigDedicated is used to specify the dedicated random access parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":25005},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH-ConfigDedicated information element","paragraph_zero_based":25006},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":25007}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"doc