{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange is used to encode either a single or a range of physical cell identities. The range is encoded by using a start value and by indicating the number of consecutive physical cell identities (including start) in the range. For fields comprising multiple occurrences of EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange, NW may configure overlapping ranges of physical cell identities.","paragraph_zero_based":36840},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange information element","paragraph_zero_based":36841},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":36842},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLIDRANGE-START","paragraph_zero_based":36843},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36844},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange ::=       SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":36845},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    start                           EUTRA-PhysCellId,","paragraph_zero_based":36846},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    range                           ENUMERATED {n4, n8, n12, n16, n24, n32, n48, n64, n84, n96,","paragraph_zero_based":36847},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                n128, n168, n252, n504, spare2, spare1}                         OPTIONAL    -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":36848},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":36849},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36850},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLIDRANGE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36851},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36852},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36853},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1","paragraph_zero_based":36854},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1 is used to indicate whether all the neighbouring cells use Antenna Port 1. When set to true, the UE may assume that at least two cell-specific antenna ports are used in all neighbouring cells.","paragraph_zero_based":36855},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1 information element","paragraph_zero_based":36856},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":36857},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PRESENCEANTENNAPORT1-START","paragraph_zero_based":36858},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36859},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1 ::=              BOOLEAN","paragraph_zero_based":36860},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36861},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PRESENCEANTENNAPORT1-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36862},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36863}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e3250e6c0cd3fb3aba61a07b59149d950b97cf801261256eaaffa40eb003836b","original_member_sha256":"43effeec8825b995fac78441fed0808abcec562c85ad3256681daf06dadbee2c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9c426aecf2b9f06a1c114d3cb4fbecb0b9dce137199471bcf824a32b6e56ba52","6cf9b6dfdd596ebc10e62503dd78f53da7832c7adc353e405249accdf7f597e9","f5cccabae807eb1e14ee59e728a5478bc9f32b98ce04cbac89ded8b25ae1d876","4d70cc17b44af94d5f1b6ce807f0ee7275b9f59df8f9d3a6abb235d7e126ef58","193554e130a296d09e1764b8ff9271fe2366371ab58ac2530803779b2802a848","6ac02486122f50c93f55cde8648aa9a8a9f45b669e5abc86517215268955e491","f7cd0e39264e8aed4ac10cdd931fbb5c124bd4722e5fe9b545f7d72557e45937","25d54b8b5842b11901665e042891a8e990dcda125bb62c3d6a8ce3bee35b96c6","7dbb1e007e1bf16b05750de1c121884fcd8fe1a34737f5b4efe37fe5c6659862","5be963fb3083d04f026c56136f401b31ce1f