{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313638.zip::R2-2313638 NR-UAV-RRC-CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-FreqConfigCommon field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"frequencyShift7p5khzSL","paragraph_zero_based":38210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Enable the NR SL transmission with a 7.5 kHz shift to the LTE raster. If the field is absent, the frequency shift is disabled.","paragraph_zero_based":38211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-AbsoluteFrequencyPointA","paragraph_zero_based":38212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Absolute frequency of the reference resource block (Common RB 0). Its lowest subcarrier is also known as Point A.","paragraph_zero_based":38213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-AbsoluteFrequencySSB","paragraph_zero_based":38214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the frequency location of sidelink SSB. The transmission bandwidth for sidelink SSB is within the bandwidth of this sidelink BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":38215},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-BWP-List","paragraph_zero_based":38216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the list of sidelink BWP(s) on which the NR sidelink communication configuration. In this release, only one BWP is allowed to be configured for NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":38217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-NbAsSync","paragraph_zero_based":38218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates whether the network can be selected as synchronization reference directly/indirectly only, if sl-SyncPriority is set to gnss. If this field is set to TRUE, the network is enabled to be selected as synchronization reference directly/indirectly. The field is only present in SidelinkPreconfigNR. Otherwise it is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":38219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SyncPriority","paragraph_zero_based":38220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates synchronization priority order, as specified in clause 5.8.6..","paragraph_zero_based":38221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-SyncConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":38222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the configuration by which the UE is allowed to receive and transmit synchronisation information for NR sidelink communication. Network configures sl-SyncConfig including txParameters when configuring UEs to transmit synchronisation information. If this field is configured in SL-PreconfigurationNR-r16, only one entry is configured in sl-SyncConfigList.","paragraph_zero_based":38223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"valueN","paragraph_zero_based":38224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicate the NR SL transmission with a valueN *5kHz shift to the LTE raster (see TS 38.101-1 [15], clause 5.4E.2).","paragraph_zero_based":38225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":38227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":38228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"V2X-SL-Shared","paragraph_zero_based":38229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is mandatory present if the carrier frequency configured for NR sidelink communication is shared by V2X sidelink communication. It is absent, Need R, otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":38230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38231}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e3250e6c0cd3fb3aba61a07b59149d950b97cf801261256eaaffa40eb003836b","original_member_sha256":"43effeec8825b995fac78441fed0808abcec562c85ad3256681daf06dadbee2c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ede47a09a85921c851101bde2db166b8cdb625fc9d1ed6fe88e3abfbd7e3a5