{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313652.zip::R2-2313652 TEI18 SDT_ReleaseEnh 38331 CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"B","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-18","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In the “LS on SDT signalling optimization for partial context transfer” (R3-234589), RAN3 indicates that the signalling procedure for the DL non-SDT data arrival in case of SDT without UE anchor relocation (as described in TS 38.300 section 18.3) may be optimised for the scenario where currently, it requires to move the UE to RRC INACTIVE state and afterwards send RAN Paging messages in the cells of the RNA. This imposes additional signalling overhead in the RAN and increases the delay to trigger transition into RRC_CONNECTED state. ","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A resumeIndication is introduced in suspendConfig included in the RRCRelease message. After receiving such indication, the UE triggers RRC connection resume procedure automatically, i.e. without waiting for Paging from the network.","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Consequences if not approved:","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The signalling optimization for the DL non-SDT data arrival in case of SDT without UE anchor relocation as indicated in R3-234589 is not supported.","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"17bfba3da8c3743440a94764df1dd7e80753d504abfaf5e795d5a1c67c51ffac","original_member_sha256":"812d8433d8c47117aecae37ff5db028576123736cb57689623cc95ade6d2faf9","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["297e4a225b3dd3e28cd5903b5dfcb51efef4eee8a187a6c6cea7e06f734a4f71","eb193349e7d7be6bf72d5aa336a022b94ae5e08b4c329f40035d961cdaf88431","057fb8bc33ce470555363516d12e5c55f4f654bb43810f3f17c12e6c040a47cc","dd535f2f7aed98f0e7efbb8f25722fd6c9ffbffb40daf4427b76c6e6d0e4cfeb","4b497feac96fbb46804403b7fe8945c76b8a0bfc038965bf8566c51426d8909e","4a3b930b2897c7175ccf31105a5bf590c11273c87ea60bcda47aabdd413aec1a","7c0faf72b5d3651df46d4b08b0cb067568b955d4ba793986fbcbfa815a8e36ac","62f06dd64101ea2dcf659aaf339cce6172d25213dbd7a09f79213