{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Start of change","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.2Definitions","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the purposes of the present document, the terms and definitions given in TR 21.905 [1], in TS 36.300 [2] and the following apply. A term defined in the present document takes precedence over the definition of the same term, if any, in TR 21.905 [1] and TS 36.300 [2].","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BH RLC channel: an RLC channel between two nodes, which is used to transport backhaul packets.","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Boundary IAB-node: as defined in TS 38.401 [4].","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Broadcast MRB: A radio bearer configured for MBS broadcast delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CAG Cell: a PLMN cell broadcasting at least one Closed Access Group identity.","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CAG Member Cell: for a UE, a CAG cell broadcasting the identity of the selected PLMN, registered PLMN or equivalent PLMN, and for that PLMN, a CAG identifier belonging to the Allowed CAG list of the UE for that PLMN.","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CAG-only cell: a CAG cell that is only available for normal service for CAG UEs.","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Cell-Defining SSB: an SSB with an RMSI associated.","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Child node: IAB-DU's and IAB-donor-DU's next hop neighbour node; the child node is also an IAB-node.","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Handover (CHO): a handover procedure that is executed only when execution condition(s) are met.","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CORESET#0: the control resource set for at least SIB1 scheduling, can be configured either via MIB or via dedicated RRC signalling.","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DAPS Handover: a handover procedure that maintains the source gNB connection after reception of RRC message for handover and until releasing the source cell after successful random access to the target gNB.","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Direct Path: a type of UE-to-Network transmission path, where data is transmitted between a UE and the network without sidelink relaying.","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Downstream: direction toward child node or UE in IAB-topology.","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Early Data Forwarding: data forwarding that is initiated before the UE executes the handover.","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Earth-centered, earth-fixed: a global geodetic reference system for the Earth intended for practical applications of mapping, charting, geopositioning and navigation, as specified in NIMA TR 8350.2 [51].","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Feeder link: wireless link between the NTN Gateway and the NTN payload.","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Geosynchronous Orbit: earth-centered orbit at approximately 35786 kilometres above Earth's surface and synchronised with Earth's rotation. A geostationary orbit is a non-inclined geosynchronous orbit, i.e. in the Earth's equator plane.","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Group ID for Network Selection: an identifier used during SNPN selection to enhance the likelihood of selecting a preferred SNPN that supports a Default Credentials Server or a Credentials Holder, as specified in TS 23.501 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"gNB: node providing NR user plane and control plane protocol terminations towards the UE, and connected via the NG interface to the 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"High Altitude Platform Station: airborne vehicle embarking the NTN payload placed at an altitude between 8 and 50 km.","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-donor: gNB that provides network access to UEs via a network of backhaul and access links.","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["207671f6cd5b02dbe4aee1ed91a7f4c00aac4f6d9de38b900e3ff118fdb6caf1","fde3455c35bdb33f97a699d6fc0dd9f6a22f3b9e5e908c0e387dd1d3ba3cbf89","3c78357ccc7312c163274c7d31861aa79c6991d4f18a68bb55c6289066bc5bcf","31c92032284b6e5f42829a5e14a5ee0981ef2ab5b4a1869a7a7fdef9fb40ed58","10adfa10ac35b955acfe3a193d078142ff041ebddec797ab9bae0a0b6ffa0073","2635c4ab1be24140bf891aed331ed3e0ecaae67e4e1a8d5311616317d60da7d0","37844a1c2ccd6e729c91a84b6797bd4b9c6aee22ed14c3b2c68e07353ec2c061","2e0e3316affd5c52e942b57121f188a2dd4572132a98be100c9ee6fa19e293a5","dc4fd6c13b507f22d932a01e737c141942ccbbeeb225dc2ea820f740bf1ef7a1","35d1280a8f52b93ade993bd8aadce6962d31a90c177814b24998154b9f79c785","46d8bdb7e5523807a9406ee9a8c14264057c7f8e42370f4c24c09b8734b1c2f5","91a1992acffc19b3d980c075323483629f5514c9c7ea7c22a8b79ad9d816e5a4","ad9265c4d3dc85237a5272f8773f9371fed9615fa1ed42780fd3aa8d7801bd07","5ec48c0b36e4bed23bac7fa89ee8794ddceb50585d5baddfa99703860edf21a0","fdac3264a1a0f55a135a748b0bf878346381eefe2a0fae59d0a5d395446caac8","b26fc7289ce150527415ab9ef3ab92e38efa9e9df092d4e72e48c35e76a4ccae","56dad1ccb6f8ed4c3587b33504e15f618674ccd154efbf4b9c2ea5dd97664a54","13c3518e8a4ce4d52196026dcc6c992f54599826d835a6dbb60b84b8b023ba6b","2e0570c756912a6cbb59ea7e3ea905a7da761adf0cf7e6b75f3eb53d2c06a6ca","226167d554072d45f2cd73140be066bade166476cd3cbae376224d750970e071","9080204266fbc6fde705805a4ead10d47b1e85f38ec6c36dfa1a296d5b5659b7","f7d49cc280f412c8e90c399183c575fbc7b8621bef3b359a1ecd0185ff1f3e5b","b5dd761a9bd214b6f504a811fe6e48b8e050f4e92986661e0d01099aa8e248be","817375907647dfee8602539a8244fae8f2e476ef1e029d6e97443122b6329fad"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[120,143],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p120"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-donor-CU: as defined in TS 38.401 [4].","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-donor-DU: as defined in TS 38.401 [4].","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-DU: gNB-DU functionality supported by the IAB-node to terminate the NR access interface to UEs and next-hop IAB-nodes, and to terminate the F1 protocol to the gNB-CU functionality, as defined in TS 38.401 [4], on the IAB-donor.","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-MT: IAB-node function that terminates the Uu interface to the parent node using the procedures and behaviours specified for UEs unless stated otherwise. IAB-MT function used in 38-series of 3GPP Specifications corresponds to IAB-UE function defined in TS 23.501 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-node: RAN node that supports NR access links to UEs and NR backhaul links to parent nodes and child nodes. The IAB-node does not support backhauling via LTE.","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB topology: the unison of all IAB-nodes and IAB-donor-DUs whose F1 and/or RRC connections are terminated at the same IAB-donor-CU.","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indirect Path: a type of UE-to-Network transmission path, where data is forwarded via a U2N Relay UE between a U2N Remote UE and the network.","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-donor partial migration: migration of an IAB-MT to a parent node underneath a different IAB-donor-CU while the collocated IAB-DU and its descendant IAB-node(s), if any, are terminated at the initial IAB-donor-CU. The procedure renders the said IAB-node as a boundary IAB-node.","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Intra-system Handover: handover that does not involve a CN change (EPC or 5GC).","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-system Handover: handover that involves a CN change (EPC or 5GC).","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Late Data Forwarding: data forwarding that is initiated after the source NG-RAN node knows that the UE has successfully accessed a target NG-RAN node.","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Mapped Cell ID: in NTN, it corresponds to a fixed geographical area.","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MBS Radio Bearer: A radio bearer configured for MBS delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSG1: preamble transmission of the random access procedure for 4-step random access (RA) type.","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSG3: first scheduled transmission of the random access procedure.","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSGA: preamble and payload transmissions of the random access procedure for 2-step RA type.","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSGB: response to MSGA in the 2-step random access procedure. MSGB may consist of response(s) for contention resolution, fallback indication(s), and backoff indication.","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Multicast/Broadcast Service: A point-to-multipoint service as defined in TS 23.247 [45].","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Multicast MRB: A radio bearer configured for MBS multicast delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Multi-hop backhauling: using a chain of NR backhaul links between an IAB-node and an IAB-donor.","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ng-eNB: node providing E-UTRA user plane and control plane protocol terminations towards the UE, and connected via the NG interface to the 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NG-C: control plane interface between NG-RAN and 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NG-U: user plane interface between NG-RAN and 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NG-RAN node: either a gNB or an ng-eNB.","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["3e31a2f7220048e45edbe2447f576b298a4006e643dcd90135ae6041f001337f","08bf1bbe33ee790bfc53bc226ec57b3beb79191ed9ae39addd1c13ecc6d56508","ab63c862c08d3974ff122354579d96c797cea46ee2222a9226a2124a0e8b41bb","3d07c6867ccc77592d1c147cb42ddf58d4c24d223496337d8bf4e16e66ebb8ab","a5ef054d49e4c3d44c11298a016f1a24eca42e99a8529e628abcb7a009cf6836","fd5398013707bf9282999848853834db3095f2f28505a5fe70957aa363a33bb6","25b9a5b420844ad0c239265ee1cd8a9d74b597c8ba5800006ac1dc1f16c316ac","07e47c4a33114bf54d8ecc1b3f032a864eccda74c4e56898d2e649ab613975a1","e9e4325dee5ccd5492505972aeb2abfcbff67090786587bd26295b663c3a7794","bb4b7da3b332225beb44ba2e1fb2dbf7f1ceae48240fbcde7360a86c3d29a916","b39a8dade90e0f0ec5e1b2dd900d9e3266e553c5e7157524772cb7ab25d40a68","e2b244e79716f92775f23b4f5e79427d2fd99f18f7beff617172b1c282b43e11","89b1bb7b3f56015053b3c4ef51eba0ee500e0abd4d37141e6a4974fabdb2ae43","3f9f4e274c063a7809e021601a9845ceb5a041b5a678e57d07f175aa10e47584","41b28d0fff20fec7088c1205da080b60dbfc977ff331dafa14bcfce1ebf5c1c6","0715b342afb000ea10dd0887f9f21f4450b3dd333bc86bf0e132dddd36dac0fe","79b8faf8e1afd071efdb8ee8c1e5001e3724e8bd156962b5d4332f3583628a78","c7383205a6b4912f5c9774fa2e61d06719939f306d9a326463d66ef7d84b9867","6a1677d51b775a79a3df3945434f68c42293974140d896e74bcb8174bf5436b7","d43f12d1e2841d5d410f2c5f44c3a36d17b1cfd36c838177e8b124a7c48b51ce","1574b100cfe0c9f1ace2baf5c4c2cbb531a6c1d9e0e0f32b4bab25ae94463923","4d41f2e07d016c0921d7f6b60176deef92be56053c348b314107b6366ac2afaf","ce7b892fa9bb03a40bddab9341ba9c46980286b0f6fa9e8ea16191ed7f52269e","f45c061d8b3a2c12674c06b2cee966244ab10140ff7d59bdd4752a39034278de"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[144,167],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p144"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-CAG Cell: a PLMN cell which does not broadcast any Closed Access Group identity.","paragraph_zero_based":168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-Cell Defining SSB: an SSB without an RMSI associated.","paragraph_zero_based":169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-Geosynchronous orbit: earth-centered orbit with an orbital period that does not match Earth's rotation on its axis. This includes Low and Medium Earth Orbit (LEO and MEO). LEO operates at altitudes between 300 km and 1500 km and MEO at altitudes between 7000 km and 25000 km, approximately.","paragraph_zero_based":170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-terrestrial network: an NG-RAN consisting of gNBs, which provide non-terrestrial NR access to UEs by means of an NTN payload embarked on an airborne or space-borne NTN vehicle and an NTN Gateway.","paragraph_zero_based":171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR backhaul link: NR link used for backhauling between an IAB-node and an IAB-donor, and between IAB-nodes in case of a multi-hop backhauling.","paragraph_zero_based":172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink communication: AS functionality enabling at least V2X communication as defined in TS 23.287 [40] and the ProSe communication (including ProSe non-Relay and UE-to-Network Relay communication) as defined in TS 23.304 [48], between two or more nearby UEs, using NR technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink discovery: AS functionality enabling ProSe non-Relay Discovery and ProSe UE-to-Network Relay discovery for Proximity based Services as defined in TS 23.304 [48] between two or more nearby UEs, using NR technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NTN Gateway: an earth station located at the surface of the earth, providing connectivity to the NTN payload using the feeder link. An NTN Gateway is a TNL node.","paragraph_zero_based":175},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NTN payload: a network node, embarked on board a satellite or high altitude platform station, providing connectivity functions, between the service link and the feeder link. In the current version of this specification, the NTN payload is a TNL node.","paragraph_zero_based":176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Numerology: corresponds to one subcarrier spacing in the frequency domain. By scaling a reference subcarrier spacing by an integer N, different numerologies can be defined.","paragraph_zero_based":177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parent node: IAB-MT's next hop neighbour node; the parent node can be IAB-node or IAB-donor-DU","paragraph_zero_based":178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PC5 Relay RLC channel: an RLC channel between L2 U2N Remote UE and L2 U2N Relay UE, which is used to transport packets over PC5 for L2 UE-to-Network Relay.","paragraph_zero_based":179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN Cell: a cell of the PLMN.","paragraph_zero_based":180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RedCap UE: a UE with reduced capabilities as specified in clause 4.2.21.1 in TS 38.306 [11].","paragraph_zero_based":181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Relay discovery: AS functionality enabling 5G ProSe UE-to-Network Relay Discovery as defined in TS 23.304 [48], using NR technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Satellite: a space-borne vehicle orbiting the Earth embarking the NTN payload.","paragraph_zero_based":183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Service link: wireless link between the NTN payload and UE.","paragraph_zero_based":184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Sidelink Discovery RSRP: RSRP measurements on PC5 link related to NR sidelink discovery.","paragraph_zero_based":185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Sidelink RSRP: RSRP measurements on PC5 link related to NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SNPN Access Mode: mode of operation whereby a UE only accesses SNPNs.","paragraph_zero_based":187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SNPN-only cell: a cell that is only available for normal service for SNPN subscribers.","paragraph_zero_based":188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SNPN Identity: the identity of Stand-alone NPN defined by the pair (PLMN ID, NID).","paragraph_zero_based":189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Transmit/Receive Point: part of the gNB transmitting and receiving radio signals to/from UE according to physical layer properties and parameters inherent to that element.","paragraph_zero_based":190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2N Relay UE: a UE that provides functionality to support connectivity to the network for U2N Remote UE(s).","paragraph_zero_based":191}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a166f622a49c5fcc5f3137e21605fcc4c46eeb9b4a4740752d84af970dfc3c27","c6ff4b378e0c05d3343f5c094aacf072aa1ca498494e2d946f251676fcb64496","954f6c757304136059ff79ea28bc693c06e579ced474a4da1983b399d8376898","8a6c7b35e3035cafd1860426a81293d9e9824d857bf489489e44c95109539c66","9c13706e8a5c8899a34905a1f5a75c8808f9ea3347f7c1223d6c023bd7627e5f","e9057144f90d14de194dc50d1db9f29f0226771e715d0f28d1b52b589cde143d","3dad59f62dd52f301be43eddac7634eea96b795fa14dead9d9858248c81b34b7","5e9f76a9c8623fac72f44fa5ea5779ec28b82b1425f0c58214db78410fff2d97","b0c2ed060bac7d298e731e9123c381bd6be82acc03208a032271ebde8adb1bbc","42995b9236febead73a157655251c139e51a9fcb04c2827b8d0b6ed8c93bd786","5cf8bfe3dc6cef83cd8203fcd947e6c1eac04c263bcb982197154f8b7d178c5c","d7b2213f0b228bf70ba3d99122463d37a8c6b40d14d663f3fd60ff47d45cede4","5c8fd81b541d4c6387687eae8620d353b6fdab001e8e17804ee335ccc4950e33","dc643d6fe88613870736a7eda788bc3e466c39e24106fac5f3c437014633b2de","f993de907da6f7031dc306b958c0b0065fd16df3713258b44f9fe1103d3c59dd","dc4ae6b00b2120f5f03faf9cb3d77ca4a2304fafddb2341c94c99a9fa690816a","f8ca629a0fe19a202c79ae3bffaacc610a48651ac3e87d91d7528ce760bb4098","15063c61c7ca5d6691e3a92e16ee46ae34a361491332e099705c7538fad1c971","ed364818e4bd065f5c26fa6af61d5d81b839a121897b12f17d2744d07d7b2e0a","ff302b2bde84ab548ea6c536174babbe8e9e7597cccfcc97aa21da2de25f876c","446b1a4d0646c3330062f8e7ffa14b454a58111fb6f3d6f3697d1a0b4e61d269","a523b41ee9ea438eb3110e7cb1124386587197079de3883f5c9767a21fd87ea8","c3f5b88b1cb384333430400993a672ee164f8f94596e63cceacdc1c06692cd3e","15bb33d9c8c5091c3fd386c2dd0876d5cff10c9311033eaebd45e437fab773ec"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[168,191],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p168"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2N Remote UE: a UE that communicates with the network via a U2N Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upstream: direction toward parent node in IAB-topology.","paragraph_zero_based":193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Uu Relay RLC channel: an RLC channel between L2 U2N Relay UE and gNB, which is used to transport packets over Uu for L2 UE-to-Network Relay.","paragraph_zero_based":194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"V2X sidelink communication: AS functionality enabling V2X communication as defined in TS 23.285 [41], between nearby UEs, using E-UTRA technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Xn: network interface between NG-RAN nodes.","paragraph_zero_based":196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.4Synchronization signal and PBCH block","paragraph_zero_based":199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The Synchronization Signal and PBCH block (SSB) consists of primary and secondary synchronization signals (PSS, SSS), each occupying 1 symbol and 127 subcarriers, and PBCH spanning across 3 OFDM symbols and 240 subcarriers, but on one symbol leaving an unused part in the middle for SSS as show in Figure 5.2.4-1. The possible time locations of SSBs within a half-frame are determined by sub-carrier spacing and the periodicity of the half-frames where SSBs are transmitted is configured by the network. During a half-frame, different SSBs may be transmitted in different spatial directions (i.e. using different beams, spanning the coverage area of a cell).","paragraph_zero_based":200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Within the frequency span of a carrier, multiple SSBs can be transmitted. The PCIs of SSBs transmitted in different frequency locations do not have to be unique, i.e. different SSBs in the frequency domain can have different PCIs. However, when an SSB is associated with an RMSI, the SSB is referred to as a Cell-Defining SSB (CD-SSB). A PCell is always associated to a CD-SSB located on the synchronization raster.","paragraph_zero_based":201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When an SSB is not associated with an RMSI, the SSB is referred to as a non-Cell Defining SSB (NCD-SSB), which can be used to perform RLM, BFD, and RRM measurements and measurements for RA resource selection inside the active DL BWP when the active BWP does not contain the CD-SSB. A UE may be configured with multiple SSBs provided that each BWP is configured with at most one SSB (CD-SSB or NCD-SSB).","paragraph_zero_based":202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.2.4-1: Time-frequency structure of SSB","paragraph_zero_based":204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Polar coding is used for PBCH.","paragraph_zero_based":205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE may assume a band-specific sub-carrier spacing for the SSB unless a network has configured the UE to assume a different sub-carrier spacing.","paragraph_zero_based":206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PBCH symbols carry its own frequency-multiplexed DMRS.","paragraph_zero_based":207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"QPSK modulation is used for PBCH.","paragraph_zero_based":208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The PBCH physical layer model is described in TS 38.202 [20].","paragraph_zero_based":209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.3Mobility in RRC_CONNECTED","paragraph_zero_based":213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.3.1Overview","paragraph_zero_based":214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Network controlled mobility applies to UEs in RRC_CONNECTED and is categorized into two types of mobility: cell level mobility and beam level mobility. Beam level mobility includes intra-cell beam level mobility and inter-cell beam level mobility.","paragraph_zero_based":215}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["45348561e5c627aa73f5939b4c163af14bb17528180b2ba80a07102d4ed4db1a","6449c911c2d69482faa715e95f70e3aa7b6fd2e504e9f68497e0a30d61705d23","c8adc6a7d0a9b0a5eb6f5ebed716815c610b8b6028402733db521bba1e9adcce","7ad907dd308671f9c0f362273658e9b687ca1dcc18ba6f8c98fc5687f30d43f5","9361b53dd5ddfcfab68ada3c81798244e5b3fc976773c501ee4d9de9936760a0","517dc90565e68d9b83c6b1c9b7a108889d0bf1b9ab2130e6dcdb642b914eb97c","6950977a5ee71098961de7d7578b95ec80888a33d7587fd653f68803af29fad9","d408d93d012b899fc93a4431a8014bc5738ddfe385f991c43f10bd14d89ec179","0bde13687fa9d534c5196a11cbc5a8527cda7dfd648a986719b63ba9d5d7ff5c","bb9231410e93be4309b9f60461bb9acc3adf264b1e3afeb3f952cba2ba666097","5be958a932845b3cc68a112efbb7119a8f9c068e894c4de242a1b3248dc9c0da","23b56c4df45100329c1e52b713c93640409a188d7942c61f53859fb0760a6d85","df70ae77277b87f0f993766efef3e2743bee0429f2e98fb19202d658402accde","442416c8170fce6ceee87473636898a64b2fc5ea415ad526aea04f00c1e5ca36","7088f500de42f907fd50428c0673709c996f697fc8f7fca251dc1cb6559213c0","b8f8ae937cc22322d508ab7eef38f0d4538bd8c1f7ad91411efa9601f106cad1","ad92f8e33237f73a22e89194939a74b06329c3697800ea4ddcf5af25cbbc68a2","04cb0bb29ff4fdc67d57b3b7bc66d977991abaac5a5b0ba1fe6a2e9337e9ed5c","2ae42af7c1b55ed0231f78739ce10efdb6a4e84f99406d21b89428e5dc806913","46b979c4d61b9c9a74214442c2b09dc9a8e3f4e176ba1ed3ae015752c2e7cb4d","599af6cacc3f2a73246ea3c06b6c40847cef81cd889bfdca8dfe2bc9c3fb0211","e8a22715286c5c9da76de3c0289b776fb3132f81b2d139964eee725cff88eb1d","ae18ef2059304411426b43ea1e772b03c89ae2b0657cf4a6f0d7fd4e52d579f6","6e78b1cb22265497154567ccdeed13085e89a6c224cac9014592af61539edea5"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[192,215],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p192"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Cell Level Mobility requires explicit RRC signalling to be triggered, i.e. handover. For inter-gNB handover, the signalling procedures consist of at least the following elemental components illustrated in Figure 9.2.3.1-1:","paragraph_zero_based":216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 9.2.3.1-1: Inter-gNB handover procedures","paragraph_zero_based":218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1.The source gNB initiates handover and issues a HANDOVER REQUEST over the Xn interface.","paragraph_zero_based":219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2.The target gNB performs admission control and provides the new RRC configuration as part of the HANDOVER REQUEST ACKNOWLEDGE.","paragraph_zero_based":220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.The source gNB provides the RRC configuration to the UE by forwarding the RRCReconfiguration message received in the HANDOVER REQUEST ACKNOWLEDGE. The RRCReconfiguration message includes at least cell ID and all information required to access the target cell so that the UE can access the target cell without reading system information. For some cases, the information required for contention-based and contention-free random access can be included in the RRCReconfiguration message. The access information to the target cell may include beam specific information, if any.","paragraph_zero_based":221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.The UE moves the RRC connection to the target gNB and replies with the RRCReconfigurationComplete.","paragraph_zero_based":222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:User Data can also be sent in step 4 if the grant allows.","paragraph_zero_based":223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In case of DAPS handover, the UE continues the downlink user data reception from the source gNB until releasing the source cell and continues the uplink user data transmission to the source gNB until successful random access procedure to the target gNB.","paragraph_zero_based":224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Only source and target PCell are used during DAPS handover. CA, DC, SUL, multi-TRP, EHC, CHO, UDC, NR sidelink configurations and V2X sidelink configurations are released by the source gNB before the handover command is sent to the UE and are not configured by the target gNB until the DAPS handover has completed (i.e. at earliest in the same message that releases the source PCell).","paragraph_zero_based":225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The handover mechanism triggered by RRC requires the UE at least to reset the MAC entity and re-establish RLC, except for DAPS handover, where upon reception of the handover command, the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Creates a MAC entity for target;","paragraph_zero_based":227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Establishes the RLC entity and an associated DTCH logical channel for target for each DRB configured with DAPS;","paragraph_zero_based":228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For each DRB configured with DAPS, reconfigures the PDCP entity with separate security and ROHC functions for source and target and associates them with the RLC entities configured by source and target respectively;","paragraph_zero_based":229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Retains the rest of the source configurations until release of the source.","paragraph_zero_based":230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:Void.","paragraph_zero_based":231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:Void.","paragraph_zero_based":232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RRC managed handovers with and without PDCP entity re-establishment are both supported. For DRBs using RLC AM mode, PDCP can either be re-established together with a security key change or initiate a data recovery procedure without a key change. For DRBs using RLC UM mode, PDCP can either be re-established together with a security key change or remain as it is without a key change. For SRBs, PDCP can either remain as it is, discard its stored PDCP PDUs/SDUs without a key change or be re-established together with a security key change.","paragraph_zero_based":233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Data forwarding, in-sequence delivery and duplication avoidance at handover can be guaranteed when the target gNB uses the same DRB configuration as the source gNB.","paragraph_zero_based":234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Timer based handover failure procedure is supported in NR. RRC connection re-establishment procedure is used for recovering from handover failure except in certain CHO or DAPS handover scenarios:","paragraph_zero_based":235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When DAPS handover fails, the UE falls back to the source cell configuration, resumes the connection with the source cell, and reports DAPS handover failure via the source without triggering RRC connection re-establishment if the source link has not been released.","paragraph_zero_based":236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When initial CHO execution attempt fails or HO fails, the UE performs cell selection, and if the selected cell is a CHO candidate and if network configured the UE to try CHO after handover/CHO failure, then the UE attempts CHO execution once, otherwise re-establishment is performed.","paragraph_zero_based":237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DAPS handover for FR2 to FR2 case is not supported in this release of the specification.","paragraph_zero_based":238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The handover of the IAB-MT in SA mode follows the same procedure as described for the UE. After the backhaul has been established, the handover of the IAB-MT is part of the intra-CU topology adaptation procedure defined in TS 38.401 [4]. Modifications to the configuration of BAP sublayer and higher protocol layers above the BAP sublayer are described in TS 38.401 [4].","paragraph_zero_based":239}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["7973a1a163e469296fff06fc25ffef75601a0ab999176584ec2fa0b824eed0ae","2afb9f42700a06d90058cb58cb7af98ae224269d7d3393f634ddfcf7c15d378d","2686922479262dbe25495b905ba980c229a8441789c03e758ad3ff91ea542257","6657fc1f53186336d3377aa0ff75244a4cc04fc2bd79bb9e4c0b05f0c2262aec","66540f226974de83bba5daa08bac9f5b11b8e6974a989d6f68949e2fdb036a7d","3777a617c03b2d77f2bd06f6751c1ce3b71238b74f260bbd1cf79e90c59f7b84","aa46ab2d4185b894fd8d1780add2c6df2291642dc38e2de5b7dd6d0ef1e5bad4","2243b51f10d8f63ec9c197a35c2f949ddea812d0dd32aa448e9d1a8212194904","0cbe216596564ba2fc0130500376560f75e9812e9b0743e3bec698e7aae82931","956b189b0a07fa4070c8e2dc098b1bfab8a2a36fc61dce70ca8a60f0fd5fd7a8","87ba0ee507ac41bef372520020d39719a393729839399b701a1dca7506e776fe","e2244a60919774fd8326b5ca6c462aa2254b78d06b073149da6acf1ae6ff1d33","9a95186af045a987ed126bb92bcd9806e616495e6ba625c63dbcda0627158cce","9d623462e54eca38ec3ccf46d8e031475c2d25601765481be4089312f215600e","7d0e6214d2f4634d0abdfd01311a6203a9e1483a8e78bee3d852765ae3da59e3","91486032dc17b8d8799f9a327185f25bd6ad2cacae83dd2e2b912480406a20e3","4f286759f17a40756a63b5768d76761ebd7996daa4f30262e2e6edafeb3e6dc0","ec63ca140ad7e509b99e564e1502fd19b0c81b601f97128e1f93932dc20792a5","0bf1a216834796d17cc65376900c5319bd45fc194aa340a810930d4b419d1917","00706ce08f638eb0f5de6f0353f5fc1d68c4a62f0aff71298a4577f086074ef7","ebcf651f008088e4b02c9d97fdf2031f6d547c14ba86ba483b2f59ffed35d429","4a42c119890bc173e7dae92efdd9384251829c0979a1083c7c7b4bd137d53b0e","edc9cc1767e7a971f4de44fe7b9473e07e6f7dd2fae90f43547c54759a4ef5b3","d4c621cbdbb58cc65191beea3b397f3f7aac3af0b37d39b063a17c12b1d7c7e7"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[216,239],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p216"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Beam Level Mobility does not require explicit RRC signalling to be triggered. Beam level mobility can be within a cell, or between cells, the latter is referred to as inter-cell beam management (ICBM). For ICBM, a UE can receive or transmit UE dedicated channels/signals via a TRP associated with a PCI different from the PCI of a serving cell, while non-UE-dedicated channels/signals can only be received via a TRP associated with a PCI of the serving cell. The gNB provides via RRC signalling the UE with measurement configuration containing configurations of SSB/CSI resources and resource sets, reports and trigger states for triggering channel and interference measurements and reports. In case of ICBM, a measurement configuration includes SSB resources associated with PCIs different from the PCI of a serving cell. Beam Level Mobility is then dealt with at lower layers by means of physical layer and MAC layer control signalling, and RRC is not required to know which beam is being used at a given point in time.","paragraph_zero_based":240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSB-based Beam Level Mobility is based on the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP and can be configured for the initial DL BWPs, for DL BWPs containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP, and if supported, for DL BWPs not containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP. SSB-based Beam Level Mobility can be also performed based on a NCD-SSB, if configured for the active DL BWP. For other DL BWPs, Beam Level Mobility can only be performed based on CSI-RS, if configured for the active DL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.4Measurements","paragraph_zero_based":243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In RRC_CONNECTED, the UE measures multiple beams (at least one) of a cell and the measurements results (power values) are averaged to derive the cell quality. In doing so, the UE is configured to consider a subset of the detected beams. Filtering takes place at two different levels: at the physical layer to derive beam quality and then at RRC level to derive cell quality from multiple beams. Cell quality from beam measurements is derived in the same way for the serving cell(s) and for the non-serving cell(s). Measurement reports may contain the measurement results of the X best beams if the UE is configured to do so by the gNB.","paragraph_zero_based":244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The corresponding high-level measurement model is described below:","paragraph_zero_based":245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 9.2.4-1: Measurement Model","paragraph_zero_based":247},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:K beams correspond to the measurements on SSB or CSI-RS resources configured for L3 mobility by gNB and detected by UE at L1.","paragraph_zero_based":248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-A: measurements (beam specific samples) internal to the physical layer.","paragraph_zero_based":249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Layer 1 filtering: internal layer 1 filtering of the inputs measured at point A. Exact filtering is implementation dependent. How the measurements are actually executed in the physical layer by an implementation (inputs A and Layer 1 filtering) is not constrained by the standard.","paragraph_zero_based":250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-A1: measurements (i.e. beam specific measurements) reported by layer 1 to layer 3 after layer 1 filtering.","paragraph_zero_based":251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Beam Consolidation/Selection: beam specific measurements are consolidated to derive cell quality. The behaviour of the Beam consolidation/selection is standardised and the configuration of this module is provided by RRC signalling. Reporting period at B equals one measurement period at A1.","paragraph_zero_based":252},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-B: a measurement (i.e. cell quality) derived from beam-specific measurements reported to layer 3 after beam consolidation/selection.","paragraph_zero_based":253},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Layer 3 filtering for cell quality: filtering performed on the measurements provided at point B. The behaviour of the Layer 3 filters is standardised and the configuration of the layer 3 filters is provided by RRC signalling. Filtering reporting period at C equals one measurement period at B.","paragraph_zero_based":254},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-C: a measurement after processing in the layer 3 filter. The reporting rate is identical to the reporting rate at point B. This measurement is used as input for one or more evaluation of reporting criteria.","paragraph_zero_based":255},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Evaluation of reporting criteria: checks whether actual measurement reporting is necessary at point D. The evaluation can be based on more than one flow of measurements at reference point C e.g. to compare between different measurements. This is illustrated by input C and C1. The UE shall evaluate the reporting criteria at least every time a new measurement result is reported at point C, C1. The reporting criteria are standardised and the configuration is provided by RRC signalling (UE measurements).","paragraph_zero_based":256},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-D: measurement report information (message) sent on the radio interface.","paragraph_zero_based":257},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-L3 Beam filtering: filtering performed on the measurements (i.e. beam specific measurements) provided at point A1. The behaviour of the beam filters is standardised and the configuration of the beam filters is provided by RRC signalling. Filtering reporting period at E equals one measurement period at A1.","paragraph_zero_based":258},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-E: a measurement (i.e. beam-specific measurement) after processing in the beam filter. The reporting rate is identical to the reporting rate at point A1. This measurement is used as input for selecting the X measurements to be reported.","paragraph_zero_based":259},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Beam Selection for beam reporting: selects the X measurements from the measurements provided at point E. The behaviour of the beam selection is standardised and the configuration of this module is provided by RRC signalling.","paragraph_zero_based":260},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-F: beam measurement information included in measurement report (sent) on the radio interface.","paragraph_zero_based":261},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Layer 1 filtering introduces a certain level of measurement averaging. How and when the UE exactly performs the required measurements is implementation specific to the point that the output at B fulfils the performance requirements set in TS 38.133 [13]. Layer 3 filtering for cell quality and related parameters used are specified in TS 38.331 [12] and do not introduce any delay in the sample availability between B and C. Measurement at point C, C1 is the input used in the event evaluation. L3 Beam filtering and related parameters used are specified in TS 38.331 [12] and do not introduce any delay in the sample availability between E and F.","paragraph_zero_based":262},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Measurement reports are characterized by the following:","paragraph_zero_based":263}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0e7741ffd38e8798aa84473103e40cffba6acb9e0e712e6124ad4295120e3cf8","4ec248d5945476b93a71f5eddbad78315131a9bd5a8427e5c940bbe336ac3ad8","f4f236b8754d46f9c5d0870d67894782c5b580351deb681d69a62fa4ff7ec058","ca4eb3840d9efe1be77a5797f16946aeda2bfb1db4e652b63eec28b7edce11a8","9932309a8e5ba8f4b9f2ed6de5056c4411df20edf637462136886c1ddd6c32d9","fa1b16cea9d17a0c9ef5e05c7a634bfc45526e86c169fa48a34fe430fa0a636d","d0da35879e8493e73a320e0e281ca0b21b54fa77c8da284d8bf2151acc72615a","583514f2e857e0b056402aa190f951cc633706e62453ca099004483693d27f3d","1961653cc45252e3f970eaa110b03219d991e3b7bed2c90eb4266ab5557dbf3b","9b8d36fa18b2a7e91e26e297bc38c2f1a6c7d557bdf4504a09fe12e38d1be5e9","24fb61dedece4cc2a4705ad55056f6772ed0b545ad4bcb1da0a3f917ad5fac6f","847ee2f639c42eca90d26b870707b5c2f397fe1ce86eb4fdd8d0194467bb330e","07e6fdc35fefb1b271fddcb77a791b9cd2113f6f96eb179d2a407f328c3e9501","f41701cd437a994e9e56c270c584ddccbce1f73a5a3f35f84b5a3d4ffc5f8783","0b25d4990eddc2f8aa4dcc2483fd449e2bf30b0ecd4b1111d4c7a4eb564c378a","22cb06709175a8f558ea43c5ca5de304efc20bf9d45582f2d35a1d5336d6d9b9","d6bf04c3e7effe0e7ad4dbb6fc1d266566599af3a21b8478df07b35075177214","0ebe039c97171ee67895557988f883969b7d45c8ecc63cc3ace7ff7580390e22","dd8b62879321043db8a5ef04ccf84811ece7e4f2144ad807cf769601ac2248fd","df6db1936f9f065fc6c9791753621ae4435684c32892951021bf9b962834fb25","accf6de25e84fa211ac1596a3a02ea9158dd524fe0f7debb2b7154a8ff435b3d","0d411fbb4706b042299bfa78397caa3a630e3132084e180ba2352dd2780b4d37","b25acf96073b5a2ed596768898fef970b5bd8aa379f43a3d5bacc5966c79b1a0","5717808a0267e77aa855ccea95158dac82881fdd04cc1bd4f89534b73c4806d3"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[240,263],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p240"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Measurement reports include the measurement identity of the associated measurement configuration that triggered the reporting;","paragraph_zero_based":264},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Cell and beam measurement quantities to be included in measurement reports are configured by the network;","paragraph_zero_based":265},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The number of non-serving cells to be reported can be limited through configuration by the network;","paragraph_zero_based":266},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Cells belonging to an exclude-list configured by the network are not used in event evaluation and reporting, and conversely when an allow-list is configured by the network, only the cells belonging to the allow-list are used in event evaluation and reporting;","paragraph_zero_based":267},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Beam measurements to be included in measurement reports are configured by the network (beam identifier only, measurement result and beam identifier, or no beam reporting).","paragraph_zero_based":268},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Intra-frequency neighbour (cell) measurements and inter-frequency neighbour (cell) measurements are defined as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":269},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SSB based intra-frequency measurement: a measurement is defined as an SSB based intra-frequency measurement provided the center frequency of the SSB of the serving cell and the center frequency of the SSB of the neighbour cell are the same, and the subcarrier spacing of the two SSBs is also the same.","paragraph_zero_based":270},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SSB based inter-frequency measurement: a measurement is defined as an SSB based inter-frequency measurement provided the center frequency of the SSB of the serving cell and the center frequency of the SSB of the neighbour cell are different, or the subcarrier spacing of the two SSBs is different.","paragraph_zero_based":271},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:For SSB based measurements, one measurement object corresponds to one SSB and the UE considers different SSBs as different cells.","paragraph_zero_based":272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2a:If a UE is configured to perform serving cell measurements based on an NCD-SSB configured in its active BWP, this NCD-SSB is considered as the SSB of the serving cell in the definition of intra-frequency and inter-frequency measurements as above.","paragraph_zero_based":273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-CSI-RS based intra-frequency measurement: a measurement is defined as a CSI-RS based intra-frequency measurement provided that:","paragraph_zero_based":274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The subcarrier spacing of CSI-RS resources on the neighbour cell configured for measurement is the same as the SCS of CSI-RS resources on the serving cell indicated for measurement; and","paragraph_zero_based":275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For 60kHz subcarrier spacing, the CP type of CSI-RS resources on the neighbour cell configured for measurement is the same as the CP type of CSI-RS resources on the serving cell indicated for measurement; and","paragraph_zero_based":276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The centre frequency of CSI-RS resources on the neighbour cell configured for measurement is the same as the centre frequency of CSI-RS resource on the serving cell indicated for measurement.","paragraph_zero_based":277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-CSI-RS based inter-frequency measurement: a measurement is defined as a CSI-RS based inter-frequency measurement if it is not a CSI-RS based intra-frequency measurement.","paragraph_zero_based":278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:Extended CP for CSI-RS based measurement is not supported in this release.","paragraph_zero_based":279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Whether a measurement is non-gap-assisted or gap-assisted depends on the capability of the UE, the active BWP of the UE and the current operating frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For SSB based inter-frequency measurement, if the measurement gap requirement information is reported by the UE, a measurement gap configuration may be provided according to the information. Otherwise, a measurement gap configuration is always provided in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE only supports per-UE measurement gaps;","paragraph_zero_based":282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE supports per-FR measurement gaps and any of the serving cells are in the same frequency range of the measurement object.","paragraph_zero_based":283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For SSB based intra-frequency measurement, if the measurement gap requirement information is reported by the UE, a measurement gap configuration may be provided according to the information. Otherwise, a measurement gap configuration is always provided in the following case:","paragraph_zero_based":284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Other than the initial BWP, if any of the UE configured BWPs do not contain the frequency domain resources of the SSB associated to the initial DL BWP, and are not configured with NCD-SSB for serving cell measurement.","paragraph_zero_based":285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In non-gap-assisted scenarios, the UE shall be able to carry out such measurements without measurement gaps. In gap-assisted scenarios, the UE cannot be assumed to be able to carry out such measurements without measurement gaps.","paragraph_zero_based":286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Network may request the UE to measure NR and/or E-UTRA carriers in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE via system information or via dedicated measurement configuration in RRCRelease. If the UE was configured to perform measurements of NR and/or E-UTRA carriers while in RRC_IDLE or in RRC_INACTIVE, it may provide an indication of the availability of corresponding measurement results to the gNB in the RRCSetupComplete message. The network may request the UE to report those measurements after security activation. The request for the measurements can be sent by the network immediately after transmitting the Security Mode Command (i.e. before the reception of the Security Mode Complete from the UE).","paragraph_zero_based":287}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e98e52518ff4456fd7f5fbe8bda495e5e7a7a7ddfffa96412aac561d6ed873ce","b0644b7dd4695e566ff19cc3cf17d0895f51a45baec84101226382b0566741a1","580e05d2a04c3fd5c5ac36f3fa4a5be17b2dec24dfc7e442edee38a9bb0b5dbd","3e92500aeb0866212f9757a5607fb30a11c0273c2e5c59c85fc4b1e79f8b8010","24285e67adca63edd01fd040434efa862339c47fdaf4870ee494250660c9cb15","b9b1bcc636a531dc9f8cc29b70b214405beab41680c1e50d0213faeac73cc615","a6f394ebe3ba4e0c4725a8b56c4bd46318662ed11bc5bba86b4c3a0ec05ce622","ba3e5b3d7eef2a3dc2409afffafa838a09b44142c704e2894637aa932f4f6abb","f9f9c7f522e05fc492bded15d862756400689e023b159b1c126bcc475480aa7d","ec49c9317e9d4dbc9afd958064d35590e24b0cc28b8361b1c377cfb2aa1cedef","7d50defd151eb11d65f5f2a53bcd5ae76ee17474262edd5768fe3b2c6ae6d63e","4a57b4b7f8a2502ea53b184d9d5babdbe2a7d1731670a0fcd8c08ae33f9dcc30","2b579bf44c93425233f2f44c2ed68c82ebe3f103dfa7afdce1cbec06357e3649","4d0a737047c28258ded4abab926fd67583597bf4cba314e57fe87394b9b1d683","caf7a7b0aceeb184dbb1d26fe92635e307148909d9b6df43a88316bd57c574ce","e3d1ccbd8aa09dac1adc5b654401b1be183318312ede9ab14396f5d5a8cc94b4","3da20aca5ede926d0c14ba55f2aba8553219b6ad7de2bf429b482c7577b5900c","17c8aba15676aad6bad40821f0abdc85f3c0a4d1fcc1a94fe15eeb3567e0f91e","9998fe1b02b1358ea9720409fe160f54fe6a4d07e7b9d0175cc3971cb0c04974","82c8a3e00b6bcaa55588dcc6a7b749be77cac983d01a43da26860760e52e0b1c","b6dd224139b1aff00263bf9c877325101a40355d54ab71ec6750300494534996","712d6edba37ca2da128509de5044af2f5d0d9e088dd840271503c768c3262810","789945d78a6004e99d2f3cc53379b4faa0b4d7ce6d64f1fb38e0126cb867e5b8","9a729d0456d9d02568d527d8206f37729edcf5efbd4b058c87c789606f9e09cc"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[264,287],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p264"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the UE was configured to perform measurements of NR and/or E-UTRA carriers while in RRC_INACTIVE, the gNB can request the UE to provide corresponding measurement results in the RRCResume message and then the UE can include the available measurement results in the RRCResumeComplete message. Alternatively, the UE may provide an indication of the availability of the measurement results to the gNB in the RRCResumeComplete message and the gNB can then request the UE to provide these measurement results.","paragraph_zero_based":288},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":289},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":290},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.7Radio Link Failure","paragraph_zero_based":291},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In RRC_CONNECTED, the UE performs Radio Link Monitoring (RLM) in the active BWP based on reference signals (SSB/CSI-RS) and signal quality thresholds configured by the network. SSB-based RLM is based on the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP and can be configured for the initial DL BWP, for DL BWPs containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP, and, if supported, for DL BWPs not containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP. Besides, SSB-based RLM can be also performed based on a non-cell defining SSB, if configured for the active DL BWP. For other DL BWPs, RLM can only be performed based on CSI-RS, if configured for the active DL BWP. In case of DAPS handover, the UE continues the detection of radio link failure at the source cell until the successful completion of the random access procedure to the target cell.","paragraph_zero_based":292},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE declares Radio Link Failure (RLF) when one of the following criteria are met:","paragraph_zero_based":293},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Expiry of a radio problem timer started after indication of radio problems from the physical layer (if radio problems are recovered before the timer is expired, the UE stops the timer); or","paragraph_zero_based":294},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Expiry of a timer started upon triggering a measurement report for a measurement identity for which the timer has been configured while another radio problem timer is running; or","paragraph_zero_based":295},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Random access procedure failure; or","paragraph_zero_based":296},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RLC failure; or","paragraph_zero_based":297},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Detection of consistent uplink LBT failures for operation with shared spectrum channel access as described in 5.6.1; or","paragraph_zero_based":298},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For IAB-MT, the reception of a BH RLF indication received from its parent node.","paragraph_zero_based":299},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"After RLF is declared, the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":300},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-stays in RRC_CONNECTED;","paragraph_zero_based":301},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-in case of DAPS handover, for RLF in the source cell:","paragraph_zero_based":302},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-stops any data transmission or reception via the source link and releases the source link, but maintains the source RRC configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":303},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-if handover failure is then declared at the target cell, the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":304},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-selects a suitable cell and then initiates RRC re-establishment;","paragraph_zero_based":305},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-enters RRC_IDLE if a suitable cell was not found within a certain time after handover failure was declared.","paragraph_zero_based":306},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-in case of CHO, for RLF in the source cell:","paragraph_zero_based":307},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-selects a suitable cell and if the selected cell is a CHO candidate and if network configured the UE to try CHO after RLF then the UE attempts CHO execution once, otherwise re-establishment is performed;","paragraph_zero_based":308},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-enters RRC_IDLE if a suitable cell was not found within a certain time after RLF was declared.","paragraph_zero_based":309},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-otherwise, for RLF in the serving cell or in case of DAPS handover, for RLF in the target cell before releasing the source cell:","paragraph_zero_based":310},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-selects a suitable cell and then initiates RRC re-establishment;","paragraph_zero_based":311}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["7cb0ee41b81add93070642c8c82014b0d6a2777d46383985b08b6112938dc6a2","7fb5365dd042a074ee0c2d2161bcdb924973204b95a3adec809b0e34e198e79e","b5351ecf189b92182033f2f2066d8d1768389b02ea3b88e075333530c6b488c0","edbf4c2af7f36a5de3d3b89a68f695377cdb2bf9bb6619335e9709093c919d70","89453cd520ecd4580319ec2d19f86a9344c188859c1be45b454a3be750bd9778","637c865340bb1b541059b44427e276b16385f7b7e2a98931723d81c6fd077bbd","bf0e42403ac1ea14fb1f991940501701f88b04fe392ba21022f8e0ea27d40998","80d7664bc3443bf066fdd3146e9e001199184642a1af73b1e3544662b3f65ece","692367e06c76e3c1a2c115b04ad019258f6d7913ab6fc351228d01d21bc9ebf4","3da797224c128fd191846aed4b188fa57c8cae593db1cc32ae600a967ef25854","1999a111d79a7792293bd2a33d9b418dc994289999b9a9fe6283ed59358a6bd0","ae699d1ef62a8875bcabe12459249d80dd47cfa629f31a760457ef854be58d93","a1c12407d63d9061eb5c4f9150cf968dac0e739f0de54dbe6677d6ef7850d83c","5f6dea1b1c9a641fa42b03388f88bb33f7f47ca88c29a4f978ffaf0e437da0b5","111fd937f9c1c75ea0be332e23ce8d866e50555da8173a4423651baacfdabc30","b46dd5eea8330e6a55fa6f280b12a40e721686c2115a5d34380cdd6924b60770","9c45744c12ab2d4770542ae2db5a84286c642b0f0683268d57435a43e293089c","c3c9b06a520b73729d364303995b9d4ede7655e36434e79463560db449bbfbbe","0edd29ba90a790fd3a5771059a8faee0fb92caafc5e5edced7f4d3373057a236","4ba29a4780890e9cb650e522417b6f4fbb52605fd8c3bcac118e7cd58b6e415a","85903921b15db2c37752cfd337466d71b7b00fbe6f80b7e8831d8b130cf9449f","cd08859277253c679ffd6e065d044fa539cc88ddfb4b1cc59caa044698e91943","0fb4242351d9af97dab3d872b688ddefd1c8513a0fa81fb0f16fd8d40ec7e77f","8f1451fef845c7aee6ed5cd93c0a6aa16e8439e40197dd118127609fb45a1c27"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[288,311],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p288"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-enters RRC_IDLE if a suitable cell was not found within a certain time after RLF was declared.","paragraph_zero_based":312},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When RLF occurs at the IAB BH link, the same mechanisms and procedures are applied as for the access link. This includes BH RLF detection and RLF recovery.","paragraph_zero_based":313},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IAB-DU can transmit a BH RLF detection indication to its child nodes in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":314},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The collocated IAB-MT initiates RRC re-establishment;","paragraph_zero_based":315},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The collocated IAB-MT is dual-connected, detects BH RLF on a BH link, and cannot perform UL re-routing for any traffic. This includes the scenario of an IAB-node operating in EN-DC or NR-DC, which uses only one link for backhauling and has BH RLF on this BH link;","paragraph_zero_based":316},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The collocated IAB-MT has received a BH RLF detection indication from a parent node, and there is no remaining backhaul link that is unaffected by the BH RLF condition indicated.","paragraph_zero_based":317},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon reception of the BH RLF detection indication, the child node may perform local rerouting for upstream traffic, if possible, over an available BH link.","paragraph_zero_based":318},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the IAB-DU has transmitted a BH RLF detection indication to a child node due to an RLF condition on the collocated IAB-MT's parent link, and the collocated IAB-MT's subsequent RLF recovery is successful, the IAB-DU may transmit a BH RLF recovery indication to this child node.","paragraph_zero_based":319},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the IAB-DU has transmitted a BH RLF detection indication to a child node due to the reception of a BH RLF detection indication by the collocated IAB-MT, and the collocated IAB-MT receives a BH RLF recovery indication, the IAB-DU may also transmit a BH RLF recovery indication to this child node.","paragraph_zero_based":320},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon reception of the BH RLF recovery indication, the child node reverts the actions triggered by the reception of the previous BH RLF detection indication.","paragraph_zero_based":321},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In case the RRC re-establishment procedure fails, the IAB-node may transmit a BH RLF indication to its child nodes. The BH RLF detection indication, BH RLF recovery indication and BH RLF indication are transmitted as BAP Control PDUs.","paragraph_zero_based":322},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":323},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":324},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.8Beam failure detection and recovery","paragraph_zero_based":325},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For beam failure detection, the gNB configures the UE with beam failure detection reference signals (SSB or CSI-RS) and the UE declares beam failure when the number of beam failure instance indications from the physical layer reaches a configured threshold before a configured timer expires. For beam failure detection in multi-TRP operation, the gNB configures the UE with two sets of beam failure detection reference signals, and the UE declares beam failure for a TRP / BFD-RS set when the number of beam failure instance indications associated with the corresponding set of beam failure detection reference signals from the physical layer reaches a configured threshold before a configured timer expires.","paragraph_zero_based":326},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSB-based Beam Failure Detection is based on the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP and can be configured for the initial DL BWPs, for DL BWPs containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP, and, if supported, for DL BWPs not containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP. Besides, SSB-based Beam Failure Detection can be also performed based on the non-cell defining SSB, if configured for the active DL BWP. For other DL BWPs, Beam Failure Detection can only be performed based on CSI-RS, if configured for the active DL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":327},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"After beam failure is detected on PCell, the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":328},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-triggers beam failure recovery by initiating a Random Access procedure on the PCell;","paragraph_zero_based":329},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-selects a suitable beam to perform beam failure recovery (if the gNB has provided dedicated Random Access resources for certain beams, those will be prioritized by the UE).","paragraph_zero_based":330},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-includes an indication of a beam failure on PCell in a BFR MAC CE if the Random Access procedure involves contention-based random access.","paragraph_zero_based":331},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon completion of the Random Access procedure, beam failure recovery for PCell is considered complete.","paragraph_zero_based":332},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"After beam failure is detected on an SCell, the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":333},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-triggers beam failure recovery by initiating a transmission of a BFR MAC CE for this SCell;","paragraph_zero_based":334},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-selects a suitable beam for this SCell (if available) and indicates it along with the information about the beam failure in the BFR MAC CE.","paragraph_zero_based":335}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["172db71fb347c20dc189295acf498e7569fc0f1d9f9ce45297075f7ebe0aa2e9","bf1bdb0c426a6844368a619e81c274a2ac111da090e5806431dccdabf8cfca87","832e4deb87ba8516e1574c4824fbb28c6abe3299b2b7f802ef24c58fdf67e321","de82d8112e11804738ba32d2d3dc155e38f8edc1768a8c7cbe4890c68a059231","f90daabf33a72f8619544483310ac80fdbe51beeed5c2bf34000c7041b41970e","e9d50c7acc72c168fca9ec95aa9c3fd0dc9470e28daba0a78fa7b8e6066277d0","834c66218ac793205fa9fcf6b10b7168332f81c60247da93955e4e8af70e60d7","3205af605d0ed824348d2155e95572c7508fbf03f3a67a02da4fe2517f2aceaa","fcd94adc07d0997ed86a2ac40c0330af389adeb3fe8c37cd244305c341716c46","fd5a400e00e118199cba2923015dd277f61958733221740aece326c918f192eb","bae8e4795a8edb3b70530f4a53e7aec63e386db2aa25befc810616793ddeeae1","fb65608c281b60540832ea9bcbe758ba6ed78ecaa6da614c5a64eed992aaa95e","e97322a9f2b1fa45e845d4d795d4d67bfaedc4441314cb5b57603a601bc7e730","6dabea5e77c23a73e63112a217dce155a58b84705dc4435a20c01ef3a8f85cc8","37009e2b400235c69e2eb4fa756eb190d7ddd150bb2cfe710b9bd3791702c91a","90d756f81d3f9c4fe731349c31cd92c3cf9cea7d5ada3e6972b0774a66a7e558","13facacf0da9cc140f14cc4d419ad5fbf3caf410eff14819e3e1ae8bf1ccd1fb","68d204c926c4e52d99afc84ee23de98419d745580c019097f2456a95398d2388","082c13f9d20e4b1658c2c80b02359e1712800e80a36b74853b67b3d642276b6a","bf4e582cb69b9939d016df97ab610f0ea52c5b5ddf2ac7a9bc6be5d4be32c4e4","ecb57adbb63af042db106bb45134039627ee0612e3e42d8a86bd7e53c60d0df8","6cdaaaae7e42e84ac796ad578abbb363ae1c7880c72b64d29c0bc1188cbd689f","867d5673597ef2f133f706e601579f1e43270643f66a71e9c8aaf9c7065ad864","1c40fef5cc4d820c57bef606dd6d531e967a7ff22990e903ab9b9f649d128b73"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[312,335],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p312"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon reception of a PDCCH indicating an uplink grant for a new transmission for the HARQ process used for the transmission of the BFR MAC CE, beam failure recovery for this SCell is considered complete.","paragraph_zero_based":336},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"After beam failure is detected for a BFD-RS set of a Serving Cell, the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":337},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-triggers beam failure recovery by initiating a transmission of a BFR MAC CE for this BFD-RS set;","paragraph_zero_based":338},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-selects a suitable beam for this BFD-RS set (if available) and indicates whether the suitable (new) beam is found or not along with the information about the beam failure in the BFR MAC CE for this BFD-RS set.","paragraph_zero_based":339},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon reception of a PDCCH indicating an uplink grant for a new transmission for the HARQ process used for the transmission of the BFR MAC CE for this BFD-RS set, beam failure recovery for this BFD-RS set is considered complete.","paragraph_zero_based":340},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"After beam failure is detected for both BFD-RS sets of PCell concurrently, the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":341},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-triggers beam failure recovery by initiating a Random Access procedure on the PCell;","paragraph_zero_based":342},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-selects a suitable beam for each failed BFD-RS set (if available) and indicates whether the suitable (new) beam is found or not along with the information about the beam failure in the BFR MAC CE for each failed BFD-RS set;","paragraph_zero_based":343},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-upon completion of the Random Access procedure, beam failure recovery for both BFD-RS sets of PCell is considered complete.","paragraph_zero_based":344},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":345},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"End of change","paragraph_zero_based":346},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":347}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"56069dad09fc2f50ed8d6a3e97b27ce3c6066c36f3e93deec947f09b897825a6","original_member_sha256":"2038c8b1e340b35ad235f544a37c574ec5be193e19ee03c00eb085ab950e7564","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["07fedb4ab263b000b150d49c15916b2f96dbdd0b4c12bee3af9a6a292f0a963a","baca9ef127b0d4a56d0a6fbfefbc43cbb2bb20175e050891a185fc4356868ab6","32f912e259e8f4a173ac389fbcaaab4e7603c33f0c32a315eaca97dd4125134c","e1ca6bbe78c64e5e837b2383c21bc2a4be6ffdf90c513850700dd0eb7d6542f7","83cd88697fdd491acb804a7dd9b690bcbfb393828603fcc0a0146002ae4fd290","6d29700cf45af7b6d9c9d118c49fb7143d39013c66857616ba7ab82d7461d62b","de77e8a8596263e9c4f9fd7d1dea3055411d2a4a073af69aa79e6f40ff29b509","69a9cd5372d9b2336b6de7133c7c8cdc0eabc403c6ff1a84dda9f3aafda251ea","54c5135e9d992236894e3cb5df26cc2c912dc8405b3eca401256ebfa7b2d877b","defec5acec969431ce03c5bfdffe9311aaeb238182fe8ec4ffc717a1f093fb8b","ee858b887396d84e28e9e2c84611eb40894d7ce76996ec7ae8468c8e4023dd92","97ac144d60193f269af836e9ecb9342fedcb99d2048a03c17c4b967b8f72b405"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[336,347],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2313690.zip::R2-2313690_Introduction of support for BWP operation without restriction in TS38.300.docx:p336"}
