{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2400627.zip::R2-2400627 Correction BT positioning mode support TS38305.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 9:UE-based positioning mode is supported only for Bluetooth AoD positioning method.","paragraph_zero_based":216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Sensor, WLAN, Bluetooth, and TBS positioning methods based on MBS signals are also supported in standalone mode, as described in the corresponding clauses.","paragraph_zero_based":218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The SL positioning and ranging methods may be supported in SL-Target UE-based or SL-Target UE-assisted/server-based mode, where \"server\" may be a SL Server UE or LMF. Table 4.3.1-2 indicates which of these versions are supported in this version of the specification for the SL positioning and ranging methods.","paragraph_zero_based":219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Table 4.3.1-2: Supported versions of SL positioning and ranging methods.","paragraph_zero_based":220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Method","paragraph_zero_based":221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-Target UE-based","paragraph_zero_based":222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-Target UE-assisted, server-based","paragraph_zero_based":223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-RTTNOTE 1","paragraph_zero_based":224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-AoANOTE 2","paragraph_zero_based":227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-TDOA","paragraph_zero_based":230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-TOA","paragraph_zero_based":233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:The SL-RTT method may also be used for ranging between UEs.","paragraph_zero_based":236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The SL-AoA method may also be used to obtain direction between UEs.","paragraph_zero_based":237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"End of changes","paragraph_zero_based":239}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5b02fa5d38f26c57ef4ae3249c9ddc3542b9c288e8b322c96b1e55a5ae8bf1e8","original_member_sha256":"c9d97b7a48bdd260906825d063a9aeaa517c5eaf9d984f932ecbcf5b265095df","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9c9ca541c4375acab78f68519c13d7ad6ed97596392e1756142f31f78b41389a","914b198d62787f9804aa57dce7367bfaf5f3f7710a16542f35777ac42e5491e1","29b9f50d573ef2c64e48df45bed018348a9c3931324c64f6d4eee4a16de4f998","da54f16b914f2d94853abaf5ee8b4b3fcb82c29815327e65ee1ca1521b95373f","824fbdd6dd07ed78f0519b431b80eeb6e9cbc4fcedf44911e85817d147349b75","38572bef22b51c2c99ece148cc106c1ce53cdac62471e5145b7c66bee03ae003","ae8ea0e4a31438c1d1238f4c6c1d8e2d3c9cfa8f84da0d6be4a682e74d85848c","7905089f439b3ef1d10da0116be640a06ecfd0734b7b885657498678c8ddc432","92628ebb4a982d35c829367f1056501a119c4ac7c608ea2556b82c09941f84c0","c799a54079e924d69a820a71968e5ab13b51df43713ccb155976372192f766c4","dae169ea1dcb7f4cb3bf1fefae8b393a9d59657e50ab289f90656f57cbe415e2","4adaf7c1509fd39b9cfb3a5ff9f50b28224bce3ca98118fbe9da3186c4e38702","c91d006281290515375001638a571f7562479922200ff1e914bf2dfbefbb7fb1","6c07e5a677557778fc985f58b8be498a135bf72bc9352d5913d902df4af7887e","2d3067877989d2c11c979b1c0bbb10c085132588710662728dbad775bb5c7057","a74846d8ce6e16d57405a372212e95ef871