{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2401274.zip::R2-2401274 Introduction of MAC CE based PL-RS update for Type1 CG PUSCH.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"B","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-18","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In Rel-16, MAC CE based pathloss RS updates for PUSCH/SRS is supported for PUSCH scheduled by DCI. Based on the RAN1 Rel-18 TEI agreement below, MAC CE based pathloss RS updates for Type 1 CG PUSCH is also supported. ","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RAN1 Agreement","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-18 TEI proposal on pathloss RS for Type 1 CG-PUSCH is agreed. Relevant TP for clause 7.1.1 in TS 38.213 is endorsed in principle.","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"•Note: Corresponding UE capability and RRC configuration will be introduced and discussed in future meetings.","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7.1.1 UE behaviour","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"According to RAN1’s Rel-18 higher layers parameter list (R1-2312708), the higher layer parameter enablePL-RS-UpdateForType1CG-PUSCH to enable MAC CE based pathloss RS update for Type 1 CG PUSCH should be introduced in RRC by RAN2. When this parameter is present, the Rel-18 feature of MAC CE based pathloss RS updates for Type 1 CG-PUSCH is enabled.","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"It is also noted that this parameter can only be configured when the UE is configured with enablePL-RS-UpdateForPUSCH-SRS since a mapping between sri-PUSCH-PowerControlId and PUSCH-PathlossReferenceRS-Id values can be updated by a MAC CE if the UE is provided enablePL-RS-UpdateForPUSCH-SRS.","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"50a2095effc85e514ac663582703f19bf6444f9ef77a91fd6ee3c360eef6c5bc","original_member_sha256":"71155dffe6c62c6d21bde43469a3470586b534266998f5593f9b07930513ab47","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a7b8faeb97c2e7bce821fcc5af64b68bb5d8224285b7bda61396971afe2db15a","8e0dc0cfc542d1e683d25af6083c6b5739bab7518cb48efeaab2ab277a8fb23a","6ba142295ff835955524f160ab38b863cea762029933cea534b00c8930bacc9e","d32c72c4c1cf0fdd7cf0013dc94f977b279a36604ce35c79a9a9af143a9464c3","5ecf8037d37e3ae3407d702f915bebc9476042