{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2401274.zip::R2-2401274 Introduction of MAC CE based PL-RS update for Type1 CG PUSCH.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    srs-PosTx-Hopping-r18               SetupRelease { SRS-PosTx-Hopping-r18 }                                  OPTIONAL    -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]],","paragraph_zero_based":241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    enablePL-RS-UpdateForType1CG-PUSCH-r18 ENUMERATED {enabled}                                                 OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]] ","paragraph_zero_based":244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DummyJ ::=                          SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":247},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    maxEnergyDetectionThreshold-r16         INTEGER(-85..-52),","paragraph_zero_based":248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    energyDetectionThresholdOffset-r16      INTEGER (-20..-13),","paragraph_zero_based":249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ul-toDL-COT-SharingED-Threshold-r16     INTEGER (-85..-52)                                                  OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    absenceOfAnyOtherTechnology-r16         ENUMERATED {true}                                                   OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":252},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":253},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":254},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":255},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"<<<<Start of the 2nd Change>>>>","paragraph_zero_based":256},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UplinkConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":257},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"carrierSwitching","paragraph_zero_based":258},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Includes parameters for configuration of carrier based SRS switching (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 6.2.1.3.","paragraph_zero_based":259},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"enableDefaultBeamPL-ForPUSCH0-0, enableDefaultBeamPL-ForPUCCH, enableDefaultBeamPL-ForSRS","paragraph_zero_based":260},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When the parameter is present, UE derives the spatial relation and the corresponding pathloss reference Rs as specified in 38.213, clauses 7.1.1, 7.2.1, 7.3.1 and 9.2.2. The network only configures these parameters for FR2.","paragraph_zero_based":261},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"enablePL-RS-UpdateForPUSCH-SRS","paragraph_zero_based":262},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When this parameter is present, the Rel-16 feature of MAC CE based pathloss RS updates for PUSCH/SRS is enabled. Network only configures this parameter when the UE is configured with sri-PUSCH-PowerControl. If this field is not configured, network configures at most 4 pathloss RS resources for PUSCH/PUCCH/SRS transmissions per BWP, not including pathloss RS resources for SRS transmissions for positioning. (See TS 38.213 [13], clause 7).","paragraph_zero_based":263}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"50a2095effc85e514ac663582703f19bf6444f9ef77a91fd6ee3c360eef6c5bc","original_member_sha256":"71155dffe6c62c6d21bde43469a3470586b534266998f5593f9b07930513ab47","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f22d99e5045a6c3031bfe248019598d8d4389dd0d40797804127e268bf9ba1a2","130bdd070c0ac3c2b5d3d1f0e964e3a9b41c8b247f0895e885a9642fb97b0330","d97ee0d009f7b5380dd77ff7f8301ec649a16aaece144f5152f79af0ab226382","0f66b228eafe377948ab9a76b409bfe84db446a1165fbf606e1376292ecc697e","e3d1256c976651dc89a83b870c14f119110a2e4d6d0c98f53b4112b9e5c8cc88","4723e7ecd7ab786ff66f519bbf4f550463b95f297a806d34cc6e7e11754ba0cc","4d2ef5d28cacf6f3f264ea56eb49b13c7a0d471b7033b7816d2cd3e5896ad96b","c0da166249ef11113e6ca2bd3b75ac6aee56f25d25dc8790f1e6828c77e586bc","19aea82a1551ab80e5735fe3b692c929c16c6782fb41b6751ac25da8ac74699a","54e8735bde378099d5e7947377a6cdad0db38d26cf5f143ecdfaf2801e9b2733","f9a00a6d71b7896b9c27b460aca03bc2bfb043402b8a10304d9700ac872c1e9e","d545863f814032fa06b9b76f2f038ff738c1912fb1d2c30a5d702e764bd0db7e","b46fb5847274aab5324b6d9808c1884a0b771d703dbcac759dc5d075bb240eb7","3c394a25c610386fbf6034e1cc5d0a9409a95a4e658a4ecd445982666ab04cbe","f445b598b80979903a8143e0c20c73d3bcfcdbf3198c2452617ae72365d9734c","63466f08e7d65364ee180c05330a7b939d71eeab597c4f92d0886b0214856bd5","eb11203bced6dedf89aae98a218a303e8bdda8f22ad35e8288c0087ada8d9188","77a4bba8cea4e2b867ace8cd7f4dcc04d8164ff0612d1f74ecb19d0ded8eceff","e75da722cd679d059ae2df898ae44f8c05cfe056336e5edea8109aa865c8bc73","b20ba7c5970d34ddba475812eb6782a345436222a1fd756c2b2ed8c6347d3532","6f9209244c0efae527a9df64e1f4bd2a7a0a450d0b74e79c688010df9bdabb57","76c1b63faa20f8dafccf02f991bcfbfb9bbe7b3479bf51f832d5678ca9923353","5ded1123cfee80945eccca3fbd7e9e2acd8d3e223d2881dddbdd1ba8647054d9","bbaffdcbf91197a5d217cc7f701b4dce8f82553b5ec4dc5bd17a99556b9c6b5d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[240,263],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2401274.zip::R2-2401274 Introduction of MAC CE based PL-RS update for Type1 CG PUSCH.docx:p240"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2401274.zip::R2-2401274 Introduction of MAC CE based PL-RS update for Type1 CG PUSCH.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"enablePL-RS-UpdateForType1CG-PUSCH","paragraph_zero_based":264},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When this parameter is present, the Rel-18 feature of MAC CE based pathloss RS updates for Type 1 CG-PUSCH is enabled. Network only configures this parameter when the UE is configured with enablePL-RS-UpdateForPUSCH-SRS.","paragraph_zero_based":265},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"firstActiveUplinkBWP-Id","paragraph_zero_based":266},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If configured for an SpCell, this field contains the ID of the UL BWP to be activated upon performing the RRC (re-)configuration. If the field is absent, the RRC (re-)configuration does not impose a BWP switch.","paragraph_zero_based":267},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If configured for an SCell, this field contains the ID of the uplink bandwidth part to be used upon activation of an SCell. The initial bandwidth part is referred to by BandiwdthPartId = 0.","paragraph_zero_based":268},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"initialUplinkBWP","paragraph_zero_based":269},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The dedicated (UE-specific) configuration for the initial uplink bandwidth-part (i.e. UL BWP#0). If any of the optional IEs are configured within this IE as part of the IE uplinkConfig, the UE considers the BWP#0 to be an RRC configured BWP (from UE capability viewpoint). Otherwise, the UE does not consider the BWP#0 as an RRC configured BWP (from UE capability viewpoint). Network always configures the UE with a value for this field if no other BWPs are configured. NOTE1","paragraph_zero_based":270},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"moreThanOneNackOnlyMode","paragraph_zero_based":271},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the mode of NACK-only feedback in the PUCCH transmission, as specified in TS 38.213 [13], clause 18. If multicast CFR is not configured, this field is not included. Otherwise, if the field is absent, UE uses mode 1 for multicast CFR.","paragraph_zero_based":272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mpr-PowerBoost-FR2","paragraph_zero_based":273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether UE is allowed to boost uplink transmission power by suspending in-band emission (IBE) requirements as specified in TS 38.101-2 [39]. Network only configures this field for FR2 serving cells.","paragraph_zero_based":274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"powerBoostPi2BPSK","paragraph_zero_based":275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If this field is set to true, the UE determines the maximum output power for PUCCH/PUSCH transmissions that use pi/2 BPSK modulation according to TS 38.101-1 [15], clause 6.2.4.","paragraph_zero_based":276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pusch-ServingCellConfig","paragraph_zero_based":277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUSCH related parameters that are not BWP-specific.","paragraph_zero_based":278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosTx-Hopping","paragraph_zero_based":279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Contains configuration related to the SRS for Positioning hopping outside the active BWP of the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uplinkBWP-ToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The additional bandwidth parts for uplink to be added or modified. In case of TDD uplink- and downlink BWP with the same bandwidthPartId are considered as a BWP pair and must have the same center frequency.","paragraph_zero_based":282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uplinkBWP-ToReleaseList","paragraph_zero_based":283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The additional bandwidth parts for uplink to be released.","paragraph_zero_based":284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uplinkChannelBW-PerSCS-List","paragraph_zero_based":285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A set of UE specific channel bandwidth and location configurations for different subcarrier spacings (numerologies). Defined in relation to Point A. The UE uses the configuration provided in this field only for the purpose of channel bandwidth and location determination. If absent, UE uses the configuration indicated in scs-SpecificCarrierList in UplinkConfigCommon / UplinkConfigCommonSIB. Network only configures channel bandwidth that corresponds to the channel bandwidth values defined in TS 38.101-1 [15], TS 38.101-2 [39], and TS 38.101-5 [75]. If the UE is a RedCap UE and needs to autonomously switch to its initial uplink bandwidth part to perform a random access procedure but its current UE specific channel bandwidth does not cover the initial uplink bandwidth part, the UE autonomously changes its UE specific channel bandwidth to cover the initial uplink bandwidth part. In that case, after completion of the random access procedure, the network ensures that the UE specific channel bandwidth fully covers the UE's active uplink bandwidth part in subsequent bandwidth part switch operations.","paragraph_zero_based":286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uplinkTxSwitchingPeriodLocation","paragraph_zero_based":287}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"50a2095effc85e514ac663582703f19bf6444f9ef77a91fd6ee3c360eef6c5bc","original_member_sha256":"71155dffe6c62c6d21bde43469a3470586b534266998f5593f9b07930513ab47","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["76225292a34ec75549c2683c3dbc832ce7ce5bedc4088a62ab85816e7c5672f1","6f7f5d8d32c37e492df61e743c7ebff32c72c8f256320d2efdcdee7c65cdfb37","37041b15882c0eb798dc8cc208f6353853995402d554e16c5f7ddd74d36dfefc","b52148bf92ff712831004e6c07c61ad52d91e819886e004d34c69469675e991e","50ef5777083d265026cbcef0c314587b7eb8ac049e8d41755994ea3115ea38b2","3eab152f335d478dce8714bfd80983d62138e7d21273a29ec56c5f9f02dde7dd","897b8130f9b25ad73d78ceb116901eb1a7ca5ea93570b8947ec9340661825c31","0a8af2c4933ddc46db382ad2360986d196105dc0ff0d1b4b1c1a2e2316f4a582","d1ad93481bc11142abef30915e3e6b9ba356a790d219f642568101f9e5d1d64d","d8ae9f98359d2388f1fa8b2c460974457689431a30f4f852737be0b21c2a5477","7b8265f58a781370c35449ab310bf37d6b6467e061b6707437ce87c10889f928","227bc7ced44a02db505013ee873ef434a464cf7769168397d4f868a6cc90789a","e6cf32df5211bdcb08c87b2b6c487af300c38c74319375c6b039b65363b90cf8","9683a33cc4b870ab8bdde4761962ea33b38362b1b28a845e2977abbcb875a4d3","415276ce9b0a4a19947aa44962961002696108cdd88350c5a209238dc25f2e3e","2bc9d6544602bdf73f5e11ef281b603b74f69914bc0a01cae5ea13643be3dddf","d497b1f8363e08f4f64d41a6064459de9e5e55fdd8cb871a6b713c590c89085e","b38a35ea8dd2c421df3654cb9d221ed1f4bba1234ad014750f444fe28c9f14e7","69273be562a32f1a5ea2b3c380d205863d74ee2900cc096928bd33c392633275","eef620e43414e4117dc95f62af36f7a6ed9227f0feb5d4cf0f4281ff15c52d79","29b950a9f46f5b0a81740945f6870a3a3868e6daf47bb90a13dc2f8193d53096","bcb3f092a9740c72831b224b926afff2bdc6ab64c052f87907ce2f2c4e7381fa","26e11d0fb6504ad5e8893c9d4cd1eb5c3ad83ee729e2ca74afec66a18bca3688","4589a32222c168f86b45923956b57ec1ed3daf097c8eb2259d2e5397cd26e030"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[264,287],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2401274.zip::R2-2401274 Introduction of MAC CE based PL-RS update for Type1 CG PUSCH.docx:p264"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2401274.zip::R2-2401274 Introduction of MAC CE based PL-RS update for Type1 CG PUSCH.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the location of UL Tx switching period is configured in this uplink carrier in case of inter-band UL CA, SUL, or (NG)EN-DC, as specified in TS 38.101-1 [15] and TS 38.101-3 [34].","paragraph_zero_based":288},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In case of (NG)EN-DC, network always configures this field to TRUE for NR carrier (i.e. with (NG)EN-DC, the UL switching period always occurs on the NR carrier).","paragraph_zero_based":289},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In case of inter-band UL CA or SUL, for dynamic uplink Tx switching between 2 bands with 2 uplink carriers or 3 uplink carriers as defined in TS 38.101-1 [15], network configures this field to TRUE for the uplink carrier(s) on one band and configures this field to FALSE for the uplink carrier(s) on the other band. This field is set to the same value for the carriers on the same band.","paragraph_zero_based":290},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uplinkTxSwitchingCarrier","paragraph_zero_based":291},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates that the configured carrier is carrier1 or carrier2 for dynamic uplink Tx switching, as defined in TS 38.101-1 [15] and TS 38.101-3 [34]. In case of (NG)EN-DC, network always configures the NR carrier as carrier 2.","paragraph_zero_based":292},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In case of inter-band UL CA or SUL, for dynamic uplink Tx switching between 2 bands with 2 uplink carriers or 3 uplink carriers as defined in TS 38.101-1 [15], network configures the uplink carrier(s) on one band as carrier1 and the uplink carrier(s) on the other band as carrier2. This field is set to the same value for the carriers on the same band.","paragraph_zero_based":293},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":294},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"<<<<End of the Change>>>>","paragraph_zero_based":295}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"50a2095effc85e514ac663582703f19bf6444f9ef77a91fd6ee3c360eef6c5bc","original_member_sha256":"71155dffe6c62c6d21bde43469a3470586b534266998f5593f9b07930513ab47","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f9f0eb04833fd5ac85af340b6be5b3768f9e8b6f7abcc458db7b9539aa876ae9","f7587e45d4bdc4d7a33446e1c3b779bcdf67040d98694ac311e89204d6fbf5ca","8dcde151b6357a960d234caaefe26cea9759cbbf222ae293dce520f2108927e2","9c65c5fa18faaa5ea6769d6955298122f5ceb93c6bc619de172207a67b7737d9","9429d445e7097e41f1f2612dbb5b040f8527397e2a209f29c579ce8fe46606b0","98b1ee0d46f8fdd99a654a60b2ede0d5847a6cba58cb6cd03c8b15ba5f0a039b","08e270d4f3f3844939c3cfcb562515a1213348690d17e0c8ae91cd5a2ecb3db0","2f4fed1262f9b47c05722c669f50624888ebbd87d268887ad4774ce88d48a630"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[288,295],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2401274.zip::R2-2401274 Introduction of MAC CE based PL-RS update for Type1 CG PUSCH.docx:p288"}
