{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2401316.zip::R2-2401316 BLE.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bt-NoElements-r18INTEGER (2..maxBT-BeaconAntElt-r18),","paragraph_zero_based":720},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bt-InterElementDist-r18INTEGER (30..130)","paragraph_zero_based":721},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":722},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":723},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":724},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":725},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BT-UniformCircularArray field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":726},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bt-NoElements","paragraph_zero_based":727},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the number of antenna elements in the circular antenna array. It is the same as the number of antenna elements in the bt-antElementList-r18 of the IE BT-BeaconInfoElement-r18","paragraph_zero_based":728},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bt-InterElementDist","paragraph_zero_based":729},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the distance between to adjacent elements in the uniform circular antenna array between ¼ and just above 1 wavelengths. Scale factor 1mm.","paragraph_zero_based":730},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":731},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The antenna element locations of the antenna array are defined along a circle with the reference point as center. The coordinates of the elements are:","paragraph_zero_based":732},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-x=0","paragraph_zero_based":733},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-y = bt-Radius* cos(2*p*(index-1)/ bt-NoElements-r18)","paragraph_zero_based":734},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-z = bt-Radius* sin(2*p*(index-1)/ bt-NoElements-r18)","paragraph_zero_based":735},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"where index is the order value of a specific antenna element in the bt-antElementList-r18 attribute of the IE BT-BeaconInfoElement-r18 – first element in the list corresponds to index 1 and so on, and","paragraph_zero_based":736},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":737},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bt-Radius = bt-InterElementDist-r18/(2*sin(p / bt-NoElements-r18))","paragraph_zero_based":738},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":739},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–BT-GenericArray","paragraph_zero_based":740},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE BT-GenericArray is used by the location server to define a generic antenna array as a list of offset locations for each antenna element, where each ordered entry in BT-GenericArray-r18 is associated to the same ordered entry in the bt-antElementList-r18 attribute of the IE BT-BeaconInfoElement-r18.","paragraph_zero_based":741},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":742},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":743}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"038bee5e08277a518e210695a9ad796eb7669167fb359201516fcfc3784430d8","original_member_sha256":"e32d7846969fb9d73f3e6db306c1eaae26983884f0f33261ecdad12458f09ea1","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ff17443415b2d2350675aba21654c8d7e1f5ec99f34f1df99a7b0e89e2461473","8a59a1e6441e455f6e8e514de7779d85dd779896dec23f0f5061aa17aa26cee9","dc5b5eefc32ad923db1b8f9baaefbc8b3049dc41346d6e20e4d206f635388e33","3c31b42d907d484166542f4a5ef81cbc691b278fa21664d2685049f37ebac270","07d008e537444105d5fabfb81cb4c49415261f2c26a6849e0d81f85eabcfdbd6","656e77a9503cbccd1a0a34b6673662f60ea9dec7841741318ca5fd049228c621","cda3797e61d91bd59c5e296fa40211ec8e22f3d601324fc2f27e2a35a1a1bba1","314f3ff51c0262e00a4a7bd799c1e76de8deb5e51c771757ab22b92f771d7d4f","4791c3b6c76ffdcf4cf67a6145ef3c3300d83187839a79c627d3b09